1
00:00:00,302 --> 00:00:02,737
♪ IN THE NOT-TOO-DISTANT
FUTURE ♪

2
00:00:02,803 --> 00:00:05,973
♪ NEXT SUNDAY, A.D. ♪

3
00:00:06,040 --> 00:00:09,010
♪ THERE WAS A GUY
NAMED JOEL ♪

4
00:00:09,077 --> 00:00:11,780
♪ NOT TOO DIFFERENT
FROM YOU OR ME ♪

5
00:00:11,847 --> 00:00:15,283
♪ HE WORKED
AT GIZMONIC INSTITUTE ♪

6
00:00:15,350 --> 00:00:18,387
♪ JUST ANOTHER FACE
IN A RED JUMPSUIT ♪

7
00:00:18,453 --> 00:00:21,388
♪ HE DID A GOOD JOB
CLEANING UP THE PLACE ♪

8
00:00:21,422 --> 00:00:23,057
♪ BUT HIS BOSSES
DIDN'T LIKE HIM ♪

9
00:00:23,123 --> 00:00:24,792
♪ SO THEY SHOT HIM
INTO SPACE ♪

10
00:00:24,858 --> 00:00:27,328
♪♪

11
00:00:27,395 --> 00:00:30,532
♪ WE'LL SEND HIM
CHEESY MOVIES ♪

12
00:00:30,598 --> 00:00:33,868
♪ THE WORST WE CAN FIND
LA LA LA ♪

13
00:00:33,935 --> 00:00:36,772
♪ HE'LL HAVE TO SIT
AND WATCH THEM ALL ♪

14
00:00:36,838 --> 00:00:39,940
♪ AND THE MONITOR IS MINE
LA LA LA ♪

15
00:00:40,007 --> 00:00:42,743
♪ NOW KEEP IN MIND
JOEL CAN'T CONTROL ♪

16
00:00:42,810 --> 00:00:46,180
♪ WHERE THE MOVIES BEGIN OR END
LA LA LA ♪

17
00:00:46,247 --> 00:00:49,217
♪ BECAUSE HE USED
THOSE SPECIAL PARTS ♪

18
00:00:49,283 --> 00:00:53,888
♪ TO MAKE HIS ROBOT FRIENDS ♪

19
00:00:53,955 --> 00:00:57,025
ROBOT ROLL CALL:
CAMBOT,

20
00:00:57,092 --> 00:00:58,192
- GYPSY...
- HI, GIRLS.

21
00:00:58,258 --> 00:01:00,060
- ... TOM SERVO...
- WHAT A COOL GUY.

22
00:01:00,128 --> 00:01:01,528
- ... CROW!
- WHAT A WISECRACKER.

23
00:01:01,595 --> 00:01:04,598
♪ IF YOU'RE WONDERING HOW
HE EATS AND BREATHES ♪

24
00:01:04,665 --> 00:01:07,735
♪ AND OTHER SCIENCE FACTS
LA LA LA ♪

25
00:01:07,802 --> 00:01:10,405
♪ THEN REPEAT TO YOURSELF
IT'S JUST A SHOW ♪

26
00:01:10,472 --> 00:01:13,442
♪ I SHOULD REALLY
JUST RELAX ♪

27
00:01:13,508 --> 00:01:16,610
♪ FOR MYSTERY SCIENCE THEATER ♪

28
00:01:16,677 --> 00:01:19,280
♪ 3000 ♪♪

29
00:01:22,617 --> 00:01:24,585
I REALLY THINK
THIS IS GOING TO BE IT.

30
00:01:24,685 --> 00:01:27,055
THIS IS MY YEAR.

31
00:01:27,122 --> 00:01:28,388
YOU SAY THAT EVERY YEAR
WE GO

32
00:01:28,457 --> 00:01:29,957
TO THE MAD SCIENTISTS
CONVENTION.

33
00:01:30,023 --> 00:01:31,793
AH, BUT THIS YEAR
IS DIFFERENT.

34
00:01:31,860 --> 00:01:34,495
THEY LAUGHED WHEN I MADE
THE MORE-PAINFUL MOUSETRAP,

35
00:01:34,562 --> 00:01:37,532
BUT MY ENTRANCE INTO
THE MAD SCIENTIST COMPETITION

36
00:01:37,598 --> 00:01:39,333
IS GOING TO MAKE ME FAMOUS.

37
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:41,468
- INFAMOUS.
- AH, THAT TOO, THAT TOO.

38
00:01:41,535 --> 00:01:43,805
OKAY, PROMISE ME, IF YOU LOSE
THE CONTEST THIS YEAR,

39
00:01:43,872 --> 00:01:46,473
YOU'RE NOT GONNA BLOW UP THE
WHOLE CONVENTION CENTER AGAIN.

40
00:01:46,540 --> 00:01:48,442
I ONLY DID THAT ONCE.

41
00:01:48,510 --> 00:01:49,810
OH, UH...UH...

42
00:01:49,877 --> 00:01:51,412
OKAY, TWICE, TWICE.
IT WAS TWICE.

43
00:01:51,478 --> 00:01:52,580
IT WAS THREE TIMES!

44
00:01:52,647 --> 00:01:55,150
THE THIRD TIME I USED
THE INCENDIARIES,

45
00:01:55,217 --> 00:01:57,085
AND IT DIDN'T ACTUALLY
MAKE THE BUILDING BLOW UP,

46
00:01:57,152 --> 00:02:00,388
IT JUST MADE IT BURN
REALLY QUICKLY.

47
00:02:00,455 --> 00:02:02,257
GOD, THAT WAS BEAUTIFUL,
WASN'T IT?

48
00:02:02,323 --> 00:02:03,725
OKAY, I'll GIVE YOU THAT.

49
00:02:03,792 --> 00:02:05,827
OH, IT'S TIME
TO CALL JOEL NOW.

50
00:02:05,893 --> 00:02:07,062
THE EXPERIMENT HAS TO START.

51
00:02:07,128 --> 00:02:08,663
RIGHT, RIGHT,
I KNOW THAT.

52
00:02:08,730 --> 00:02:11,833
COME IN, JOELENE, YOU
FREE-FLOATING SPACE FERRET.

53
00:02:11,900 --> 00:02:14,368
WELL, SIRS, I'M READY

54
00:02:14,435 --> 00:02:16,737
FOR THIS WEEK'S
INVENTION EXCHANGE.

55
00:02:16,803 --> 00:02:19,307
YOU KNOW HOW THEY HAVE
AIRBAGS FOR CARS?

56
00:02:19,373 --> 00:02:21,008
BUT THEY HAVEN'T INVENTED
ANYTHING YET

57
00:02:21,075 --> 00:02:22,910
FOR US MOTORCYCLISTS,

58
00:02:22,977 --> 00:02:26,647
SO I CAME UP WITH THIS--
THE AIRBAG HELMET.

59
00:02:26,713 --> 00:02:27,948
WHAT DO YOU THINK?

60
00:02:28,015 --> 00:02:30,785
OH, GREAT, GET RALPH NADER
ON THE PHONE.

61
00:02:30,852 --> 00:02:32,820
AND THEN CALL
GARY BUSEY.

62
00:02:32,887 --> 00:02:34,655
- IS IT OUR TURN NOW?
- YES.

63
00:02:34,722 --> 00:02:37,025
OKAY, THIS IS OUR INVENTION
FOR THIS WEEK.

64
00:02:37,092 --> 00:02:38,827
IT'S CALLED THE CHALKMAN.

65
00:02:38,893 --> 00:02:40,362
YES, WE'RE ENTERING THIS
IN THE MAD SCIENTIST COMPETITION

66
00:02:40,428 --> 00:02:41,462
THIS YEAR.

67
00:02:41,528 --> 00:02:42,597
OH, WE HAVE OTHER CHOICES,

68
00:02:42,663 --> 00:02:43,665
BUT THIS IS THE ONE
WE'RE GOING WITH.

69
00:02:43,698 --> 00:02:45,065
THIS IS VERY STRONG.

70
00:02:45,132 --> 00:02:47,702
ALL RIGHT, OKAY,
YOU'RE THROWING A PARTY,

71
00:02:47,768 --> 00:02:50,103
IT'S 3:00 A.M., AND NONE
OF THE GUESTS ARE LEAVING.

72
00:02:50,170 --> 00:02:51,940
THAT'S WHEN YOU BRING OUT
THE CHALKMAN.

73
00:02:52,007 --> 00:02:54,742
YES, AS EVERY SELF-RESPECTING
SCIENTIST KNOWS,

74
00:02:54,808 --> 00:02:57,178
THE SOUND OF HUMAN FINGERNAILS
ON A CHALKBOARD

75
00:02:57,245 --> 00:02:58,680
IS MOST ANNOYING.

76
00:02:58,747 --> 00:03:02,383
IT INITIATES THE PRIMAL FEAR
RESPONSE IN ALL MAMMALS.

77
00:03:02,450 --> 00:03:05,453
MUCH LIKE A CHIMPANZEE
SCURRYING ACROSS THE PLAINS

78
00:03:05,520 --> 00:03:07,122
OF THE SERENGETI IN FEAR.

79
00:03:07,188 --> 00:03:09,657
SIMPLY PUT YOUR CHALKMAN
ON THE PLATEN.

80
00:03:09,723 --> 00:03:11,927
- THIS IS A REAL CHALKBOARD
- PUT ON SIDE "B".

81
00:03:11,993 --> 00:03:13,828
SIDE "B".
EXCELLENT.

82
00:03:13,895 --> 00:03:17,332
AND JUST, YOU'LL NOTICE,
THE TONEARM HAS

83
00:03:17,398 --> 00:03:20,268
REAL HUMAN FINGERNAILS
EMBEDDED IN THE HAND.

84
00:03:20,335 --> 00:03:22,203
NOW PLACE IT ON THE PLATEN...

85
00:03:22,270 --> 00:03:25,005
[HORRIBLE FINGERNAIL
SCREECHING]

86
00:03:25,072 --> 00:03:26,975
... OH...
OPEN IT.

87
00:03:27,042 --> 00:03:29,543
- THEY'LL STAY.
- CLOSE IT.

88
00:03:29,610 --> 00:03:31,980
[SCREECHING]
THEY LEAVE.

89
00:03:32,047 --> 00:03:34,315
- OPEN IT.
- THEY'LL STAY.

90
00:03:34,382 --> 00:03:36,450
- CLOSE IT.
- THEY'LL LEAVE.

91
00:03:36,517 --> 00:03:38,385
- OPEN IT.
- STAY.

92
00:03:38,418 --> 00:03:41,188
AND SO ON AND SO ON
AND SO ON.

93
00:03:41,255 --> 00:03:43,223
WELL, WHAT DO YOU THINK
OF THAT, JOEL-MEISTER?

94
00:03:43,290 --> 00:03:45,125
- WOW, IT'S REALLY ANNOYING.

95
00:03:45,192 --> 00:03:46,760
- [BOTH]
THANK YOU.

96
00:03:46,827 --> 00:03:49,130
ALL RIGHT, SO WHAT'S
THIS WEEK'S EXPERIMENT?

97
00:03:49,197 --> 00:03:51,465
IT'S CALLED "THE ROBOT VS.
THE AZTEC MUMMY,"

98
00:03:51,532 --> 00:03:54,068
AND IT'S ALMOST AS ANNOYING
AS THIS CHALKMAN HERE.

99
00:03:54,135 --> 00:03:56,503
YES, BUT FIRST WE'RE GOING
TO SCOUR YOUR PALATE

100
00:03:56,570 --> 00:03:59,140
WITH A LITTLE CINEMATIC
SCIENCE FICTION SORBET.

101
00:03:59,207 --> 00:04:01,742
IT'S AN OLD SERIAL CALLED
"COMMANDO CODY

102
00:04:01,808 --> 00:04:03,612
AND THE ROCKET MEN
FROM THE MOON."

103
00:04:03,678 --> 00:04:06,147
UH, BE CAREFUL, LARRY,
I'VE INSTALLED

104
00:04:06,213 --> 00:04:08,482
A NEW SECURITY SYSTEM HERE
IN DEEP 13,

105
00:04:08,548 --> 00:04:10,117
SO BE CAREFUL
WHICH BUTTONS YOU PUSH

106
00:04:10,183 --> 00:04:11,118
ON THE PANEL, ALL RIGHT?

107
00:04:11,185 --> 00:04:12,520
NEAT-O, OKAY,
HOW DOES IT WORK?

108
00:04:12,587 --> 00:04:15,290
OH, WELL, STAND OVER THERE
ON THAT MARK

109
00:04:15,357 --> 00:04:17,292
AND PRETEND
YOU'RE FROM ACCOUNTING.

110
00:04:17,358 --> 00:04:20,795
OKAY.
YOU MEAN THIS MARK HERE?

111
00:04:20,862 --> 00:04:24,032
- YES.
- OH---

112
00:04:24,098 --> 00:04:29,403
HMM, INTERESTING.

113
00:04:29,470 --> 00:04:33,107
HERE--
HERE'S YOUR MOVIE, JOEL.

114
00:04:33,173 --> 00:04:36,877
[ALARM BUZZING]
MOVIE SIGN!

115
00:04:45,185 --> 00:04:49,690
♪♪

116
00:04:49,757 --> 00:04:51,325
AW, YOU'RE GETTING TO HEAVY.

117
00:04:51,392 --> 00:04:54,495
- A REPUBLIC SERIAL.
- YEAH.

118
00:04:54,562 --> 00:04:55,997
YOU EVER HEARD
OF SERIALS BEFORE?

119
00:04:56,063 --> 00:04:58,833
YEAH, LIGHT OAT.
OH, LOOK, IT'S PUMPKIN BOY.

120
00:04:58,900 --> 00:05:01,102
NO, IT'S NOT THAT KIND
OF SERIAL.

121
00:05:01,168 --> 00:05:04,038
- SO IT MEANS, A, UH--
- OH, SO IT'S A WHEAT THING?

122
00:05:04,105 --> 00:05:07,275
NO, A MOVIE THAT'S
IN SERIES.

123
00:05:07,342 --> 00:05:09,710
- WHAT?
- OH, YOU'LL CATCH ON.

124
00:05:09,777 --> 00:05:11,212
IT'S NOT A WHOLE MOVIE.

125
00:05:11,278 --> 00:05:15,115
WHY WOULD SOMEONE GO AND SEE
PART OF A MOVIE?

126
00:05:15,182 --> 00:05:17,452
UH... I DON'T KNOW.

127
00:05:17,518 --> 00:05:19,387
THERE'S ALWAYS A BORING SHORT.

128
00:05:19,453 --> 00:05:22,890
- YEAH.
- MY SHORTS ARE NEVER BORING.

129
00:05:22,957 --> 00:05:25,192
THANK YOU, TOM.

130
00:05:25,258 --> 00:05:29,397
♪♪

131
00:05:29,463 --> 00:05:31,765
IS THE MUSIC ALWAYS
THIS POOR IN SERIALS?

132
00:05:31,832 --> 00:05:36,403
[JOEL LAUGHS]
YES.

133
00:05:36,470 --> 00:05:40,442
I'M THINKING I MIGHT
GET IT THEN.

134
00:05:40,508 --> 00:05:43,177
HE'S THE HEAVY.

135
00:05:43,243 --> 00:05:46,113
YOU CAN TELL WHEN
THE MUSIC SWELLS UP.

136
00:05:46,180 --> 00:05:47,748
ALL RIGHT.

137
00:05:47,815 --> 00:05:53,520
♪♪

138
00:05:53,587 --> 00:05:56,590
[EXPLOSION]

139
00:05:56,657 --> 00:05:58,492
I GUESS THAT'S THE END
OF CHAPTER ONE.

140
00:05:58,558 --> 00:06:01,695
[TOM, IMITATING NARRATOR]
OKLAHOMA, 1934.

141
00:06:01,762 --> 00:06:03,898
THE OIL FIELDS ARE ABLAZE.

142
00:06:03,965 --> 00:06:09,903
♪♪

143
00:06:11,038 --> 00:06:12,640
[EXPLOSION]

144
00:06:14,142 --> 00:06:17,043
HOLY...

145
00:06:17,112 --> 00:06:18,947
HEY, LOOK, THERE'S A SALE
AT PENNY'S.

146
00:06:19,013 --> 00:06:21,048
"BIG STUFF BLOWING UP
EVERYWHERE."

147
00:06:21,115 --> 00:06:22,750
MAYBE IT'S A FIRE SALE.

148
00:06:22,817 --> 00:06:25,152
[TOM CHUCKLES]

149
00:06:25,218 --> 00:06:30,323
♪♪

150
00:06:30,390 --> 00:06:34,228
"NEW PETITION
AGAINST TAX LAW."

151
00:06:34,295 --> 00:06:36,463
"THE CONTINUED WAVE
OF DEATH-DEALING EXPLOSIONS

152
00:06:36,530 --> 00:06:38,967
"STRUCK YESTERDAY
AT AREA DEFENSE HEADQUARTERS.

153
00:06:39,033 --> 00:06:41,202
"AS ON PREVIOUS OCCASIONS,
THE AUTHORITIES ARE UNABLE

154
00:06:41,268 --> 00:06:42,870
"TO DETECT THE CAUSE
OF THESE BLASTS,

155
00:06:42,937 --> 00:06:43,905
WHICH HAVE DONE UNTOLD DAMAGE."

156
00:06:43,972 --> 00:06:44,938
WHO'S THAT GUY
MIXING DRINKS.

157
00:06:45,005 --> 00:06:46,673
UH, PROFESSOR TOM COLLINS.

158
00:06:46,740 --> 00:06:47,975
WELL, THERE ARE SEVERAL
THEORIES, JOAN,

159
00:06:48,042 --> 00:06:49,877
BUT SO FAR,
NO ONE IS EVEN SURE

160
00:06:49,943 --> 00:06:51,645
WHAT KIND OF EXPLOSIVES
ARE BEING USED

161
00:06:51,712 --> 00:06:52,947
OR HOW THEY'RE SET OFF.

162
00:06:53,013 --> 00:06:55,215
MAYBE MR. HENDERSON WILL HAVE
SOME INFORMATION FOR US

163
00:06:55,282 --> 00:06:56,583
WHEN HE GETS IN
FROM WASHINGTON.

164
00:06:56,650 --> 00:06:58,752
THAT GUY HENDERSON WOULDN'T
TELL YOU WHAT TIME IT IS.

165
00:06:58,820 --> 00:07:00,622
JUST WHAT IS HIS JOB,
ANYWAY?

166
00:07:00,688 --> 00:07:02,257
MAYBE HE DOESN'T HAVE A WATCH.

167
00:07:02,323 --> 00:07:05,425
HE ONLY ANSWERS TO A FEW PEOPLE
IN THIS COUNTRY OF OURS.

168
00:07:05,493 --> 00:07:07,462
I THINK THAT--
[KNOCK ON DOOR]

169
00:07:07,528 --> 00:07:09,997
AND THEY'RE ALL NAMED SUE.

170
00:07:10,063 --> 00:07:12,032
- HELLO, MR. HENDERSON.
- HELLO, COMMANDER CODY.

171
00:07:12,098 --> 00:07:14,035
- WHAT TIME IS IT?
- TED, MISS GILBERT.

172
00:07:14,102 --> 00:07:15,937
HOW ARE YOU GETTING ALONG
WITH THE ROCKET SHIP?

173
00:07:16,003 --> 00:07:17,538
AS WELL AS CAN BE
EXPECTED, SIR.

174
00:07:17,605 --> 00:07:19,773
OUR TESTS WITH THE MODEL
ARE SATISFACTORY.

175
00:07:19,840 --> 00:07:21,242
IF THE GOVERNMENT WOULD LET US
MAKE A FEW TEST FLIGHTS

176
00:07:21,308 --> 00:07:22,310
WITH THE ROCKET--

177
00:07:22,377 --> 00:07:23,677
IT'S OUT OF THE QUESTION.

178
00:07:23,743 --> 00:07:25,747
THIS WHOLE PROJECT'S
STRICTLY TOP SECRET.

179
00:07:25,813 --> 00:07:28,817
SINCE YOU PEOPLE DEVELOPED
THE ROCKET SHIP FOR US

180
00:07:28,883 --> 00:07:30,350
AND WE'LL BE THE ONES
OPERATING IT,

181
00:07:30,417 --> 00:07:32,953
IT HAS BEEN DECIDED THAT YOU
SHOULD KNOW MORE OF OUR PLANS.

182
00:07:33,020 --> 00:07:34,122
GEE, NICE HEAD.

183
00:07:34,188 --> 00:07:36,023
I'VE BEEN AUTHORIZED
TO TELL YOU THIS MUCH.

184
00:07:36,090 --> 00:07:38,625
ITS PRIMARY USE WILL BE
TO COMBAT THIS WAVE

185
00:07:38,692 --> 00:07:40,828
OF SABOTAGE AND DESTRUCTION
OF OUR DEFENSE SYSTEM.

186
00:07:40,895 --> 00:07:42,095
DUH...

187
00:07:42,163 --> 00:07:43,263
YOU MEAN THE GOVERNMENT KNOWS
WHAT'S CAUSING IT?

188
00:07:43,330 --> 00:07:44,565
YEAH, THEY READ
THE PAPERS TOO.

189
00:07:44,632 --> 00:07:46,600
TESTS OF THE WRECKAGE SHOW
THAT THE EXPLOSIONS

190
00:07:46,667 --> 00:07:47,968
ARE OF ATOMIC ORIGIN.

191
00:07:48,035 --> 00:07:50,403
YOU MEAN SOMEONE'S DROPPING
ATOMIC BOMBS ON US?

192
00:07:50,470 --> 00:07:52,240
NOT BOMBS.
NO PLANES HAVE BEEN OBSERVED,

193
00:07:52,307 --> 00:07:54,075
AND THE EXPLOSIONS AREN'T
SEVERE ENOUGH.

194
00:07:54,142 --> 00:07:56,177
NO, FROM WHAT I'VE LEARNED
OF THE NATURE OF THE BLASTS,

195
00:07:56,243 --> 00:07:58,212
THEY SEEM MORE LIKE
AN ATOMIC RAY OF SOME KIND.

196
00:07:58,278 --> 00:07:59,447
OF COURSE,
THAT'S JUST A GUESS.

197
00:07:59,513 --> 00:08:01,515
IT'S THE SAME GUESS
THAT WE'VE MADE

198
00:08:01,582 --> 00:08:03,717
BECAUSE IT'S THE ONLY
POSSIBLE ANSWER.

199
00:08:03,750 --> 00:08:05,385
BUT NO ONE HAVE EVER
BEEN ABLE TO MAKE

200
00:08:05,452 --> 00:08:06,620
AN ATOMIC RAY MACHINE.

201
00:08:06,687 --> 00:08:08,890
YOU MEAN NO ONE ON EARTH
EVER HAS.

202
00:08:08,957 --> 00:08:10,023
HUH?

203
00:08:10,057 --> 00:08:11,058
SAY, THIS ROCKET
WE'RE BUILDING WILL BE ABLE

204
00:08:11,092 --> 00:08:12,125
TO FLY TO THE MOON.

205
00:08:12,193 --> 00:08:13,160
MAYBE SOMEONE UP THERE
HAS BUILT ONE

206
00:08:13,227 --> 00:08:14,262
THAT COULD GET DOWN HERE.

207
00:08:14,328 --> 00:08:15,997
WE BELIEVE THAT POSSIBLE.

208
00:08:16,063 --> 00:08:18,098
AND FOR SOME TIME, OUR
ASTRONOMERS HAVE BEEN NOTICING

209
00:08:18,165 --> 00:08:20,735
AN UNUSUAL AMOUNT
OF ATOMIC ACTIVITY ON THE MOON.

210
00:08:20,802 --> 00:08:22,570
ISN'T ANY AMOUNT
OF ATOMIC ACTIVITY

211
00:08:22,637 --> 00:08:23,570
ON THE MOON UNUSUAL?

212
00:08:23,637 --> 00:08:26,040
ATOMIC BLASTS ON THE EARTH.

213
00:08:26,107 --> 00:08:27,942
THE TWO KNOWN FACTS
FIT TOGETHER.

214
00:08:28,008 --> 00:08:30,377
- YES, IT ADDS UP.
- LIKE A GROCERY BILL.

215
00:08:30,443 --> 00:08:32,747
SO THAT'S WHY YOU WANT US
TO FLY TO THE MOON.

216
00:08:32,813 --> 00:08:34,115
YES, AND WHEN YOU GET
TO THE MOON,

217
00:08:34,182 --> 00:08:36,317
FIND OUT IF THESE ATTACKS
ARE ACTUALLY COMING FROM THERE.

218
00:08:36,383 --> 00:08:37,518
AND BRING BACK SOME CHEESE.

219
00:08:37,585 --> 00:08:38,785
AND TRY TO DEVISE SOME PLAN
FOR STOPPING THEM.

220
00:08:38,852 --> 00:08:40,387
IN THE MEANTIME,
WE'LL DO WHAT WE CAN

221
00:08:40,453 --> 00:08:43,123
WITH THESE ATTACKS HERE.

222
00:08:43,190 --> 00:08:44,592
IS YOUR FLYING SUIT
STILL WORKING?

223
00:08:44,658 --> 00:08:46,127
- NO, IT NEEDS TO BE LET OUT.
- YES.

224
00:08:46,193 --> 00:08:47,562
WE MAY ASK YOU TO USE IT.

225
00:08:47,628 --> 00:08:51,232
IF A RAY GUN IS BEING USED
TO CAUSE THESE BLASTS,

226
00:08:51,298 --> 00:08:53,467
IT'S PROBABLY BEING OPERATED
FROM THE GROUND.

227
00:08:53,533 --> 00:08:55,402
AND IF YOU COULD GET
TO THE SCENE OF THE ATTACK

228
00:08:55,468 --> 00:08:57,372
SOON ENOUGH,
YOU MIGHT BE ABLE

229
00:08:57,438 --> 00:08:59,007
TO FIND SOME CLUE
TO THE ATTACKERS.

230
00:08:59,073 --> 00:09:00,975
- I'LL BE GLAD TO TRY.
- GOOD.

231
00:09:01,042 --> 00:09:02,443
OR IF WE FIND OUT
WHAT TIME IT IS.

232
00:09:02,510 --> 00:09:04,545
- ALL RIGHT, SIR.
- GOOD-BYE.

233
00:09:04,612 --> 00:09:06,580
- GOOD-BYE.

234
00:09:06,647 --> 00:09:10,483
♪♪

235
00:09:10,550 --> 00:09:13,487
[TRAIN WHISTLE BLOWING]

236
00:09:16,457 --> 00:09:19,627
THERE SHE IS,
RIGHT ON TIME.

237
00:09:19,693 --> 00:09:21,428
IT'S A TRAIN, ALL RIGHT.

238
00:09:23,063 --> 00:09:24,865
[EXPLOSION]
WHOA!

239
00:09:27,167 --> 00:09:29,837
- FEELS GOOD, DON'T IT?
- THAT DID IT.

240
00:09:29,903 --> 00:09:33,607
- NICE SHOOTING, LIONEL.
- THANKS, TYCO.

241
00:09:36,977 --> 00:09:38,912
ALL RIGHT, I'LL GET OUT THERE
RIGHT AWAY.

242
00:09:38,980 --> 00:09:41,282
SAY, GIVE ME A HAND
WITH THE FLYING SUIT, TED.

243
00:09:41,348 --> 00:09:42,950
YOU'RE GONNA WEAR THAT TIE
TO FLY IN?

244
00:09:43,017 --> 00:09:45,252
... WAS BLASTED OUT
IN THE WEST END OF THE VALLEY.

245
00:09:45,318 --> 00:09:47,187
A RANCHER REPORTED
HE SAW A TRUCK PARKED

246
00:09:47,253 --> 00:09:49,690
ON A HILL
OVERLOOKING THE TRACKS

247
00:09:49,757 --> 00:09:52,258
WITH TWO MEN IN IT
WORKING SOME KIND OF A GUN.

248
00:09:52,327 --> 00:09:53,627
THEY PULLED OUT
RIGHT AFTER THE WRECK

249
00:09:53,693 --> 00:09:55,462
AND HEADED TOWARD
KERN HILLS.

250
00:09:55,528 --> 00:09:57,332
HENDERSON'S OFFICE GAVE ME
A DESCRIPTION OF THE TRUCK,

251
00:09:57,398 --> 00:09:58,598
SO I'M GOING OUT
TO LOOK FOR IT.

252
00:09:58,665 --> 00:09:59,967
I SUPPOSE YOU'LL BE
WANTING THIS.

253
00:10:00,033 --> 00:10:01,468
YES, AND I'LL TAKE
THE GUN TOO.

254
00:10:01,535 --> 00:10:03,203
I MAY NEED IT.

255
00:10:03,270 --> 00:10:07,207
♪♪

256
00:10:07,273 --> 00:10:09,010
GOOD LUCK,
PUMPKIN BOY.

257
00:10:09,077 --> 00:10:11,812
TAKE YOUR PROTEIN PILLS
AND PUT YOUR HELMET ON.

258
00:10:11,878 --> 00:10:13,247
- WINDOW!
- HEY, LOOK OUT!

259
00:10:13,313 --> 00:10:16,317
- HELLO, WINDOW!
- BOY, THAT WAS CLOSE.

260
00:10:20,253 --> 00:10:21,255
I'M OUTTA HERE.

261
00:10:21,322 --> 00:10:25,225
OH... OH, MOMMY.
OH...

262
00:10:25,292 --> 00:10:26,627
GOOD AFTERNOON,
LADIES AND GENTLEMEN.

263
00:10:26,693 --> 00:10:28,395
WE ARE CRUISING AT
APPROXIMATELY 50 FEET.

264
00:10:28,462 --> 00:10:31,198
THE CAPTAIN HAS TURNED OFF
THE "NO SCREAMING" SIGN,

265
00:10:31,265 --> 00:10:34,235
AND WE JUST EMPTIED
THE WASHROOM.

266
00:10:34,302 --> 00:10:40,240
♪♪

267
00:10:40,307 --> 00:10:43,743
LOOKS LIKE AN ATOMIC
NOSE HAIR CLIPPER.

268
00:10:51,785 --> 00:10:54,922
WHY DO THEY HATE TRAINS
SO MUCH?

269
00:10:54,988 --> 00:10:56,490
IT'S NOT SO MUCH
THAT THEY HATE TRAINS,

270
00:10:56,557 --> 00:10:58,558
THEY HATE WHAT THEY
STAND FOR.

271
00:10:58,625 --> 00:11:01,262
OH, THAT CLEARS
EVERYTHING UP.

272
00:11:05,398 --> 00:11:09,237
WHOA.

273
00:11:09,303 --> 00:11:12,640
GOING DOWN.

274
00:11:15,308 --> 00:11:20,113
JANE, STOP THIS CRAZY THING!

275
00:11:20,180 --> 00:11:22,683
UNH!

276
00:11:22,750 --> 00:11:24,185
I THINK HE'S GOTTA
TAKE A LEAK.

277
00:11:35,095 --> 00:11:37,230
LUCKILY, THEY WON'T SEE HIM.

278
00:11:37,297 --> 00:11:39,767
NOW!

279
00:11:39,833 --> 00:11:42,368
HE WAS CLEVERLY DISGUISED
AS A HERSHEY'S KISS.

280
00:11:42,437 --> 00:11:44,405
I THINK HE'S JUST
DRAWN ATTENTION TO HIMSELF.

281
00:11:44,472 --> 00:11:46,707
[JOEL CHUCKLES]

282
00:11:46,773 --> 00:11:49,410
WHY DON'T THEY SHOOT HIM
WITH THE RAY GUN?

283
00:11:49,477 --> 00:11:51,778
WELL, BECAUSE EVEN BACK THEN
IN THE MOVIES,

284
00:11:51,845 --> 00:11:54,848
EVEN THE CROOKS HAD A SENSE
OF FAIR PLAY, TOM SERVO.

285
00:11:54,915 --> 00:11:57,952
OKAY, UH, IT'S A SERIAL, JOEL,
NOT A MOVIE.

286
00:11:58,052 --> 00:11:59,587
- RIGHT.
- A SERIAL!

287
00:11:59,653 --> 00:12:02,088
LET'S GET OUT OF HERE.
- AND LEAVE THE RAY GUN?

288
00:12:02,155 --> 00:12:03,623
WHAT ELSE CAN WE DO?
[GUNSHOTS]

289
00:12:03,690 --> 00:12:04,992
WELL, YOU COULD TAKE
THE TRUCK.

290
00:12:05,058 --> 00:12:07,260
NAH.

291
00:12:07,327 --> 00:12:08,595
MUCH BETTER TO RUN
IN THE DESERT ON FOOT,

292
00:12:08,662 --> 00:12:11,065
WITH NO PROVISIONS
OR ANYTHING.

293
00:12:11,132 --> 00:12:13,733
- AND EAT YOUR GUN.
- [JOEL CHUCKLES]

294
00:12:13,800 --> 00:12:15,635
HEY, IT MATCHES MY HELMET
AND EVERYTHING.

295
00:12:15,702 --> 00:12:18,238
ALL I NEED IS A SPARKMASTER
PLAY SET AND I'M DONE.

296
00:12:18,305 --> 00:12:20,607
THE LOSS OF THE RAY GUN
IS NOT TOO SERIOUS.

297
00:12:20,673 --> 00:12:22,342
I BROUGHT SUFFICIENT EQUIPMENT
FROM THE MOON

298
00:12:22,408 --> 00:12:23,610
TO BUILD SEVERAL OF THEM.

299
00:12:23,677 --> 00:12:25,813
BUT I DO NOT CARE
TO HAVE THE EARTH PEOPLE LEARN

300
00:12:25,880 --> 00:12:28,082
THE SECRETS
OF OUR WEAPONS.

301
00:12:28,148 --> 00:12:29,550
FROM THE DESCRIPTION
YOU GAVE ME

302
00:12:29,617 --> 00:12:31,218
OF YOUR ATTACKER'S
COSTUME,

303
00:12:31,252 --> 00:12:32,820
IT MUST HAVE BEEN
COMMANDO CODY

304
00:12:32,887 --> 00:12:33,953
AND HIS FLYING SUIT.

305
00:12:34,020 --> 00:12:35,122
OR A TRASHCAN HEAD.

306
00:12:35,188 --> 00:12:36,557
HE WILL PROBABLY TAKE
OUR RAY GUN

307
00:12:36,623 --> 00:12:38,792
TO HIS LABORATORY
FOR EXAMINATION,

308
00:12:38,858 --> 00:12:41,328
SO YOU MUST GO THERE AT ONCE
AND RECOVER THE ATOMIC CHAMBER

309
00:12:41,395 --> 00:12:42,630
FROM THE RAY GUN.

310
00:12:42,697 --> 00:12:44,898
THAT'S A LARGE ORDER, KRUG.

311
00:12:44,965 --> 00:12:47,535
WE HIRED OUT TO WORK YOUR
RAY GUN, BUT THIS BUSINESS--

312
00:12:47,602 --> 00:12:50,270
YOU WERE HIRED TO DO ANYTHING
THAT I MAY CONSIDER NECESSARY

313
00:12:50,337 --> 00:12:53,207
TO PAVE THE WAY FOR OUR
INVASION FROM THE MOON.

314
00:12:53,273 --> 00:12:54,842
YOU'RE BEING WELL PAID
FOR YOUR WORK,

315
00:12:54,908 --> 00:12:57,210
SO DO AS YOU'RE ORDERED.

316
00:12:57,277 --> 00:12:59,447
YEAH, WELL PAID,
BUT IN MOON ROCKS.

317
00:12:59,513 --> 00:13:02,348
MAYBE WE CAN AFFORD
ONE OF YOUR SUITS.

318
00:13:08,822 --> 00:13:10,523
HEY, THIS LOOKS LIKE
THE RIGHT DOOR.

319
00:13:10,590 --> 00:13:13,060
IS WORKING ON THIS GUN
GOING TO HOLD UP

320
00:13:13,127 --> 00:13:14,195
FINISHING THE ROCKET SHIP?

321
00:13:14,262 --> 00:13:15,328
- NO.
- MAYBE.

322
00:13:15,395 --> 00:13:16,797
I'LL JUST GIVE IT
A QUICK EXAMINATION

323
00:13:16,863 --> 00:13:18,332
AND THEN TURN IT OVER
TO THE AUTHORITIES.

324
00:13:18,398 --> 00:13:21,135
WE'LL STILL BE ABLE TO TAKE OFF
FOR THE MOON NEXT WEDNESDAY.

325
00:13:21,202 --> 00:13:25,873
♪♪

326
00:13:25,940 --> 00:13:29,042
OH, I HAT TO SHOOT
A BUTT LIKE THAT.

327
00:13:29,108 --> 00:13:30,210
[JOEL CHUCKLES]

328
00:13:30,277 --> 00:13:33,180
TAKE IT EASY
AND YOU WON'T GET HURT.

329
00:13:33,247 --> 00:13:34,648
MOVE BACK.

330
00:13:34,715 --> 00:13:38,018
THAT'S EXACTLY WHAT MY
AEROBICS INSTRUCTOR SAID.

331
00:13:41,722 --> 00:13:44,090
YEE-HAW!

332
00:13:44,157 --> 00:13:47,327
GOOD THING SCIENTISTS ARE
SUCH GOOD FIGHTERS.

333
00:13:47,393 --> 00:13:49,697
YEAH, SCIENTISTS VERSUS
HIRED THUGS--

334
00:13:49,763 --> 00:13:52,667
GEEKS AND THUGS,
YOU GOTTA LOVE IT.

335
00:13:52,733 --> 00:13:57,605
♪♪

336
00:13:57,672 --> 00:13:58,938
[GUNSHOT]

337
00:14:00,607 --> 00:14:02,577
BOY, THEY'RE USING A LOT
OF BREAKAWAY CHAIRS.

338
00:14:02,643 --> 00:14:05,145
OH, I THOUGHT THAT WAS
A LOOSE STOOL.

339
00:14:10,683 --> 00:14:13,153
AND THIS IS FOR
LOUIS PASTEUR!

340
00:14:19,025 --> 00:14:22,528
NICE FALL.

341
00:14:22,597 --> 00:14:25,632
EXCUSE ME,
MAY I CUT IN?

342
00:14:25,698 --> 00:14:27,968
ANOTHER BLOW FOR SCIENCE.

343
00:14:33,640 --> 00:14:35,342
ONE...

344
00:14:35,408 --> 00:14:38,012
TWO...

345
00:14:38,078 --> 00:14:40,413
THREE STRIKES--
YOU'RE OUTTA THERE.

346
00:14:40,480 --> 00:14:42,617
ROUTINE 27.

347
00:14:46,120 --> 00:14:47,988
AND DON'T TRY
TO FOLLOW US.

348
00:14:48,055 --> 00:14:50,657
TELL YOUR FRIENDS.

349
00:14:50,723 --> 00:14:52,558
HEY, THEY LEFT THE RAY GUN.

350
00:14:52,627 --> 00:14:54,828
YEAH, BUT THEY TOOK
THE BATTERIES.

351
00:14:59,132 --> 00:15:02,135
I DIDN'T KNOW
JACKIE GLEASON WAS IN THIS.

352
00:15:07,340 --> 00:15:13,247
THEY'RE IN THE MIDDLE...
OF A GIANT CHESS GAME.

353
00:15:13,313 --> 00:15:15,148
HMM, FRESH-GROUND PEPPER?

354
00:15:15,215 --> 00:15:18,418
KRUG CALLING RETTIK.

355
00:15:18,485 --> 00:15:20,453
LOOKS LIKE A PEPPERMILL.

356
00:15:20,520 --> 00:15:21,555
- YOU SEE--
- YEAH.

357
00:15:21,622 --> 00:15:22,823
- YEAH, GET IT?
- MM-HMM.

358
00:15:22,890 --> 00:15:25,825
- I'M LAUGHING HARD INSIDE.
- COME IN, KRUG.

359
00:15:25,892 --> 00:15:27,493
- THE ROCKET SHIP
IS LEAVING HERE

360
00:15:27,560 --> 00:15:29,797
IN FIVE DAYS
TO INVESTIGATE OUR MOON.

361
00:15:29,863 --> 00:15:32,065
I DID NOT BELIEVE THE EARTHMEN
POSSESSED A SHIP

362
00:15:32,132 --> 00:15:33,567
CAPABLE OF MAKING
THE JOURNEY.

363
00:15:33,633 --> 00:15:35,635
I JUST LEARNED
ABOUT IT MYSELF,

364
00:15:35,702 --> 00:15:37,337
BUT I'M SURE MY INFORMATION
IS CORRECT.

365
00:15:37,403 --> 00:15:39,873
STOP TALKING INTO
A SHOE BUFFER.

366
00:15:39,940 --> 00:15:43,843
- WE WILL BE PREPARED...
- HE LOOKS LIKE WILLARD SCOTT.

367
00:15:43,910 --> 00:15:46,247
AND DON'T FORGET THE CHEESE.

368
00:15:46,313 --> 00:15:51,418
AND SPEAKING OF CHEESE...

369
00:15:51,485 --> 00:15:55,622
OH, HOW I LOVE HIM.

370
00:15:55,688 --> 00:16:00,360
♪♪

371
00:16:03,563 --> 00:16:06,733
THEY'RE GONNA LAUNCH
FROM A MINIATURE GOLF COURSE?

372
00:16:06,800 --> 00:16:09,703
BE FINE IF
THEY CLEAR THE WINDMILL.

373
00:16:16,510 --> 00:16:18,578
I STILL THINK THIS IS
NO TRIP FOR A WOMAN.

374
00:16:18,645 --> 00:16:20,147
NOW, DON'T START THAT AGAIN.

375
00:16:20,213 --> 00:16:21,648
YOU'LL BE VERY GLAD
TO HAVE SOMEONE ALONG

376
00:16:21,715 --> 00:16:22,817
WHO CAN COOK YOUR MEALS.

377
00:16:22,883 --> 00:16:24,150
I'LL SAY WE WILL.
DON'T GIVE HER ANY...

378
00:16:24,183 --> 00:16:26,187
YEAH, AND PRETTY SOON
I'LL BE ABLE TO VOTE.

379
00:16:26,253 --> 00:16:27,988
I LIKE TO EAT TOO.

380
00:16:28,055 --> 00:16:30,790
NICE ENSEMBLE,
ANYWAY.

381
00:16:30,857 --> 00:16:32,392
ARE THE DICKS
COMING WITH US?

382
00:16:32,458 --> 00:16:35,895
UH, NO, WE CALL THEM
POLICE OFFICERS NOW, DEAR.

383
00:16:35,962 --> 00:16:39,032
OH, I DIDN'T KNOW.
I CAN'T EVEN VOTE.

384
00:16:39,098 --> 00:16:41,568
WELL, THE BEST OF LUCK
TO ALL OF YOU, SIR.

385
00:16:41,635 --> 00:16:43,670
HOPE THIS THING
WORKS ALL RIGHT.

386
00:16:43,737 --> 00:16:45,438
SO DO WE.
GOOD-BYE.

387
00:16:45,505 --> 00:16:48,008
GOOD-BYE, SIR.

388
00:16:48,075 --> 00:16:52,245
WE'LL JUST WAIT BACK HERE WHERE
IT'S SAFE, BY THE THRUSTERS.

389
00:16:52,312 --> 00:16:54,313
- HIYA, FOLKS.
- HELLO, HANK.

390
00:16:54,382 --> 00:16:56,250
- ALL SET?
- ALL WARMED UP.

391
00:16:56,317 --> 00:16:57,918
WE CAN TAKE OFF RIGHT NOW,
THAT IS, IF THE SHIP WILL

392
00:16:58,018 --> 00:16:59,553
STAND UP THE TESTS WE MADE
WITH THE MODEL.

393
00:16:59,620 --> 00:17:01,522
I THINK IT WILL.
NOW LET'S GO.

394
00:17:13,533 --> 00:17:15,968
SAFETY BELTS FASTENED?

395
00:17:16,035 --> 00:17:17,872
THEY'RE SITTING
IN OFFICE CHAIRS.

396
00:17:17,938 --> 00:17:19,973
FIRE PILOT JETS.

397
00:17:20,040 --> 00:17:22,275
MAKE SURE YOU HAVE
YOUR STAPLES.

398
00:17:22,342 --> 00:17:23,610
LEAN BACK TO SIMULATE
G-FORCES.

399
00:17:23,677 --> 00:17:26,380
- EVERYONE.
- FIRE MAIN JETS.

400
00:17:31,017 --> 00:17:33,387
GOOD.

401
00:17:36,190 --> 00:17:38,092
IN CASE OF AN EMERGENCY,

402
00:17:38,158 --> 00:17:40,960
YOUR OFFICE CHAIR BECOMES
A FLOATATION DEVICE.

403
00:17:45,332 --> 00:17:51,272
♪♪

404
00:17:54,675 --> 00:17:57,878
WHY, YOU'D HARDLY KNOW
WE WERE MOVING.

405
00:17:57,945 --> 00:17:59,012
WELL, BELIEVE IT OR NOT,
WE ARE,

406
00:17:59,078 --> 00:18:00,447
AT A LOT OF MILES PER MINUTE.

407
00:18:00,513 --> 00:18:02,348
SHE'S LIVING UP
TO THE TESTS WE MADE.

408
00:18:02,415 --> 00:18:07,087
- SET A COURSE FOR THE MOON.
- RIGHT.

409
00:18:07,153 --> 00:18:08,822
"A LOT OF MILES PER MINUTE"?

410
00:18:08,888 --> 00:18:11,892
HERE, FILE THIS,
I'M GOING TO THE WASHROOM.

411
00:18:11,958 --> 00:18:14,127
HERE, SIT IN MY SEAT.
I WANNA PLAY WITH YOUR STUFF.

412
00:18:18,865 --> 00:18:20,433
HEY, TRIPLE WORD SCORE!

413
00:18:20,500 --> 00:18:23,537
HEY, IS THIS A CONTRACTION?
YOU CAN'T HYPHENATE.

414
00:18:26,240 --> 00:18:27,842
YOU KNOW, I COULD MAKE IT
IN HALF THE TIME

415
00:18:27,908 --> 00:18:30,143
IF I HAD A STRAIGHTEDGE.

416
00:18:32,312 --> 00:18:36,250
SURE IS SUNNY IN SPACE.

417
00:18:36,317 --> 00:18:37,550
WE'RE JUST ABOUT HERE.

418
00:18:37,650 --> 00:18:41,255
HALFWAY ON THE COMPASS.

419
00:18:43,790 --> 00:18:45,425
LOOKS LIKE WE'RE
ON THE RIGHT TRACK.

420
00:18:45,492 --> 00:18:48,128
WE OUGHT TO BE DOWN
IN ANOTHER TWO HOURS.

421
00:18:48,195 --> 00:18:50,263
HOPE THEY HAVE A HO-JOS.

422
00:18:57,972 --> 00:19:00,673
THERE'S A CITY
JUST AHEAD.

423
00:19:00,740 --> 00:19:03,110
♪♪

424
00:19:03,177 --> 00:19:06,813
WHERE DO WE SET DOWN?

425
00:19:06,880 --> 00:19:08,115
LET'S TAKE HER BACK
IN THOSE HILLS,

426
00:19:08,182 --> 00:19:10,617
WHERE WE CAN FIND A PLACE
TO HIDE THE SHIP.

427
00:19:10,650 --> 00:19:12,618
THEN I'LL FLY OVER THE CITY
IN THE ROCKET SUIT.

428
00:19:12,685 --> 00:19:13,953
OKAY.

429
00:19:14,020 --> 00:19:16,757
YEAH, A GUY IN A LEATHER JACKET
WITH HIS BUTT ON FIRE.

430
00:19:16,823 --> 00:19:18,425
THEY'LL NEVER NOTICE THAT.
[CHUCKLES]

431
00:19:20,960 --> 00:19:23,163
SET HER DOWN
IN THAT CANYON.

432
00:19:23,230 --> 00:19:24,798
SHOULDN'T WE LAND
THE SHIP FIRST?

433
00:19:24,865 --> 00:19:26,933
OKAY.

434
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:31,805
HEY, THE MOON LOOKS
JUST LIKE ARIZONA, YOU GUYS.

435
00:19:34,507 --> 00:19:36,410
DOES IT REALLY?

436
00:19:36,477 --> 00:19:38,578
- NO.

437
00:19:38,645 --> 00:19:40,980
YOU SHOULD KNOW.

438
00:19:41,047 --> 00:19:46,953
♪♪

439
00:19:56,028 --> 00:19:57,363
HERE, LET ME HELP YOU DOWN.

440
00:19:57,430 --> 00:19:58,498
CUT! EDIT!

441
00:19:58,565 --> 00:20:00,333
ONE SMALL STEP FOR MAN,

442
00:20:00,400 --> 00:20:04,403
ONE GIANT LEAP FOR...
AIYEEE...

443
00:20:06,240 --> 00:20:09,275
MUST GO THROUGH
A LOT OF PANTS.

444
00:20:11,812 --> 00:20:15,048
HEY, IT'S EITHER
ANCIENT GREECE OR VEGAS.

445
00:20:15,115 --> 00:20:18,618
CAESAR'S WORLD.

446
00:20:18,685 --> 00:20:21,622
OH.

447
00:20:21,688 --> 00:20:22,957
WELL, THIS LOOKS TO BE
A WALL.

448
00:20:23,023 --> 00:20:25,625
I'LL GO THIS WAY.

449
00:20:25,692 --> 00:20:29,062
YOU ARE GOING IN THE RIGHT
DIRECTION, EARTHMAN.

450
00:20:29,128 --> 00:20:30,397
HOW'D THEY KNOW MY NAME?

451
00:20:30,463 --> 00:20:34,400
ENTER THE FIRST DOOR
YOU COME TO.

452
00:20:34,467 --> 00:20:36,102
- IT'S BOB BARKER.
- TURN THE CONTROL.

453
00:20:36,168 --> 00:20:38,372
THE DOOR WILL OPEN.

454
00:20:43,543 --> 00:20:46,380
HMM, HOT, COLD, OPEN.

455
00:20:46,447 --> 00:20:49,082
[DOOR CREAKING]

456
00:20:49,148 --> 00:20:50,650
YOU'D THINK ON THE MOON
THEY'D GET THE CREAKS OUT.

457
00:20:50,750 --> 00:20:52,152
[JOEL, WHISPERING]
GO ON INSIDE, IT'S OKAY.

458
00:20:52,218 --> 00:20:53,287
GO ON.

459
00:20:57,323 --> 00:20:59,258
[WHOOSHING]
EXCUSE ME.

460
00:20:59,325 --> 00:21:03,930
FIRST FLOOR, LINGERIE,
READY-TO-WEAR, NOTIONS, TOUPEES.

461
00:21:03,997 --> 00:21:06,400
- MOON MEN.
- THREE-PEES.

462
00:21:06,467 --> 00:21:08,302
[JOEL CHUCKLES]

463
00:21:14,875 --> 00:21:17,010
I AM ORAKON.

464
00:21:17,077 --> 00:21:20,047
THIS IS MY BROTHER XENON
AND MY OTHER BROTHER XENON.

465
00:21:20,113 --> 00:21:21,782
WELCOME, COMMANDO CODY.

466
00:21:32,125 --> 00:21:34,895
I AM RETTIK,
RULER OF THE MOON.

467
00:21:34,962 --> 00:21:36,863
APPARENTLY, YOU WERE
EXPECTING ME.

468
00:21:36,930 --> 00:21:38,765
OF COURSE.
FOR MANY YEARS

469
00:21:38,832 --> 00:21:40,567
OUR RADIO HAS
KEPT US INFORMED

470
00:21:40,633 --> 00:21:42,202
OF EVENTS ON EARTH.

471
00:21:42,268 --> 00:21:44,037
AND MY MEN THERE
HAVE ADVISED ME

472
00:21:44,103 --> 00:21:45,272
OF YOUR EVERY MOVE.

473
00:21:45,338 --> 00:21:46,407
I'VE LOVED YOU FROM AFAR.

474
00:21:46,473 --> 00:21:47,640
I SEE YOU HAVE ADOPTED
OUR LANGUAGE.

475
00:21:47,707 --> 00:21:51,277
YES, ALL OUR PEOPLE ARE
REQUIRED TO SPEAK ENGLISH

476
00:21:51,345 --> 00:21:53,913
SO WE CAN OPERATE MORE
EFFICIENTLY IN YOUR COUNTRY.

477
00:21:53,980 --> 00:21:55,482
AND WEAR UNDERWEAR
ON OUR HEADS.

478
00:21:55,548 --> 00:21:57,217
MIND TELLING ME WHY YOUR MEN
ARE CARRYING OUT

479
00:21:57,250 --> 00:21:59,185
THAT CAMPAIGN OF DESTRUCTION
ON EARTH?

480
00:21:59,252 --> 00:22:00,487
IT'S AN ELECTION YEAR.

481
00:22:00,553 --> 00:22:02,488
THEY ARE MERELY SOFTENING
UP YOUR DEFENSES

482
00:22:02,555 --> 00:22:05,225
FOR OUR IMPENDING
INVASION.

483
00:22:05,292 --> 00:22:07,260
WHY DO YOU WANT
TO INVADE THE EARTH?

484
00:22:07,327 --> 00:22:09,328
BECAUSE THE ATMOSPHERE
ON THE MOON

485
00:22:09,395 --> 00:22:10,963
HAS BECOME
IS SO THIN AND DRY

486
00:22:11,030 --> 00:22:13,100
IT IS IMPOSSIBLE FOR US
TO RAISE FOOD

487
00:22:13,167 --> 00:22:15,668
EXCEPT IN PRESSURIZED
GREENHOUSES

488
00:22:15,735 --> 00:22:18,572
GET A HUMIDIFIER.

489
00:22:18,638 --> 00:22:19,940
SO WE ARE PLANNING
A MASS MIGRATION

490
00:22:20,007 --> 00:22:21,340
TO YOUR WORLD.

491
00:22:21,408 --> 00:22:23,943
YOU'LL FIND THAT CONQUERING
THE EARTH ISN'T SO SIMPLE.

492
00:22:24,010 --> 00:22:26,212
UNLESS YOU BRING TREATS.

493
00:22:26,278 --> 00:22:28,448
BECAUSE OF OUR
ATOMIC WEAPONS.

494
00:22:28,515 --> 00:22:31,083
ON THE MOON WE HAVE
AN ELEMENT, LUNARIAM,

495
00:22:31,183 --> 00:22:33,820
WHICH IS FAR SUPERIOR
TO URANIUM,

496
00:22:33,887 --> 00:22:36,188
AS A BASE FOR
ATOMIC REACTIONS.

497
00:22:36,255 --> 00:22:38,358
AND WE CAN COMPLETELY
CONTROL THE FORCE

498
00:22:38,425 --> 00:22:40,227
OF THESE REACTIONS,

499
00:22:40,293 --> 00:22:42,528
ENABLING US TO BUILD
ATOMIC WEAPONS

500
00:22:42,595 --> 00:22:44,597
RANGING FROM HUGE
CANNONS TO THESE

501
00:22:44,663 --> 00:22:46,433
SMALL RAY PISTOLS.

502
00:22:46,500 --> 00:22:52,105
WISH WE HAD ONE OF THEM
DOOMSDAY MACHINES.

503
00:22:52,172 --> 00:22:54,107
IT'S VERY CONSIDERATE
OF YOU TO GIVE ME

504
00:22:54,173 --> 00:22:55,775
ALL THIS INFORMATION.

505
00:22:55,842 --> 00:22:58,945
YOU DESERVE SOME REWARD
FOR YOUR LONG JOURNEY,

506
00:22:59,012 --> 00:23:01,482
BUT UNFORTUNATELY I
CANNOT PERMIT YOU

507
00:23:01,548 --> 00:23:03,217
TO RETURN TO EARTH
WITH IT.

508
00:23:03,283 --> 00:23:05,652
- WHAT, LOVELY PARTING GIFTS?
- MAYBE I HAVE SOMETHING
TO SAY ABOUT THAT.

509
00:23:05,718 --> 00:23:09,488
EAT LEAD, SPACE PANSY.

510
00:23:09,555 --> 00:23:11,223
[WHOOSHING]

511
00:23:11,290 --> 00:23:13,460
OH, I THOUGHT THAT
WAS A SMOKE DETECTOR.

512
00:23:13,527 --> 00:23:15,062
SO MUCH FOR THE
EFFECTIVENESS OF

513
00:23:15,128 --> 00:23:16,095
YOUR WEAPONS.

514
00:23:16,162 --> 00:23:20,467
NOW I WILL DEMONSTRATE
ONE OF OURS.

515
00:23:20,533 --> 00:23:23,470
BOREDOM?

516
00:23:23,537 --> 00:23:24,470
[FIRES]

517
00:23:24,537 --> 00:23:28,742
[EXPLOSION]
NOT THE PEPPERMILL.

518
00:23:28,808 --> 00:23:33,313
SEIZE HIM!

519
00:23:35,248 --> 00:23:37,750
YOU COULD SEE THEY'RE
A MORE ADVANCED CIVILIZATION,

520
00:23:37,783 --> 00:23:39,552
THEIR FURNITURE
DOESN'T BREAK.

521
00:23:39,618 --> 00:23:42,222
AH, OH, OKAY.

522
00:23:42,288 --> 00:23:45,758
WELL, IT TIPS OVER
BUT IT DOESN'T BREAK.

523
00:23:45,825 --> 00:23:49,897
WAIT, HOLD STILL, WAIT,
WAIT, WAIT.

524
00:23:49,963 --> 00:23:55,402
NO, NOT HIM,
I LOVE HIM.

525
00:23:55,468 --> 00:23:56,402
NOPE.

526
00:23:56,470 --> 00:23:57,570
WHICH ONE?

527
00:23:57,637 --> 00:23:58,838
NO, NOT HIM.

528
00:23:58,905 --> 00:24:02,675
NO, THAT WOULD BE WRONG.

529
00:24:02,742 --> 00:24:05,578
I'VE GOT TO SHOOT
SOMEONE.

530
00:24:05,645 --> 00:24:07,680
[FIRES, EXPLOSION]

531
00:24:07,747 --> 00:24:08,748
OH!

532
00:24:08,815 --> 00:24:11,050
NO!

533
00:24:11,117 --> 00:24:14,220
HE WAS ONE
OF MY FAVORITES.

534
00:24:14,287 --> 00:24:16,455
♪♪

535
00:24:25,598 --> 00:24:28,468
THAT WAS MY ASS FACE.

536
00:24:28,535 --> 00:24:29,702
OH, WE BETTER GET
OUT OF HERE.

537
00:24:29,768 --> 00:24:31,972
I CAN'T STAND IT.

538
00:24:32,038 --> 00:24:33,340
I CAN'T STAND IT.

539
00:24:33,407 --> 00:24:34,673
WE'RE GETTING TOO
HEAVY FOR THIS.

540
00:24:34,740 --> 00:24:35,675
[FIRES]

541
00:24:35,742 --> 00:24:38,110
[EXPLOSION]

542
00:24:38,178 --> 00:24:42,115
♪♪

543
00:24:52,425 --> 00:24:54,360
WHAT IS THAT NOISE?

544
00:24:54,427 --> 00:24:56,195
WHAT IS THAT, JOEL?

545
00:24:56,262 --> 00:24:57,363
AH, I THINK I KNOW
WHAT'S WRONG.

546
00:24:57,430 --> 00:24:59,465
CAMBOT FOLLOW ME OVER
HERE, LOOK AT THEM,

547
00:24:59,532 --> 00:25:01,133
THEY'RE A BUNCH OF--
SEEM LIKE A BUNCH

548
00:25:01,200 --> 00:25:02,535
OF DEMON DOGS
OR SOMETHING.

549
00:25:02,602 --> 00:25:03,903
WHAT ARE DEMON DOGS?

550
00:25:03,970 --> 00:25:06,238
WELL, THEY'RE LIKE CHIHUAHUAS
BUT WITHOUT ANY FLESH.

551
00:25:06,305 --> 00:25:08,073
AND IT LOOKS LIKE
THEY'RE COVERING THIS SHIP.

552
00:25:08,140 --> 00:25:09,075
FOLLOW ME BACK.

553
00:25:09,142 --> 00:25:10,710
WE GOT A COUPLE
PROBLEMS, JOE.

554
00:25:10,777 --> 00:25:11,845
WHAT ARE THEY, CROW?

555
00:25:11,912 --> 00:25:13,747
WELL, FIRST, THEY'RE
COVERING THE SHIP,

556
00:25:13,813 --> 00:25:15,248
THEY'RE GOING TO WEIGH
US DOWN, OUR ORBIT'S

557
00:25:15,315 --> 00:25:16,248
GONNA START TO DECAY

558
00:25:16,315 --> 00:25:18,017
AND WE'LL ENTER
EARTH'S ATMOSPHERE.

559
00:25:18,083 --> 00:25:19,018
WE'RE GOING TO BURN UP.

560
00:25:19,085 --> 00:25:20,153
CRISPY CRITTER TIME.

561
00:25:20,220 --> 00:25:21,153
WHAT'S NUMBER TWO?

562
00:25:21,220 --> 00:25:23,088
WELL AS PUPPIES GO
WITH NO FLESH,

563
00:25:23,155 --> 00:25:24,757
THEY GOT LIKE
ZERO CUDDLE FACTOR.

564
00:25:24,823 --> 00:25:26,125
ALL RIGHT, WE GOT TO
GET THEM OFF THIS SHIP,

565
00:25:26,192 --> 00:25:27,393
THAT'S ALL THERE IS
TO IT.

566
00:25:27,460 --> 00:25:29,595
I NEED A MAN, A VOLUNTEER
SOMEBODY TO GO OUT THERE

567
00:25:29,662 --> 00:25:30,630
AND SHOO THEM OFF.

568
00:25:30,697 --> 00:25:32,865
OH, I THINK
THE CHOICE IS OBVIOUS.

569
00:25:32,932 --> 00:25:34,367
WHO'S GOT THE MIGHTY
VOICE THAT DOGS

570
00:25:34,433 --> 00:25:35,902
CAN'T SAY NO TO?

571
00:25:35,968 --> 00:25:38,037
- UH, LORNE GREENE.
- YEAH, I WAS THINKING
ABOUT THAT.

572
00:25:38,103 --> 00:25:40,473
I SAID "WHO'S GOT THE
MIGHTY VOICE THAT DOGS CAN'T--"

573
00:25:40,540 --> 00:25:43,243
[BOTH] - YOU DO, TOM SERVO.
- RIGHT, OKAY.

574
00:25:43,310 --> 00:25:44,510
WHO'S WICKED AWESOME?

575
00:25:44,577 --> 00:25:46,245
- UH, THE CLASH.
- EVO.

576
00:25:46,312 --> 00:25:47,647
WHO'S THE HUMAN WHO CAN'T
BREATHE IN SPACE

577
00:25:47,713 --> 00:25:49,148
AND GET DOGS OFF
THEIR SHIP?

578
00:25:49,215 --> 00:25:51,852
RIGHT, I CAN'T, TOM SERVO,
YOU'RE THE MAN.

579
00:25:51,952 --> 00:25:52,885
WHO'S BAD?

580
00:25:52,952 --> 00:25:54,487
- [BOTH] TOM SERVO.
- WHO'S BAD?

581
00:25:54,553 --> 00:25:56,723
- [BOTH] TOM SERVO.
- THAT'S RIGHT, I'M BAD.

582
00:25:56,790 --> 00:25:57,723
NOW GIVE ME A ROLLED-UP
NEWSPAPER,

583
00:25:57,790 --> 00:25:59,325
AND DON'T BOTHER
SO SHUT THE DOOR.

584
00:25:59,392 --> 00:26:01,427
I'LL BE RIGHT BACK,
KEEP MY DINNER WARM.

585
00:26:01,493 --> 00:26:03,128
BOY, I'M GLAD HE'S
GOING OUT THERE, JOEL.

586
00:26:03,195 --> 00:26:05,332
I CAN'T EVEN LOOK AT A PLATE
OF SPARE RIBS

587
00:26:05,398 --> 00:26:06,365
WITHOUT GETTING WOOZY.

588
00:26:06,432 --> 00:26:07,700
YEAH, DON'T WORRY
ABOUT IT, CROW,

589
00:26:07,767 --> 00:26:09,668
LET'S JUST WATCH THE MONITOR
AND SEE WHAT HAPPENS.

590
00:26:09,735 --> 00:26:11,437
[TOM]
OKAY, PUPPY PARTY'S OVER.

591
00:26:11,503 --> 00:26:15,075
EVERYBODY OFF, THIS IS TOM
SERVO YOUR WORST
DOGGY NIGHTMARE.

592
00:26:15,142 --> 00:26:16,475
DON'T GET ME MAD,
I DON'T THINK

593
00:26:16,542 --> 00:26:18,143
YOU'D LIKE ME WHEN
I'M MAD.

594
00:26:18,210 --> 00:26:19,478
OH, WAIT, STOP IT.

595
00:26:19,545 --> 00:26:20,780
PUT YOUR LEGS DOWN.

596
00:26:20,847 --> 00:26:22,615
[LAUGHS]
ICKY! CACA!

597
00:26:22,682 --> 00:26:23,817
OH, LET ME IN.

598
00:26:23,917 --> 00:26:27,053
OH, JEEZ, NEXT TIME
I'LL RUB YOUR FACES IN IT.

599
00:26:27,120 --> 00:26:28,053
[BOTH]
OH!

600
00:26:28,120 --> 00:26:30,357
TOM SERVO, WHAT HAPPENED?

601
00:26:30,423 --> 00:26:32,325
WELL, JOEL, THERE'S
ONLY ONE WAY TO PUT IT.

602
00:26:32,392 --> 00:26:34,193
THEY DISGRACED THEMSELVES
ON ME.

603
00:26:34,260 --> 00:26:35,362
I FEEL SO DIRTY.

604
00:26:35,428 --> 00:26:37,763
HAVEN'T EFFECTED YOUR
LOOKS ANY.

605
00:26:37,830 --> 00:26:39,232
YUCK, GIVES ME THE WILLIES.

606
00:26:39,298 --> 00:26:40,967
OH WHY WOULD ANYONE WANT
TO DO THAT

607
00:26:41,033 --> 00:26:44,237
TO LOVEABLE OLD ME,
TOM SERVO?

608
00:26:44,303 --> 00:26:45,638
WELL, TOM, LISTEN,

609
00:26:45,705 --> 00:26:47,740
THERE'S BEEN SOMETHING
I'VE BEEN DREADING TELLING YOU

610
00:26:47,807 --> 00:26:50,110
SINCE THE DATE OF
YOUR CREATION.

611
00:26:50,177 --> 00:26:52,845
WHEN YOU WERE STILL
ON THE DRAWING BOARD,

612
00:26:52,912 --> 00:26:55,815
I BASED YOUR PLANS ON
A FIRE HYDRANT.

613
00:26:55,882 --> 00:26:57,417
OH, MAN, YOU CAN LOOK
ME IN THE BUBBLE

614
00:26:57,483 --> 00:27:01,053
AND TELL ME THAT,
I'M A PUBLIC UTILITY.

615
00:27:01,120 --> 00:27:03,222
IT'S OVER, I'M GOING
TO GO HOSE OFF.

616
00:27:03,288 --> 00:27:05,692
[LAUGHS]

617
00:27:05,758 --> 00:27:07,893
♪♪

618
00:27:11,765 --> 00:27:13,800
♪♪

619
00:27:16,670 --> 00:27:18,638
HOW'D YOU GET RID
OF THOSE DEMON DOGS?

620
00:27:18,705 --> 00:27:19,705
I DON'T KNOW.

621
00:27:19,772 --> 00:27:22,608
THIS IS THE FEATURE
PRESENTATION.

622
00:27:22,675 --> 00:27:23,810
CASTEÑDA?

623
00:27:23,877 --> 00:27:25,712
I DIDN'T KNOW THIS
WAS GOING TO BE A MUSICAL.

624
00:27:25,778 --> 00:27:28,280
JORGE MONDRAGON, HE MUST
BE PLAYING THE MONSTER.

625
00:27:28,348 --> 00:27:30,617
NO, IT'S THE MUMMY.

626
00:27:30,683 --> 00:27:31,617
"ROBOT."

627
00:27:31,685 --> 00:27:32,685
[ALL]
YAY!

628
00:27:32,752 --> 00:27:34,087
"VS. THE AZTEC MUMMY"?

629
00:27:34,153 --> 00:27:36,588
[ALL]
BOO!

630
00:27:39,692 --> 00:27:40,927
ALFRED SALAZAR.

631
00:27:40,993 --> 00:27:43,863
HE'S A BOXER, ISN'T HE?

632
00:27:43,930 --> 00:27:45,998
I DON'T KNOW.

633
00:27:46,065 --> 00:27:47,567
GARCIA DE LEON.

634
00:27:47,633 --> 00:27:49,202
FOUNTAIN OF YOUTH GUY?

635
00:27:49,268 --> 00:27:53,138
- NO.
- OH.

636
00:27:53,205 --> 00:27:55,208
I DO THINK JOSE LI-HO
IS THE INVENTOR

637
00:27:55,275 --> 00:27:57,410
OF THAT CREAM
SANDWICH THOUGH.

638
00:27:57,477 --> 00:28:02,482
- OH, OKAY.
- THE LI-HO.

639
00:28:02,548 --> 00:28:07,887
WHEN IN MEXICO VISIT
C.L.A.S.A. STUDIOS.

640
00:28:07,953 --> 00:28:09,388
BUT DON'T DRINK THE WATER.

641
00:28:09,455 --> 00:28:12,758
THIS MOVIE IS THE PRODUCER'S
ANSWER TO MONTEZUMA'S REVENGE.

642
00:28:16,763 --> 00:28:18,363
WHEN IN CORAL GABLES, FLORIDA,

643
00:28:18,432 --> 00:28:20,433
VISIT SOUNDLAB INC
AND VISIT OUR

644
00:28:20,500 --> 00:28:22,168
GLASS-BOTTOMED BOATS.

645
00:28:22,235 --> 00:28:24,737
WHEN IN SAN FERNANDO,
VISIT MANUEL.

646
00:28:24,803 --> 00:28:26,072
AND TICKLE HIS BELLY.

647
00:28:26,138 --> 00:28:27,307
TICKLE HIS BELLY.

648
00:28:27,373 --> 00:28:29,242
HE'LL SHAKE HIS LEG
FOR YOU.

649
00:28:33,212 --> 00:28:35,082
NICE TITLE CARD PAINTING,
DON'T YOU THINK?

650
00:28:35,148 --> 00:28:36,348
YEAH, WHAT IS THAT?

651
00:28:36,415 --> 00:28:37,517
KIND OF A MUMMY?

652
00:28:37,550 --> 00:28:38,552
IT LOOKS LIKE
A MUMMY.

653
00:28:38,618 --> 00:28:39,552
MUST'VE TAKEN MINUTES.

654
00:28:39,618 --> 00:28:40,787
MR. MUMMY.

655
00:28:40,853 --> 00:28:43,188
[NARRATOR]
HOW FAR CAN THE HUMAN MIND

656
00:28:43,255 --> 00:28:45,858
PENETRATE THE MYSTERIES
OF THE GREAT BEYOND?

657
00:28:45,925 --> 00:28:47,160
13-FEET, FOUR INCHES,

658
00:28:47,227 --> 00:28:48,628
1920 OLYMPICS.

659
00:28:48,695 --> 00:28:51,463
IS BASED UPON AN
EXTRAORDINARY EXPERIMENT.

660
00:28:51,530 --> 00:28:54,100
CARRIED OUT BY DRS.
HUGHES AND TOONEY--

661
00:28:54,167 --> 00:28:56,903
TOONEY, OH-OH,
FRANCIS, OH.

662
00:28:56,970 --> 00:28:59,305
THERE IS NO DOUBT
AS TO ITS AUTHENTICITY--

663
00:28:59,372 --> 00:29:01,073
EXCEPT FOR OUR
OWN DOUBTS.

664
00:29:01,140 --> 00:29:02,442
PARTICIPATING IN
THE EXPERIMENT

665
00:29:02,508 --> 00:29:04,477
SWORN TO BY A
NOTARY PUBLIC,

666
00:29:04,543 --> 00:29:07,013
PRECLUDE THE POSSIBILITY
OF ANY FRAUD.

667
00:29:07,080 --> 00:29:09,748
THIS PICTURE IS A
COMBINATION OF FACTUAL DATA

668
00:29:09,815 --> 00:29:11,717
MIXED WITH FICTION.

669
00:29:11,818 --> 00:29:13,720
SORT OF LIKE THE
IRAN-CONTRA AFFAIR.

670
00:29:13,787 --> 00:29:16,388
MEXICO, THIS IS THE CITY,
MY NAME IS FRIDAY,

671
00:29:16,455 --> 00:29:20,460
I CARRY A BADGE, I DON'T NEED
NO STINKING BADGE.

672
00:29:20,527 --> 00:29:22,028
THIS IS A REAL CAR,

673
00:29:22,095 --> 00:29:24,363
THE PEOPLE, HOWEVER,
ARE FICTIONAL.

674
00:29:24,430 --> 00:29:26,867
THEIR ACTING,
HOWEVER, IS BAD.

675
00:29:26,933 --> 00:29:27,867
- REAL BAD.
- REAL BAD.

676
00:29:27,933 --> 00:29:32,805
[DOOR CLOSES]

677
00:29:32,872 --> 00:29:35,142
REAL SLOW, TOO.

678
00:29:35,208 --> 00:29:40,980
THESE ARE TWO GUYS
WITH HATS.

679
00:29:41,047 --> 00:29:42,015
[DOORBELL BUZZES]

680
00:29:42,082 --> 00:29:43,517
I'M COMING.

681
00:29:43,583 --> 00:29:44,983
JUST A MINUTE.

682
00:29:45,083 --> 00:29:46,318
HOLD ONTO YOUR SHORTS.

683
00:29:46,385 --> 00:29:47,420
I'M COMING.

684
00:29:47,487 --> 00:29:50,223
MY LEGS ARE OLD,
MY TEETH ARE GRAY.

685
00:29:50,290 --> 00:29:55,362
DON'T LEAVE,
I'M COMING.

686
00:29:55,428 --> 00:29:56,362
GOOD EVENING.

687
00:29:56,428 --> 00:29:57,830
- GOOD EVENING.
- GOOD EVENING.

688
00:29:57,897 --> 00:29:58,832
- GOOD EVENING.
- GOOD EVENING.

689
00:29:58,898 --> 00:29:59,865
GOOD EVENING.

690
00:29:59,932 --> 00:30:01,968
GOOD EVENING.

691
00:30:02,035 --> 00:30:04,437
GOOD EVENING.

692
00:30:04,503 --> 00:30:07,173
DR. DIAZ, DR. ESTER, WHAT A
PLEASURE TO HAVE YOU HERE.

693
00:30:07,240 --> 00:30:09,975
DR. KILDARE, DR. SHOAL,
DR. PEPPER.

694
00:30:10,042 --> 00:30:11,577
VERY WELL, THANK YOU,
AND YOU?

695
00:30:11,643 --> 00:30:13,412
THE SAME OLD LABORS,
ALWAYS WORKING.

696
00:30:13,478 --> 00:30:14,413
TRYING TO FIND NEW WAYS

697
00:30:14,480 --> 00:30:16,048
TO HELP PATIENTS
DIE PAINLESSLY.

698
00:30:16,115 --> 00:30:17,150
- FUNNY.
- PLEASE DON'T JOKE,

699
00:30:17,183 --> 00:30:18,150
BUT WON'T YOU COME IN?

700
00:30:18,250 --> 00:30:20,152
MY HUSBAND IS IN THERE
WAITING FOR YOU.

701
00:30:20,220 --> 00:30:21,253
AT HOME THIS EVENING.

702
00:30:21,320 --> 00:30:22,255
IT'S NO TROUBLE, DOCTOR.

703
00:30:22,322 --> 00:30:23,255
WE'RE DELIGHTED.

704
00:30:23,322 --> 00:30:25,692
WHO'D COMPLAIN AT HAVING
THE OPPORTUNITY

705
00:30:25,758 --> 00:30:27,460
OF VISITING WITH SUCH
A BEAUTIFUL YOUNG LADY

706
00:30:27,527 --> 00:30:28,828
AS YOUR WIFE, FLORA.

707
00:30:28,895 --> 00:30:29,828
FLATTERER.

708
00:30:29,895 --> 00:30:30,963
ISN'T THAT FLOYD,
THE BARBER?

709
00:30:31,030 --> 00:30:32,065
FINE, DOCTOR.

710
00:30:32,132 --> 00:30:33,065
PLEASE, SIT DOWN,
GENTLEMEN.

711
00:30:33,132 --> 00:30:36,802
THANK YOU.

712
00:30:36,870 --> 00:30:38,203
HEY, NOT EVERYBODY SIT
WITH HER,

713
00:30:38,270 --> 00:30:39,272
SPREAD OUT, COME ON.

714
00:30:39,338 --> 00:30:41,140
FLOYD GETS THE
COMFY CHAIR.

715
00:30:41,207 --> 00:30:42,608
I'VE TAKEN THE LIBERTY
OF CALLING YOU HERE

716
00:30:42,675 --> 00:30:44,443
BECAUSE I THINK IT'S TIME
I REVEAL SOMETHING

717
00:30:44,510 --> 00:30:45,578
VERY SERIOUS.

718
00:30:45,645 --> 00:30:46,612
LET'S HEAR IT THEN.

719
00:30:46,678 --> 00:30:48,347
MY UNDERWEAR IS
100 YEARS OLD.

720
00:30:48,413 --> 00:30:49,348
IT'S ABOUT THE AZTEC
BREASTPLATE

721
00:30:49,415 --> 00:30:50,317
AND THE BRACELET,
GENTLEMEN.

722
00:30:50,383 --> 00:30:51,350
HOW IS THAT?

723
00:30:51,417 --> 00:30:52,352
I PUT THEM ON
AT NIGHT AND DANCE.

724
00:30:52,418 --> 00:30:53,352
... THE WHOLE THING WAS

725
00:30:53,418 --> 00:30:54,387
FORGOTTEN LONG AGO.

726
00:30:54,453 --> 00:30:55,522
IT'S A CLOSED BOOK, DOCTOR.

727
00:30:55,588 --> 00:30:57,957
THAT'S EXACTLY WHAT
I THOUGHT TOO.

728
00:30:58,023 --> 00:30:59,725
BUT THINGS HAVE HAPPENED
LATELY THAT

729
00:30:59,792 --> 00:31:02,795
I THINK YOU TWO SHOULD
KNOW ABOUT.

730
00:31:02,862 --> 00:31:03,863
MY FRIENDS, BE PATIENT
AND ALLOW ME

731
00:31:03,930 --> 00:31:04,897
TO TELL YOU A STORY.

732
00:31:04,963 --> 00:31:05,965
WE CAN'T.

733
00:31:06,032 --> 00:31:08,367
ALTHOUGH YOU KNOW PART
OF THE HISTORY,

734
00:31:08,433 --> 00:31:09,368
THERE ARE SOME THINGS
YOU IGNORE.

735
00:31:09,435 --> 00:31:10,603
LIKE YOU?

736
00:31:10,670 --> 00:31:12,638
THE BEST THING TO DO IS
TO BEGIN AT THE BEGINNING.

737
00:31:12,705 --> 00:31:14,140
I THINK THAT'S BEGIN
THE BEGIN.

738
00:31:14,207 --> 00:31:18,110
THAT OCCASION YEARS AGO.

739
00:31:18,177 --> 00:31:20,747
FIVE TO BE EXACT,
WHEN WE HELD A CONVENTION

740
00:31:20,813 --> 00:31:23,115
ON PSYCHIATRY IN THE CITY.

741
00:31:23,182 --> 00:31:25,452
I ATTENDED AND GAVE
A TALK ON THE RESULTS

742
00:31:25,518 --> 00:31:28,553
OF MY STUDIES RELATED TO
THE REGRESSION OF A PATIENT

743
00:31:28,622 --> 00:31:31,523
TO A PAST LIFE THROUGH
THE USES OF HYPNOSIS.

744
00:31:31,590 --> 00:31:33,827
MY THEORY WAS GREETED WITH
AMAZEMENT AND INCREDULITY.

745
00:31:33,893 --> 00:31:36,462
I SHOULD'VE OPENED
WITH A JOKE.

746
00:31:36,528 --> 00:31:38,030
AMONG OTHERS ATTENDING
THAT DAY,

747
00:31:38,097 --> 00:31:40,533
- WERE YOU, DR. ESTHER?
- FLOYD, THE BARBER.

748
00:31:40,600 --> 00:31:41,533
AND YOU, DR. VILLAS.

749
00:31:41,600 --> 00:31:43,068
OF COURSE, TENNESSEE
ERNIE FORD.

750
00:31:43,135 --> 00:31:44,070
DR. KRUPP.

751
00:31:44,137 --> 00:31:45,972
AND THE EVIL JUDGE
ROBERT BORK.

752
00:31:46,038 --> 00:31:47,340
SUBJECT OF RIDICULE.

753
00:31:47,407 --> 00:31:49,542
AND I LEFT THE CONVENTION
BITTER AND DEFEATED.

754
00:31:49,608 --> 00:31:50,843
SAME AS ALWAYS.

755
00:31:50,910 --> 00:31:52,978
I GOT TO THE HOUSE FEELING
UNSURE OF THESE IDEAS.

756
00:31:53,045 --> 00:31:54,447
I'D BEEN SQUELCHED.

757
00:31:54,513 --> 00:31:56,482
BUT I JUST COULDN'T ACCEPT
THE OTHER OPINIONS OF MY THEORY

758
00:31:56,548 --> 00:31:58,017
YOU EVER BEEN
SQUELCHED, JOEL?

759
00:31:58,083 --> 00:32:01,320
UH-UH.

760
00:32:01,387 --> 00:32:03,122
THAT NIGHT, FLORA
OFFERED TO UNDERGO

761
00:32:03,188 --> 00:32:04,457
A HYPNOTIC TEST.

762
00:32:04,523 --> 00:32:07,227
SHE BECAME FAUNA,
MY LITTLE HOUSEPLANT.

763
00:32:07,293 --> 00:32:09,495
HEY, IT'S BETSY ROSS,
YOU GUYS.

764
00:32:09,562 --> 00:32:12,665
IN CAMEO.

765
00:32:12,732 --> 00:32:14,400
DURING HER PAST LIFE,

766
00:32:14,467 --> 00:32:16,435
FLORA HAD LIVED AMONG
THE GREAT PEOPLE

767
00:32:16,502 --> 00:32:17,437
OF THE AZTECS.

768
00:32:17,503 --> 00:32:19,005
SHE TOLD OF SUCH
STRANGE THINGS,

769
00:32:19,072 --> 00:32:20,373
AMAZING THINGS.

770
00:32:20,440 --> 00:32:22,642
NAUGHTY THINGS.

771
00:32:22,708 --> 00:32:24,343
HER NAME HAD BEEN XOCHITL.

772
00:32:24,410 --> 00:32:25,912
SHE WAS DEEPLY IN LOVE
WITH A BRAVE

773
00:32:25,978 --> 00:32:29,548
AND HIGH-BORN WARRIOR
CALLED POPOCA.

774
00:32:29,615 --> 00:32:32,518
THEY GOT A MAD
POSH FOR HATS.

775
00:32:32,585 --> 00:32:34,020
SO THEY DECIDED
TO RUN AWAY,

776
00:32:34,087 --> 00:32:35,422
EVEN THOUGH IT WAS
HER SACRED DUTY

777
00:32:35,488 --> 00:32:36,688
TO PRESERVE HER
MAIDENHOOD,

778
00:32:36,755 --> 00:32:39,358
AND BE SACRIFICED TO
THE GOD DE CAPLA COPA.

779
00:32:39,425 --> 00:32:40,893
- THE GOD OF DECAFFEINATED
COFFEE.
- THEY WERE DISCOVERED

780
00:32:40,960 --> 00:32:44,397
BY THE TRIBAL PRIESTS.

781
00:32:44,463 --> 00:32:46,665
THEY PREPARED HEARTY
SOUPS AND BROTHS

782
00:32:46,732 --> 00:32:48,300
AND FORCED THEM
ON THEIR GUESTS

783
00:32:48,367 --> 00:32:51,370
FOR THEY TRULY KNEW
HOW TO HANDLE A HUNGRY MAN.

784
00:32:51,437 --> 00:32:54,740
THIS IS CHICKEN NOODLE SOUP
THAT I LET STEEP

785
00:32:54,807 --> 00:32:58,510
ALL DAY IN THE SUN,
IT'S LIKE SUN TEA.

786
00:32:58,577 --> 00:33:00,178
- BETTER THAN BORSCHT,
- YEP.

787
00:33:00,245 --> 00:33:01,513
FOR YOUR GOOD HEALTH.

788
00:33:01,580 --> 00:33:04,483
SEE, MOMMY'S DRINKING IT,
HMM, NUM-NUM-NUM-NUM-NUM,

789
00:33:04,550 --> 00:33:06,052
OPEN UP, HERE'S
THE STEAM SHOVEL,

790
00:33:06,118 --> 00:33:09,155
HOT, HOT.

791
00:33:09,222 --> 00:33:11,623
NOTHING LIKE
A HOT STEAM SHOVEL.

792
00:33:11,690 --> 00:33:13,192
GETS YOU GOING
IN THE MORNING.

793
00:33:13,258 --> 00:33:15,895
[ALMADA]
AS PUNISHMENT, THE WARRIOR
WAS BURIED ALIVE,

794
00:33:15,962 --> 00:33:18,063
AND AN ETERNAL CURSE
WAS PLACED UPON HIM.

795
00:33:18,130 --> 00:33:20,065
THEN THINGS GOT BAD.

796
00:33:20,132 --> 00:33:23,568
GHEORGHE ZAMFIR, MASTER
OF THE PAN FLUTE, PLAYED.

797
00:33:23,635 --> 00:33:24,803
BUT IT DIDN'T LAST LONG.

798
00:33:24,870 --> 00:33:26,072
AS PART OF HER PUNISHMENT,

799
00:33:26,138 --> 00:33:28,808
SHE WAS SUBMITTED TO
THE DREADED BINOCULAR JOKE.

800
00:33:28,875 --> 00:33:29,908
[SINGING IN AZTEC]

801
00:33:29,975 --> 00:33:33,445
THEN, ETHEL MERMAN OPENED
WITH A SONG.

802
00:33:33,512 --> 00:33:36,315
OH, THIS IS HORRIBLE.

803
00:33:37,250 --> 00:33:38,718
[VOLUME DECREASES]

804
00:33:42,888 --> 00:33:45,458
[MAKING CHANTING NOISES]

805
00:33:50,328 --> 00:33:53,332
KIND OF LIKE FINGERS
ON A CHALKBOARD.

806
00:33:53,398 --> 00:33:58,437
[SINGING CONTINUES]

807
00:34:05,143 --> 00:34:07,347
- WHAT THE?
- THAT'S BETTER.

808
00:34:07,413 --> 00:34:10,115
[MUSIC DECREASES IN VOLUME]
PEELING THE CHROME
OFF MY BODY.

809
00:34:10,182 --> 00:34:13,252
[DECREASES IN VOLUME AGAIN]

810
00:34:19,625 --> 00:34:20,793
[MUSIC CONTINUES]

811
00:34:20,860 --> 00:34:23,963
[SINGING]
♪ MAZOLA CORN GOODNESS ♪

812
00:34:30,135 --> 00:34:31,970
- [HUMMING]
- HEY, IT'S A PERUVIAN

813
00:34:32,037 --> 00:34:35,975
ALLSTATE REPRESENTATIVE.

814
00:34:36,042 --> 00:34:37,843
HE'S STONED.

815
00:34:37,910 --> 00:34:43,248
[JOEL LAUGHS]

816
00:34:43,315 --> 00:34:46,818
THE CEREMONY LASTED
WELL INTO THE NIGHT.

817
00:34:50,288 --> 00:34:51,457
WHAT A PARTY.

818
00:34:51,523 --> 00:34:55,595
I'VE GOT RHYTHM
IN MY DIODES.

819
00:34:55,662 --> 00:34:57,663
LET'S SEE, NOW, WHAT CAN
WE DO WITH HER HAIR?

820
00:34:57,730 --> 00:34:59,365
WELL, WE COULD GIVE HER
A SWINGING BOB,

821
00:34:59,432 --> 00:35:00,933
OR, OH, SHE'S SCHEDULED
TO DIE,

822
00:35:01,000 --> 00:35:02,935
JUST GIVE HER A BLOW DRY
AND A RINSE.

823
00:35:03,002 --> 00:35:04,770
IT DOESN'T SEEM FAIR
THAT THEY TEASE HER HAIR

824
00:35:04,837 --> 00:35:06,872
RIGHT BEFORE SHE'S KILLED.

825
00:35:06,938 --> 00:35:08,573
TEASING'S ALWAYS BAD.

826
00:35:08,640 --> 00:35:10,943
THIS HAS GOT TO BE
ONE OF THE MOST BORING RIDES

827
00:35:11,010 --> 00:35:13,445
AT DISNEYLAND, DO YOU
REALIZE THAT, YOU GUYS?

828
00:35:13,512 --> 00:35:17,550
AZTECS OF THE CARIBBEAN?

829
00:35:17,650 --> 00:35:19,585
HOW LOW WILL SHE GO?

830
00:35:19,652 --> 00:35:22,222
THEN SHE WAS
BENT AT THE WAIST?

831
00:35:22,288 --> 00:35:23,990
HEY, WATCH YOUR
HAND, BUDDY.

832
00:35:24,057 --> 00:35:26,758
KIND OF LOOKS LIKE
DIRTY DANCING, DOESN'T IT?

833
00:35:26,825 --> 00:35:28,627
[SINGING]
♪ I'VE REACHED THE END ♪

834
00:35:28,693 --> 00:35:30,028
♪ OF MY LIFE ♪

835
00:35:30,095 --> 00:35:33,798
♪ AND I'M WAITING
FOR THE KNIFE TO FALL ♪

836
00:35:36,768 --> 00:35:39,672
MAN, LOOK, IT'S THE JETS.

837
00:35:39,738 --> 00:35:45,277
[SPEAKING IN AZTEC]

838
00:35:45,343 --> 00:35:46,645
WHAT'S HE SAYING?

839
00:35:46,712 --> 00:35:48,713
HE'S SAYING LIVE FAST,
DIE YOUNG,

840
00:35:48,780 --> 00:35:51,217
AND LEAVE A GOOD-LOOKING
CORPSE.

841
00:35:51,317 --> 00:35:52,652
THAT WAS YEARS BEFORE
JAMES DEAN

842
00:35:52,718 --> 00:35:53,920
EVEN EXISTED.

843
00:35:53,987 --> 00:35:54,953
[ALMADA]
SHE WAS ADORNED WITH THE

844
00:35:55,020 --> 00:35:56,255
BRACELETS AND
THE BREASTPLATE,

845
00:35:56,322 --> 00:35:58,557
WHICH WERE ENGRAVED
WITH HIEROGLYPHICS,

846
00:35:58,623 --> 00:36:02,462
INDICATING WHERE THE AZTEC
TREASURE WAS HIDDEN.

847
00:36:02,528 --> 00:36:04,197
THEN THEY CUT OUT
HER HEART.

848
00:36:04,263 --> 00:36:06,165
BUT AS SHE BEGAN TO
REGAIN CONSCIOUSNESS,

849
00:36:06,232 --> 00:36:07,967
AND THE EXACT MOMENT I
CAME TO THE END

850
00:36:08,033 --> 00:36:09,668
OF MY LITTLE EXPERIMENT,

851
00:36:09,735 --> 00:36:13,272
SHE STRUGGLED
AND BEGAN TO SHOUT.

852
00:36:13,338 --> 00:36:16,508
[SCREAMING]

853
00:36:16,575 --> 00:36:18,577
FLORA HAD A TERRIBLE
ATTACK OF SOME KIND,

854
00:36:18,643 --> 00:36:20,245
AND HER BLOOD PRESSURE
DROPPED TO SUCH

855
00:36:20,312 --> 00:36:22,782
AN EXTENT, THAT WE
WERE AFRAID SHE MIGHT DIE.

856
00:36:22,848 --> 00:36:23,883
A COUPLE OF WEEKS LATER,

857
00:36:23,950 --> 00:36:25,652
WE DISCOVERED THAT
DR. KRUPP,

858
00:36:25,718 --> 00:36:26,785
A MAN WHO HAD SUDDENLY BECOME

859
00:36:26,852 --> 00:36:28,922
A DANGEROUS CRIMINAL
IN THE UNDERWORLD,

860
00:36:28,988 --> 00:36:31,123
HAD BEEN THERE SPYING
DURING MY EXPERIMENT.

861
00:36:31,190 --> 00:36:33,692
♪♪

862
00:36:37,128 --> 00:36:38,363
[ALMADA]
THE EXPERIMENT HAD BEEN

863
00:36:38,430 --> 00:36:39,865
A COMPLETE SUCCESS.

864
00:36:39,932 --> 00:36:42,033
BUT SINCE WE REALIZED THAT
NO ONE WOULD BELIEVE US

865
00:36:42,100 --> 00:36:45,103
UNLESS WE COULD COME UP
WITH ABSOLUTE PROOF.

866
00:36:45,170 --> 00:36:46,572
WE DECIDED TO SEARCH
IN THE BASEMENT.

867
00:36:46,638 --> 00:36:49,175
I COULDN'T WAIT TO SHOW
THEM MY BUMPER POOL TABLE.

868
00:36:49,242 --> 00:36:52,545
AND MY FINE SELECTION
OF JAMS AND JELLIES

869
00:36:52,612 --> 00:36:55,915
AND A COMPOST THAT I HAD
LAID OUT.

870
00:36:55,982 --> 00:36:58,283
♪♪

871
00:37:01,920 --> 00:37:04,590
FLORA, OUR GUIDE, WAS TIED
TO MY WAIST

872
00:37:04,657 --> 00:37:08,527
SO WE WOULDN'T
BE SEPARATED.

873
00:37:08,593 --> 00:37:10,495
♪♪

874
00:37:12,632 --> 00:37:16,335
WHY FLOYD BROUGHT
THE BEAVER, I DON'T KNOW.

875
00:37:20,272 --> 00:37:24,710
OH, MY, THERE'S A LIGHT.

876
00:37:24,777 --> 00:37:28,713
WE'RE THINKING OF
EXPANDING THIS WHOLE THING.

877
00:37:28,780 --> 00:37:30,617
MAKING A RUMPUS ROOM.

878
00:37:30,650 --> 00:37:32,818
FOR OUR RUMPUS.

879
00:37:32,885 --> 00:37:35,722
AND SPEAKING OF RUMPUSES,
THERE'S FLORA.

880
00:37:35,788 --> 00:37:40,558
LEFT FOOT, RIGHT,
LEFT RIGHT.

881
00:37:40,627 --> 00:37:41,893
AH!

882
00:37:41,960 --> 00:37:45,263
WE'LL HAVE THIS BLOCKING
DOWN IN NO TIME.

883
00:37:45,330 --> 00:37:46,798
SUDDENLY, THERE IT WAS,

884
00:37:46,865 --> 00:37:49,668
MY SIX-SIDED BUMPER
POOL TABLE.

885
00:38:02,213 --> 00:38:04,450
I THINK A SWAG LAMP HERE
AND A BEADED CURTAIN

886
00:38:04,517 --> 00:38:07,553
WOULD REALLY BRIGHTEN
THE PLACE UP.

887
00:38:07,620 --> 00:38:09,722
♪ ONCE A JOLLY SWAG LAMP ♪

888
00:38:09,788 --> 00:38:12,558
♪ WAITED BY THE BOULEVARD ♪

889
00:38:12,625 --> 00:38:14,727
♪♪

890
00:38:19,132 --> 00:38:23,335
[WHISPERING]
GO THAT WAY.

891
00:38:26,838 --> 00:38:28,773
THERE WAS
NO DENYING IT,

892
00:38:28,840 --> 00:38:31,410
WE WERE WALKING
IN A CIRCLE.

893
00:38:31,477 --> 00:38:34,913
♪♪

894
00:38:41,953 --> 00:38:44,923
PROFESSOR, I THINK WE'RE UP
AGAINST A DEAD END.

895
00:38:44,990 --> 00:38:46,158
IT CAN'T BE POSSIBLE.

896
00:38:46,225 --> 00:38:47,993
THE AZTECS WOULDN'T BUILD
A SECRET PASSAGE WAY

897
00:38:48,060 --> 00:38:49,828
JUST TO HAVE IT END UP
FOR NO RHYME OR REASON.

898
00:38:49,895 --> 00:38:54,933
NOT THE KIND OF AZTEC
YOU'RE USED TO DEALING WITH.

899
00:38:55,000 --> 00:38:58,303
IT'S A CUL DE SAC.

900
00:38:58,370 --> 00:39:01,140
PROFESSOR, IT
SOUNDS HOLLOW.

901
00:39:01,207 --> 00:39:03,942
WELL, STOP KNOCKING
ON MY HEAD.

902
00:39:04,008 --> 00:39:05,177
BUT IT'S SO THICK
THAT IT'S SENSELESS

903
00:39:05,243 --> 00:39:06,245
TO TRY TO BREAK THROUGH.

904
00:39:06,312 --> 00:39:07,480
MY HEAD?

905
00:39:07,547 --> 00:39:12,283
OR THE WALL?

906
00:39:12,350 --> 00:39:17,623
I'LL PUSH.

907
00:39:17,690 --> 00:39:23,628
PINACATE, LEND ME
A HAND, PLEASE.

908
00:39:23,695 --> 00:39:26,765
NOT THAT HAND,
YOUR CLEAN HAND.

909
00:39:26,832 --> 00:39:28,800
OH, THAT WAS
YOUR CLEAN HAND.

910
00:39:28,867 --> 00:39:31,937
HELP IF YOU'RE CLEAN.

911
00:39:32,003 --> 00:39:33,205
FLORA, COME ON.

912
00:39:33,272 --> 00:39:37,510
WE JARRED IT OPEN.

913
00:39:40,412 --> 00:39:43,215
GO AHEAD, BEAVE.

914
00:39:43,282 --> 00:39:47,953
IT'S THE SAME SET
WE WERE ON BEFORE.

915
00:39:57,463 --> 00:40:02,200
IT'S THE PHANTOM
OF THE OPERA.

916
00:40:04,503 --> 00:40:06,605
- OUCH!
- THIS MUST BE THE ROOM
BENEATH THE PYRAMID.

917
00:40:06,672 --> 00:40:11,810
- GOOD
- YES, BUT I KNOW IT ISN'T
THE TEMPLE.

918
00:40:11,877 --> 00:40:15,513
- LOOK WHAT I FOUND,
COME HERE.
- A LAUNDRY CHUTE.

919
00:40:15,580 --> 00:40:16,548
WHAT IS IT?

920
00:40:16,615 --> 00:40:18,217
IT LOOKS LIKE A WELL.

921
00:40:18,250 --> 00:40:19,452
WELL, I THINK IT'S
AN AIR SHAFT,

922
00:40:19,518 --> 00:40:21,420
BUT UNDOUBTEDLY
IT WILL LEAD US SOMEWHERE.

923
00:40:21,487 --> 00:40:22,655
PROBABLY TO THE TEMPLE.

924
00:40:22,722 --> 00:40:24,123
MAYBE THE AIR.

925
00:40:24,190 --> 00:40:26,192
WELL, THEN, WHAT
ARE WE WAITING FOR?

926
00:40:26,258 --> 00:40:27,760
NO DOUBT IT WILL
ADVANCE THE PLOT.

927
00:40:27,827 --> 00:40:29,728
- COME ON.
- THIN AS IT IS.

928
00:40:29,795 --> 00:40:30,863
WOMEN, CHILDREN FIRST,

929
00:40:30,930 --> 00:40:34,933
I'LL STAND HERE
AND HOLD THE FLASHLIGHT.

930
00:40:35,000 --> 00:40:38,003
REMARKABLE, IT WAS
THE NEIGHBOR'S BASEMENT.

931
00:40:38,070 --> 00:40:40,338
ONCE AGAIN, I CAN USE
THEIR VHS

932
00:40:40,405 --> 00:40:41,940
WITHOUT THEM KNOWING.

933
00:40:48,580 --> 00:40:52,417
WE SHOVED EVERYBODY
THROUGH THE LITTLE HOLE.

934
00:41:01,760 --> 00:41:05,030
[ALMADA]
AFTER DESCENDING SEVERAL
FLIGHTS OF STAIRS,

935
00:41:05,097 --> 00:41:07,633
WE SUDDENLY ENCOUNTERED
THE HAIR-RAISING FACE

936
00:41:07,700 --> 00:41:10,235
OF THE GOD DE CAPLA COPA.

937
00:41:10,302 --> 00:41:12,370
WE HAD REACHED
THE LOWER TEMPLE,

938
00:41:12,437 --> 00:41:14,973
AND THE AZTEC TOMB
THAT FLORA HAD MENTIONED.

939
00:41:15,040 --> 00:41:18,177
AND THE LIGHTING
WAS GOOD.

940
00:41:18,243 --> 00:41:20,745
YOU COULD SHOOT
A SCENE HERE.

941
00:41:20,812 --> 00:41:23,048
♪♪

942
00:41:25,383 --> 00:41:27,452
LIGHTS, PLEASE.

943
00:41:27,520 --> 00:41:29,522
THERE WE CAME ACROSS
THE SKELETON

944
00:41:29,588 --> 00:41:31,590
OF WHAT HAD ONCE
BEEN XOCHITL.

945
00:41:31,657 --> 00:41:34,025
- LOOKS LIKE CHICKEN WINGS.
- SOLID GOLD BREASTPLATE.

946
00:41:34,092 --> 00:41:35,260
XOCHITL.

947
00:41:35,327 --> 00:41:36,328
THIS IS HORRIBLE
TO THINK

948
00:41:36,395 --> 00:41:39,432
I WAS SHE.

949
00:41:39,498 --> 00:41:44,737
BUT YOU'RE YOU NOW.

950
00:41:44,803 --> 00:41:46,905
YOU KNOW, WE'RE THE FIRST
PERSONS TO BREAK IN HERE.

951
00:41:46,972 --> 00:41:48,640
THE OTHER PEOPLE
USED THE DOOR.

952
00:41:48,707 --> 00:41:51,543
IT'S A WORLD THAT
SLUMBERED ALL THESE YEARS.

953
00:41:51,610 --> 00:41:55,713
AND BEGINS TO
AWAKEN NOW.

954
00:41:55,780 --> 00:41:57,883
WE FOUND WHAT
WE WANTED SO BADLY.

955
00:41:57,950 --> 00:41:59,050
THE SUMP PUMP.

956
00:41:59,083 --> 00:42:00,018
NO, EDWARD.

957
00:42:00,085 --> 00:42:01,087
DON'T DO IT.

958
00:42:01,153 --> 00:42:03,988
[ALL]
DO IT, EDWARD, DO IT!

959
00:42:04,055 --> 00:42:06,225
♪♪

960
00:42:09,193 --> 00:42:11,830
THERE'S A TOOTSIE POP
STILL IN HIS MOUTH.

961
00:42:11,897 --> 00:42:15,000
- IT'S KOJAK.
- IT REALLY LASTS A LONG TIME.

962
00:42:15,067 --> 00:42:18,037
THE HEAD SHOULD
REALLY SCREW RIGHT OFF.

963
00:42:18,103 --> 00:42:20,907
THIS'LL LOOK SWELL
IN MY OFFICE.

964
00:42:30,048 --> 00:42:32,150
NOW AT LAST I'LL BE ABLE
TO DEMONSTRATE THIS

965
00:42:32,250 --> 00:42:33,685
TO MY COLLEAGUES.

966
00:42:33,752 --> 00:42:35,120
AND PROVE MY THEORY.

967
00:42:35,187 --> 00:42:37,422
IT'S SIMPLY AMAZING.

968
00:42:37,488 --> 00:42:38,923
SIMPLY.

969
00:42:38,990 --> 00:42:41,293
JUST A FEUD AFTER I GOT
THE BREASTPLATE,

970
00:42:41,360 --> 00:42:43,495
I ASKED YOU ALL HERE,
INCLUDING DR. KRUPP

971
00:42:43,562 --> 00:42:45,597
- AS YOU'LL RECALL.
- CERTAINLY.

972
00:42:45,663 --> 00:42:47,132
I'D SAY THAT IT WAS
THE GREATEST EXPERIENCE

973
00:42:47,198 --> 00:42:48,133
- OF MY LIFE.
- AND MINE, TOO.

974
00:42:48,200 --> 00:42:49,468
ME, TOO.

975
00:42:49,535 --> 00:42:51,070
- YOU MUST ALSO RECALL THAT I
-- I'LL BUY INTO THAT.

976
00:42:51,137 --> 00:42:52,537
SAID THAT I'D STUDIED
THE BREASTPLATE AND THAT I

977
00:42:52,605 --> 00:42:53,805
- TRIED TO DECIPHER THE
HIEROGLYPHICS
- SVELDT

978
00:42:53,872 --> 00:42:55,173
AND SEE WHAT THEY MEANT.

979
00:42:55,240 --> 00:42:57,375
SINCE I KNEW THAT THE MESSAGE
WOULD TELL HOW TO FIND

980
00:42:57,442 --> 00:42:59,512
- THAT HIDDEN TREASURE.
- YES, BUT I REMEMBER

981
00:42:59,578 --> 00:43:01,780
YOUR TELLING THAT YOU
ALSO NEEDED THE BRACELET.

982
00:43:01,847 --> 00:43:03,315
EXACTLY, DOCTOR.

983
00:43:03,382 --> 00:43:05,017
ONE OBJECT COMPLIMENTED
THE OTHER.

984
00:43:05,050 --> 00:43:06,152
- THEY'RE AN ENSEMBLE.
- WITHOUT THE BRACELET,

985
00:43:06,218 --> 00:43:08,353
IT WAS SIMPLY IMPOSSIBLE
TO DECIPHER THE CODE.

986
00:43:08,420 --> 00:43:10,155
SO I DECIDED TO GO
BACK FOR IT,

987
00:43:10,222 --> 00:43:13,725
IN SPITE OF THE AZTEC CURSE
THAT SURROUNDED IT.

988
00:43:13,792 --> 00:43:16,462
HE WHO DEFILES A TOMB
OF THE AZTECS,

989
00:43:16,528 --> 00:43:18,297
AND FINDS THE SACRED PLATE,

990
00:43:18,363 --> 00:43:21,367
WILL RUN THE RISK
OF DEATH, AND HIS FAMILY

991
00:43:21,400 --> 00:43:22,868
AS WELL, UNTIL THE
BREASTPLATE IS REPLACED.

992
00:43:22,935 --> 00:43:26,072
- AND GET BIG BUCK TEETH.
- WHAT IS HE, ROD MCKUEN?

993
00:43:26,138 --> 00:43:28,540
LIGHTS.

994
00:43:28,607 --> 00:43:30,075
SO ONCE AGAIN
THE THREE OF US

995
00:43:30,142 --> 00:43:31,810
GOT TOGETHER AND
RETURNED TO THE TOMB.

996
00:43:31,877 --> 00:43:33,278
THIS TIME LOADED
OUT OF OUR MINDS.

997
00:43:33,345 --> 00:43:34,647
WHEN WE REACHED THERE
AND I WAS JUST ABOUT

998
00:43:34,713 --> 00:43:36,282
TO PICK UP THE BRACELET,

999
00:43:36,348 --> 00:43:37,917
MY FATHER-IN-LAW
STUMBLED ON SOMETHING

1000
00:43:37,983 --> 00:43:39,618
AND CALLED MY ATTENTION
TO IT.

1001
00:43:39,685 --> 00:43:41,220
- OW.
- LOOK HERE.

1002
00:43:41,287 --> 00:43:42,220
I STUMBLED ON SOMETHING.

1003
00:43:42,287 --> 00:43:43,255
IT'S MY FOOT.

1004
00:43:43,322 --> 00:43:45,723
IT'S ATTACHED TO
THE BOTTOM OF MY ANKLE.

1005
00:43:45,790 --> 00:43:50,062
BOY, WERE WE DRUNK.

1006
00:43:50,128 --> 00:43:52,430
IT'S AN AZTEC IUD.

1007
00:43:52,497 --> 00:43:55,033
LOOK THERE, DOESN'T THAT
GRAVE BELONG TO POPOCA?

1008
00:43:55,100 --> 00:43:57,168
YES, ACCORDING TO
THE LEGEND, IT DOES.

1009
00:43:57,235 --> 00:44:02,908
IN THAT CASE, WHERE
IS HE NOW?

1010
00:44:02,975 --> 00:44:05,277
[SHUFFLING]

1011
00:44:06,712 --> 00:44:10,748
IT WAS SCATMAN CROTHERS.

1012
00:44:10,848 --> 00:44:13,718
[SHUFFLING CONTINUES]

1013
00:44:24,397 --> 00:44:26,498
HEY, THIS ONE SAYS
"FLUSH TWICE

1014
00:44:26,565 --> 00:44:28,800
THE CAFETERIA'S
A LONG WAY OFF."

1015
00:44:28,867 --> 00:44:32,237
WHOA, WHAT'S THAT?

1016
00:44:32,303 --> 00:44:33,472
GUARD!

1017
00:44:33,538 --> 00:44:36,742
I THOUGHT YOU SAID
WE WERE THE FIRST ONES HERE.

1018
00:44:36,808 --> 00:44:40,278
HEY, ZIP 'EM UP, MAN,
SOMEONE'S COMING.

1019
00:44:40,345 --> 00:44:43,948
[ZIPPING SOUND]

1020
00:44:44,015 --> 00:44:49,320
♪ ME AND MY SHADOW ♪

1021
00:44:49,388 --> 00:44:51,257
AND THEN OUT OF THE DARKNESS,

1022
00:44:51,323 --> 00:44:54,527
APPEARED THE GHASTLY
AND TERRIFYING POPOCA.

1023
00:44:54,593 --> 00:44:57,495
THE AZTEC WARRIOR
HAD COME BACK TO LIFE.

1024
00:44:57,562 --> 00:44:59,398
COME BACK TO
LIFE TO RETRIEVE

1025
00:44:59,465 --> 00:45:01,633
THE OBJECTS THAT HAD BEEN
LEFT IN HIS CARE

1026
00:45:01,700 --> 00:45:05,037
FOR ETERNITY.

1027
00:45:05,103 --> 00:45:06,572
[SQUEALING NOISES]

1028
00:45:06,638 --> 00:45:10,708
PARROT BOY.

1029
00:45:10,775 --> 00:45:13,478
ICE, I'M MELTING MAN TO MAN.

1030
00:45:13,545 --> 00:45:14,480
[SNIFFLING]

1031
00:45:14,547 --> 00:45:17,348
MUMMY, AZTEC MUMMY.

1032
00:45:17,415 --> 00:45:19,383
[GROANING]

1033
00:45:19,452 --> 00:45:21,853
TURN THEM OFF AGAIN.

1034
00:45:21,920 --> 00:45:23,388
LIGHTS AGAIN.

1035
00:45:23,455 --> 00:45:24,457
[GROANS]

1036
00:45:24,523 --> 00:45:25,523
IT'S A FLOOR SHORE.

1037
00:45:25,590 --> 00:45:29,193
IT'S A LOVELY SINGING VOICE.

1038
00:45:29,260 --> 00:45:31,230
THIS GUY'S GOT A BIG
CAREER IN SHOWBIZ.

1039
00:45:31,297 --> 00:45:32,898
[GROANING]

1040
00:45:34,265 --> 00:45:35,333
[GRUNTS]

1041
00:45:35,400 --> 00:45:36,902
THAT REALLY HURT.

1042
00:45:36,968 --> 00:45:40,005
NOW JUGGLING'S NOT
IN HIS ROUTINE.

1043
00:45:40,072 --> 00:45:43,675
[MOANS]

1044
00:45:43,742 --> 00:45:45,710
- AH...
- PINACATE.

1045
00:45:45,777 --> 00:45:48,247
GUYS, HELP ME, HE'S
GIVING ME A SNUGGY.

1046
00:45:48,313 --> 00:45:49,948
HELP ME.

1047
00:45:50,015 --> 00:45:52,083
PULL, PULL ME, FAST.

1048
00:45:52,117 --> 00:45:54,085
[ALL GROANING]

1049
00:45:54,152 --> 00:45:56,688
[STRUGGLING NOISES]

1050
00:45:56,755 --> 00:46:00,392
THE TRIPLE WEDGEE
FROM A MUMMY.

1051
00:46:05,697 --> 00:46:07,032
- LIGHTS.
- TO BE PERFECTLY FRANK,

1052
00:46:07,098 --> 00:46:08,567
I THOUGHT MY TIME HAD COME.

1053
00:46:08,633 --> 00:46:10,868
IF IT HADN'T BEEN FOR
MY FRIENDS,

1054
00:46:10,935 --> 00:46:11,870
I'D BEEN TORN TO PIECES.

1055
00:46:11,937 --> 00:46:13,538
IT'S INCREDIBLE.

1056
00:46:13,605 --> 00:46:14,907
A MUMMY COMES BACK TO LIFE

1057
00:46:14,973 --> 00:46:17,108
AFTER HUNDREDS OF YEARS
IN A SUB BUNKER.

1058
00:46:17,175 --> 00:46:19,578
DR. DIAZ, YOU HAVE MY
WORD OF HONOR

1059
00:46:19,645 --> 00:46:22,480
THAT THE STORY I HAVE
BEEN TELLING IS THE TRUTH.

1060
00:46:22,547 --> 00:46:24,048
OKAY, MIXED WITH
A LITTLE FICTION.

1061
00:46:24,115 --> 00:46:26,318
OKAY, I'M LYING
MY BUTT OFF.

1062
00:46:26,385 --> 00:46:27,853
BECAUSE HE LOVED
YOUNG XOCHITL.

1063
00:46:27,920 --> 00:46:30,555
HIS CURSE WAS TO GUARD THE
PRICELESS BRACELET

1064
00:46:30,622 --> 00:46:32,657
AS WELL AS
THE GOLDEN BREASTPLATE.

1065
00:46:32,723 --> 00:46:34,727
TO DO SO FOR ALL ETERNITY.

1066
00:46:34,793 --> 00:46:36,795
OR A 100,000 MILES,
WHATEVER CAME FIRST.

1067
00:46:36,862 --> 00:46:39,363
HIS POOR SOUL WOULD
NEVER FIND REPOSE.

1068
00:46:39,430 --> 00:46:40,965
CONTINUE, EDWARD.

1069
00:46:41,032 --> 00:46:44,235
- WELL THE BAT ON MANY--
- DON'T PICK ME UP ON IT.

1070
00:46:44,302 --> 00:46:46,172
[GROANS]
LET'S GO, CROW.

1071
00:46:46,238 --> 00:46:47,538
- YOU NEED TO MOP IN HERE.
- RIGHT.

1072
00:46:47,605 --> 00:46:49,942
I THOUGHT THE WHOLE BUSINESS
HAD BEEN FORGOTTEN.

1073
00:46:50,008 --> 00:46:52,343
BUT I FOUND THAT
THE AZTEC CURSE

1074
00:46:52,410 --> 00:46:53,512
STILL FOLLOWED US.

1075
00:46:53,578 --> 00:46:56,282
ONE NIGHT, THE MUMMY CAME
TO THIS HOUSE

1076
00:46:56,348 --> 00:46:58,550
TO GET HIS TREASURE PIECES.

1077
00:46:58,583 --> 00:47:00,118
AND HE KIDNAPPED FLORA.

1078
00:47:00,185 --> 00:47:02,587
♪♪

1079
00:47:05,990 --> 00:47:08,693
OH, MAN, I DON'T THINK
I CAN HANDLE THE SOUND

1080
00:47:08,760 --> 00:47:10,462
OF THOSE DOGS
BARKING ANYMORE.

1081
00:47:10,528 --> 00:47:12,197
AT LEAST THE
THE THEATER'S SOUNDPROOF.

1082
00:47:12,263 --> 00:47:14,700
TOO BAD, THEY MIGHT DROWN
OUT THE SOUND

1083
00:47:14,767 --> 00:47:15,667
OF THAT BIG DOG
ON THE FILM.

1084
00:47:15,733 --> 00:47:17,668
[KNOCKING SOUNDS]

1085
00:47:17,735 --> 00:47:19,638
WHAT IS IT, TOM SERVO?

1086
00:47:19,705 --> 00:47:21,640
I THINK, YEAH, JOEL,

1087
00:47:21,707 --> 00:47:24,008
I THINK ONE OF THOSE
DEMON DOGS IS DOING

1088
00:47:24,075 --> 00:47:25,710
"A SHAVE AND A HAIRCUT"
KNOCK ON THE BACK DOOR.

1089
00:47:25,777 --> 00:47:26,712
WHAT?

1090
00:47:26,778 --> 00:47:27,845
WHAT IS IT, FELLA?

1091
00:47:27,913 --> 00:47:29,047
[WHIMPERING]

1092
00:47:29,113 --> 00:47:30,782
I THINK HE'S TRYING
TO TELL US SOMETHING.

1093
00:47:30,815 --> 00:47:32,017
[WHIMPERING]

1094
00:47:32,050 --> 00:47:34,753
DAD? HE'S TRAPPED?

1095
00:47:34,820 --> 00:47:36,455
UNDER A ROCK?

1096
00:47:36,522 --> 00:47:37,822
DOWN IN DEAD ROCK CANYON?

1097
00:47:37,890 --> 00:47:40,625
[MAN]
STOP PATRONIZING ME
AND OPEN THIS DOOR.

1098
00:47:40,692 --> 00:47:41,627
DON'T LET HIM IN.

1099
00:47:41,693 --> 00:47:43,128
HEY, COME ON IN HERE.

1100
00:47:43,195 --> 00:47:44,495
UP, UP, COME ON UP.

1101
00:47:44,563 --> 00:47:46,732
UH-OH, NOT ON THE FURNITURE,
THAT'S NOT GOOD.

1102
00:47:46,798 --> 00:47:49,500
I AM ENOCH, KING
AND CHARISMATIC LEADER

1103
00:47:49,568 --> 00:47:50,602
OF THE DOG PEOPLE,

1104
00:47:50,668 --> 00:47:51,937
- ARF-ARF.
- CUTE.

1105
00:47:52,003 --> 00:47:53,105
WE HAVE TRAVELLED
MANY PARTS

1106
00:47:53,172 --> 00:47:54,873
AS TO PRAY TO
THE GIANT BONE

1107
00:47:54,940 --> 00:47:57,542
AND JUST MAYBE
GET A TASTE.

1108
00:47:57,608 --> 00:47:58,943
GIANT DOG BONE?

1109
00:47:59,010 --> 00:48:00,312
YES, BUT WE DID NOT
KNOW THE BONE

1110
00:48:00,378 --> 00:48:02,013
WOULD BE INHABITED.

1111
00:48:02,080 --> 00:48:03,015
HM.

1112
00:48:03,082 --> 00:48:04,282
JOEL, I THINK THE BONE

1113
00:48:04,382 --> 00:48:06,183
THEY'RE TALKING ABOUT
IS OUR SHIP.

1114
00:48:06,252 --> 00:48:07,818
HEY, CAMBOT, PUT
THE SCHEMATIC DRAWING

1115
00:48:07,885 --> 00:48:10,622
OF THE SATELLITE LOVE,
THE 25-25, UP ON SCREEN,

1116
00:48:10,688 --> 00:48:13,558
I THINK IT'S UNDER
25-25 IN YOUR FILE.

1117
00:48:13,625 --> 00:48:15,193
[JOEL]
WOW, IT LOOKS EXACTLY

1118
00:48:15,260 --> 00:48:17,228
LIKE A GIANT DOG BONE.

1119
00:48:17,295 --> 00:48:18,230
NOT JUST ANY BONE,

1120
00:48:18,297 --> 00:48:19,965
BUT THE SACRED NYLON
CHEW TOY

1121
00:48:20,032 --> 00:48:22,167
WRITTEN OF BY THE
HOLY RUG WEATHER RAT,

1122
00:48:22,233 --> 00:48:24,603
RUG WEATHERMAN,
JOHN AMBRY.

1123
00:48:24,670 --> 00:48:25,970
OUR INTENTION WAS
TO BURY YOU ON

1124
00:48:26,037 --> 00:48:27,205
THE FAR SIDE OF THE MOON.

1125
00:48:27,272 --> 00:48:29,307
BUT NOW WE'LL HAVE TO
CHANGE OUR PLANS.

1126
00:48:29,373 --> 00:48:31,242
WOW, WELL, LISTEN
YOU GOT TO GET

1127
00:48:31,310 --> 00:48:32,710
YOUR FOLLOWERS OFF
OUR SHIP,

1128
00:48:32,777 --> 00:48:34,412
THERE'S SO MANY OF THEM
AND THEY'RE MULTIPLYING

1129
00:48:34,478 --> 00:48:35,680
AT SUCH AN
ALARMING RATE,

1130
00:48:35,747 --> 00:48:36,715
THAT WE'RE GOING
TO GO INTO

1131
00:48:36,782 --> 00:48:38,783
THE EARTH'S ATMOSPHERE
AND EXPLODE.

1132
00:48:38,817 --> 00:48:40,885
YEAH, AND THEN
YOU'LL BE HOT DOGS.

1133
00:48:40,952 --> 00:48:41,887
[BOTH GROWL]

1134
00:48:41,953 --> 00:48:43,322
HEY, COME ON, CROW,

1135
00:48:43,388 --> 00:48:44,957
- COME ON, HE'S OUR GUEST--
- NOT GOING TO BE A PROBLEM,

1136
00:48:45,023 --> 00:48:47,458
AT MY SIGNAL,
THE DOGS WILL LEAVE.

1137
00:48:47,525 --> 00:48:50,062
BUT THEY OBEY ME,
AND ONLY ME.

1138
00:48:50,128 --> 00:48:52,297
FIRST, LET US
EXCHANGE PLEASANTRIES.

1139
00:48:52,363 --> 00:48:53,965
THEN, WE WILL
DRINK TRANIA.

1140
00:48:54,032 --> 00:48:55,800
FROM A DISH ON
THE FLOOR, BOY?

1141
00:48:55,867 --> 00:48:58,037
- [BOTH GROWL]
- CROW, NOW STOP IT, LISTEN.

1142
00:48:58,103 --> 00:48:59,938
HE HASN'T EVEN MET
EVERYBODY,

1143
00:49:00,005 --> 00:49:02,540
WELL, EXCEPT FOR
TOM SERVO, RIGHT?

1144
00:49:02,607 --> 00:49:04,108
AH, THE ATTRACTIVE ONE.

1145
00:49:04,175 --> 00:49:05,510
HEY, WATCH IT, PAL,
YOU'RE LOOKING AT

1146
00:49:05,577 --> 00:49:08,280
100% PRIME CUT AMERICAN
ROBOTIC MALE.

1147
00:49:08,347 --> 00:49:09,613
AND I DON'T PARTY
WITH PUPPIES,

1148
00:49:09,682 --> 00:49:11,248
- I'M OUT OF HERE.
- OH.

1149
00:49:11,282 --> 00:49:12,483
WELL, MY NAME IS JOEL,

1150
00:49:12,550 --> 00:49:13,718
AND I'M FROM
THE PLANET EARTH.

1151
00:49:13,785 --> 00:49:16,488
WHERE I COME FROM,
DOGS ARE MAN'S BEST FRIEND.

1152
00:49:16,555 --> 00:49:17,655
YOU'RE KIDDING.

1153
00:49:17,722 --> 00:49:18,723
YEAH, IT'S TRUE.

1154
00:49:18,790 --> 00:49:21,058
AND YOU MET CROW
OVER HERE.

1155
00:49:21,125 --> 00:49:22,427
SHAKE, BOY, SHAKE.

1156
00:49:22,493 --> 00:49:24,495
- I DON'T LIKE THIS BIRD--
- HEY, SIT.

1157
00:49:24,562 --> 00:49:25,763
BUT NOW I'LL EXPLAIN

1158
00:49:25,830 --> 00:49:28,067
HOW TO RID YOUR SHIP
OF THE DOGS.

1159
00:49:28,133 --> 00:49:30,268
OH, WAIT A MINUTE,
YOU HAVEN'T MET GYPSY YET.

1160
00:49:30,335 --> 00:49:31,603
- THIS IS GYPSY.
- AH, AH, AH.

1161
00:49:31,670 --> 00:49:34,305
HEY, GYPSY, NO.

1162
00:49:34,372 --> 00:49:35,773
GYPSY, NO.

1163
00:49:35,840 --> 00:49:37,142
[GROWLING]

1164
00:49:37,208 --> 00:49:39,143
- COME ON, OH.
- HEY.

1165
00:49:39,210 --> 00:49:41,413
- OH, NO, WE'RE KIBBLE.
- WAY TO GO, GIRL.

1166
00:49:41,480 --> 00:49:43,182
[ALARM BUZZING]
MOVIE SIGN!

1167
00:49:43,248 --> 00:49:45,417
BACK ON.

1168
00:49:56,093 --> 00:50:02,200
- [ALMADA] HE TIED HER TO THE
SACRIFICIAL STONE,
- NOW, LET'S GO HOME.

1169
00:50:02,267 --> 00:50:04,135
♪ TIE A SLEEPING FLORA ♪

1170
00:50:04,202 --> 00:50:07,005
♪ ROUND THE ALTAR STONE ♪

1171
00:50:07,072 --> 00:50:08,740
- HEY.
- OBVIOUSLY, THE MUMMY INTENDED

1172
00:50:08,807 --> 00:50:11,008
TO MAKE HISTORY REPEAT ITSELF.

1173
00:50:11,075 --> 00:50:13,112
HE WAS GOING TO CUT OUT
FLORA'S HEART AND OFFER

1174
00:50:13,178 --> 00:50:15,147
IT TO THE GOD DE CAPLA COPA.

1175
00:50:15,213 --> 00:50:16,715
THE THREE OF US RUSHED
TO THE PYRAMID

1176
00:50:16,782 --> 00:50:18,817
TO TRY TO RESCUE FLORA.

1177
00:50:18,850 --> 00:50:20,552
AND WE STOOD TRANSFIXED
FOR A MOMENT

1178
00:50:20,618 --> 00:50:23,020
AT THE SCENE WE SAW.

1179
00:50:23,088 --> 00:50:25,157
THE MUMMY WAS STANDING
NEXT TO THE STONE.

1180
00:50:25,223 --> 00:50:28,127
HE WAS HOLDING A KNIFE
HIGH IN HIS RIGHT HAND.

1181
00:50:28,193 --> 00:50:29,728
I JUMPED TO THE FLOOR
AND LUCKILY WAS ABLE

1182
00:50:29,795 --> 00:50:32,163
TO HIT THE BLADE
WITH A BULLET.

1183
00:50:32,230 --> 00:50:34,800
DUH.

1184
00:50:34,867 --> 00:50:37,035
[ALMADA]
IT LUNGED AT ME AND
IT'S ENORMOUS HANDS

1185
00:50:37,102 --> 00:50:38,570
GOT HOLD OF MY THROAT.

1186
00:50:38,637 --> 00:50:40,972
LIFE WAS LEAVING ME
RAPIDLY WHEN FLORA'S

1187
00:50:41,038 --> 00:50:42,907
FATHER SUDDENLY HELD A CROSS
UP IN FRONT OF ITS FACE.

1188
00:50:42,973 --> 00:50:44,608
WHICH WAS ODD BECAUSE
HE WAS JEWISH.

1189
00:50:44,675 --> 00:50:48,680
... HOLD THE MUMMY AT BAY
WHILE WE FREED FLORA.

1190
00:50:48,747 --> 00:50:50,082
IN A FRENZY, WE UNTIED HER

1191
00:50:50,148 --> 00:50:51,583
AND GOT HER AWAY
FROM THE STONE.

1192
00:50:51,617 --> 00:50:52,883
THEN THE PROFESSOR ORDERED
US TO GET HER

1193
00:50:52,950 --> 00:50:54,152
OUT OF THE PYRAMID.

1194
00:50:54,218 --> 00:50:55,520
GET OUT OF THE PYRAMID.

1195
00:50:55,587 --> 00:50:56,688
HIS TONE WAS SO ADAMANT,

1196
00:50:56,755 --> 00:50:59,490
AND I WAS SO CONCERNED
FOR FLORA'S SAFETY

1197
00:50:59,557 --> 00:51:01,927
THAT WE OBEYED HIM BLINDLY.

1198
00:51:01,993 --> 00:51:03,462
AND WHEN WE GOT OUT,
I REALIZED THAT HE

1199
00:51:03,528 --> 00:51:04,728
HADN'T FOLLOWED US.

1200
00:51:04,797 --> 00:51:07,365
FLOYD'S OUT, THANK GOD.

1201
00:51:07,432 --> 00:51:10,002
OH, WHAT ABOUT OPIE.

1202
00:51:10,068 --> 00:51:11,102
IN THAT VERY INSTANT,

1203
00:51:11,168 --> 00:51:13,938
- A TREMENDOUS EXPLOSION.
- OOP, YES.

1204
00:51:14,005 --> 00:51:17,308
OH, EXPLOSION, YES.

1205
00:51:17,375 --> 00:51:19,210
♪♪

1206
00:51:20,745 --> 00:51:23,080
THE PROFESSOR HAD GIVEN
UP HIS LIFE

1207
00:51:23,148 --> 00:51:24,115
IN ORDER TO SAVE OURS.

1208
00:51:24,182 --> 00:51:25,250
AND HIS CAREER.

1209
00:51:25,283 --> 00:51:27,085
MUMMY HAD STAYED UNDER
TONS OF BOULDERS,

1210
00:51:27,152 --> 00:51:29,120
AND THE BAT HAD BEEN
SENT TO PRISON,

1211
00:51:29,187 --> 00:51:30,388
- THE BAT?
- OF COURSE WE THOUGHT
THE WHOLE BUSINESS

1212
00:51:30,455 --> 00:51:31,790
HAD COME TO AN END.

1213
00:51:31,857 --> 00:51:33,825
- BUT IT DIDN'T HAPPEN
THAT WAY
- WHO'S THE BAT?

1214
00:51:33,892 --> 00:51:36,127
THE BAT, WHO IS REALLY
THE INFAMOUS DR. KRUPP.

1215
00:51:36,193 --> 00:51:38,830
[ALL]
OH.

1216
00:51:38,897 --> 00:51:41,132
IN HIS MAD DETERMINATION
TO GET MY TREASURE,

1217
00:51:41,198 --> 00:51:43,135
HE KIDNAPPED MY DAUGHTER,

1218
00:51:43,202 --> 00:51:45,503
AND FLORA AND THEN
HYPNOTIZED HER.

1219
00:51:45,570 --> 00:51:47,205
DO TELL US THE REST,
MY FRIEND.

1220
00:51:47,272 --> 00:51:48,540
THEN WHAT HAPPENED?

1221
00:51:48,607 --> 00:51:51,777
IN THIS STATE, SHE TOOK
THE DOCTOR TO THE AZTEC TOMB.

1222
00:51:51,843 --> 00:51:53,512
HE IMMEDIATELY LOCATED
THE MUMMY,

1223
00:51:53,578 --> 00:51:55,447
TAKING THE BREASTPLATE
AND THE BRACELET.

1224
00:51:55,513 --> 00:51:57,915
WELL, KRUPP CALLED ME ON THE
PHONE NOT TOO MUCH LATER.

1225
00:51:57,948 --> 00:52:00,752
I WAS ORDERED TO GO THERE
AND DECIPHER THE HIEROGLYPHICS,

1226
00:52:00,818 --> 00:52:03,020
TO ENABLE THE DEMON
TO LOCATE THE TREASURE.

1227
00:52:03,087 --> 00:52:04,755
AND YOU AGREED?

1228
00:52:04,823 --> 00:52:06,658
CAN'T YOU SEE THAT I
HAD TO OBEY?

1229
00:52:06,725 --> 00:52:07,658
TO SAVE MY WIFE WHO
HAD BEEN KIDNAPPED

1230
00:52:07,725 --> 00:52:09,493
BY THE DOCTOR.

1231
00:52:09,560 --> 00:52:12,197
- AND MY LITTLE GIRL--
- AH, BUT THERE'S ANOTHER
THING YOU SHOULD KNOW.

1232
00:52:12,263 --> 00:52:15,033
HE NEEDED THE AZTEC TREASURE
FOR A SPOT ON HIS WALL
IN THE REC ROOM.

1233
00:52:15,100 --> 00:52:16,568
HE NEEDED THAT AZTEC
TREASURE TO WORK ON

1234
00:52:16,635 --> 00:52:17,868
AN EXPERIMENT.

1235
00:52:17,935 --> 00:52:21,305
HE ALSO SAID THE EXPERIMENT,
OF COURSE, WAS COSTLY.

1236
00:52:21,372 --> 00:52:23,242
NOW YOU KNOW HOW
I WAS FORCED TO DO IT.

1237
00:52:23,308 --> 00:52:25,243
I WENT TO KRUPP'S LABORATORY.

1238
00:52:25,310 --> 00:52:27,778
AND BEGAN TO DECIPHER
THE HIEROGLYPHICS.

1239
00:52:27,845 --> 00:52:29,380
TENS OF THOSE
CRIMINALS

1240
00:52:29,447 --> 00:52:31,415
LIVES WERE IN GRAVE DANGER.

1241
00:52:31,517 --> 00:52:33,485
OUR ONLY HOPE WAS
THE MUMMY,

1242
00:52:33,552 --> 00:52:36,387
GUIDED BY UNKNOWN FORCES,

1243
00:52:36,453 --> 00:52:38,923
WOULD BE ABLE TO FIND
DR. KRUPP'S HIDEOUT

1244
00:52:38,990 --> 00:52:40,792
JUST THE WAY HE HAD
FOUND MY HOUSE

1245
00:52:40,858 --> 00:52:42,160
ON A PREVIOUS OCCASION.

1246
00:52:42,227 --> 00:52:44,828
HE COULD CALL INFORMATION.

1247
00:52:44,897 --> 00:52:47,965
BUT THE MOMENT ARRIVED
WHEN I COULD STALL NO LONGER.

1248
00:52:48,032 --> 00:52:49,267
I FINISHED IT.

1249
00:52:49,333 --> 00:52:51,035
THAT'S FINE.

1250
00:52:51,102 --> 00:52:53,605
LET'S SEE HERE, "WE
THE PEOPLE OF..."

1251
00:52:53,672 --> 00:52:56,575
HEY, THIS'LL
NEVER WORK.

1252
00:52:56,642 --> 00:52:58,477
YOU KNOW WHAT TO DO
NOW, DON'T YOU BRUNO?

1253
00:52:58,543 --> 00:53:00,045
START A VICTORY GARDEN?

1254
00:53:00,112 --> 00:53:01,647
HAVE A BAKE SALE?

1255
00:53:01,713 --> 00:53:03,047
SUPPORT RADIO FREE EUROPE?

1256
00:53:03,113 --> 00:53:04,182
COLLECT SHINY THINGS?

1257
00:53:04,248 --> 00:53:05,950
BUY BONDS WHERE YOU
WORK OR BANK?

1258
00:53:06,017 --> 00:53:10,622
GET A GUN?

1259
00:53:10,688 --> 00:53:11,990
GET A GUN, THAT'S
A GOOD THING.

1260
00:53:12,057 --> 00:53:13,892
HE ALWAYS RESORTS
TO VIOLENCE.

1261
00:53:13,958 --> 00:53:17,195
JUST WHAT ARE YOU
GOING TO DO, MURDER US?

1262
00:53:17,262 --> 00:53:18,963
NO, I'M GOING TO KILL YOU.

1263
00:53:19,030 --> 00:53:22,533
YOU UNSCRUPULOUS PIG.

1264
00:53:22,600 --> 00:53:23,535
MUMMY'S HOME.

1265
00:53:23,602 --> 00:53:25,037
NOW YOU'RE GOING TO GET IT.

1266
00:53:25,103 --> 00:53:27,938
[GUNFIRE]

1267
00:53:28,005 --> 00:53:31,008
BULLETS BOUNCE RIGHT OFF.

1268
00:53:31,075 --> 00:53:33,010
OR GO RIGHT THROUGH.

1269
00:53:33,077 --> 00:53:35,180
DOESN'T REALLY HAVE IT.

1270
00:53:35,247 --> 00:53:37,982
YEAH, KEEP SHOOTING, BRUNO,
IT'S GOING TO WORK, REALLY.

1271
00:53:38,048 --> 00:53:43,822
AH!

1272
00:53:43,888 --> 00:53:45,757
- BEAUTIFUL.
- [SCREAMS]

1273
00:53:45,823 --> 00:53:48,058
OOPS.

1274
00:53:48,125 --> 00:53:49,527
RIGHT WHERE IT HURTS.

1275
00:53:49,593 --> 00:53:52,497
ON THE FLOOR.

1276
00:53:52,563 --> 00:53:54,198
[SCREAMS]

1277
00:53:54,265 --> 00:54:00,105
HE'S WEARING A
SMOKING JACKET, YOU GUYS.

1278
00:54:00,172 --> 00:54:02,040
I'M OUT.

1279
00:54:02,107 --> 00:54:03,842
- WHOA.
- THERE'S SOME FURNITURE
WE MISSED.

1280
00:54:03,908 --> 00:54:06,612
[SCREAMS]

1281
00:54:06,678 --> 00:54:08,245
[GROANS]

1282
00:54:08,313 --> 00:54:12,683
I'VE SAVED THE BEAVER.

1283
00:54:12,750 --> 00:54:15,220
I'VE SAVED FLORA.

1284
00:54:24,362 --> 00:54:25,397
LOOK OUT.

1285
00:54:25,463 --> 00:54:26,932
C'MON, BEAVE, LET'S
GO CHECK THIS OUT.

1286
00:54:33,003 --> 00:54:34,238
THEY SEEM STUNNED.

1287
00:54:34,305 --> 00:54:37,008
NO!
DOCTOR, HELP ME!

1288
00:54:37,075 --> 00:54:40,812
CAN'T YOU HEAR?
NO... HELP ME!

1289
00:54:40,878 --> 00:54:43,882
YEAH, YOU'RE FIRST ON THE LIST
OF PEOPLE TO HELP.

1290
00:54:43,948 --> 00:54:46,583
PLEASE, HELP ME!
HELP ME!

1291
00:54:46,652 --> 00:54:48,252
[ALMADA]
THE MUMMY REALIZED
WHO THE CRIMINALS WERE

1292
00:54:48,320 --> 00:54:49,487
AND SETTLED ACCOUNTS WITH THEM.

1293
00:54:49,553 --> 00:54:51,522
THEN, WHEN HE SAW
THE DOCTOR TRYING TO ESCAPE,

1294
00:54:51,588 --> 00:54:52,923
HE PICKED HIM UP
LIKE A RAG DOLL

1295
00:54:52,990 --> 00:54:54,458
AND THREW HIM INTO
A PIT FULL OF RATTLERS.

1296
00:54:54,525 --> 00:54:56,895
EVERY GOOD LABORATORY HAS
A PIT FULL OF RATTLERS.

1297
00:54:56,962 --> 00:54:58,228
AAH!

1298
00:54:58,295 --> 00:55:01,767
- WOULD THAT BE A BAD TOUCH?
- YEAH, I THINK SO.

1299
00:55:01,833 --> 00:55:06,437
WE WERE TIRED, BUT IT WAS
A GOOD KIND OF TIRED.

1300
00:55:06,503 --> 00:55:08,138
MUMMY'S DONE CLEANING.

1301
00:55:08,205 --> 00:55:09,773
[ALMADA]
AFTERWARDS, WITH THE BREASTPLATE
AND THE BRACELET

1302
00:55:09,840 --> 00:55:12,343
IN HIS HAND,
HE SLOWLY SHUFFLED AWAY

1303
00:55:12,410 --> 00:55:16,080
INTO THE DARKNESS
AND SOON WAS LOST FROM SIGHT.

1304
00:55:16,147 --> 00:55:18,182
I'LL NEVER FORGET
THE STRONG AFFECTION

1305
00:55:18,282 --> 00:55:19,583
I HAD FOR FLORA'S FATHER.

1306
00:55:19,650 --> 00:55:21,787
SUCH A KIND MAN
WHOSE INTELLIGENT ADVICE

1307
00:55:21,853 --> 00:55:23,020
BROUGHT ABOUT OUR SALVATION.

1308
00:55:23,087 --> 00:55:26,257
AND THE MUMMY WENT
BACK TO THE PYRAMID?

1309
00:55:26,323 --> 00:55:27,792
NO, HE HAD TWO NIGHTS
AT THE COPA.

1310
00:55:27,858 --> 00:55:29,260
NO, THEY DESTROYED
HIS TEMPLE.

1311
00:55:29,327 --> 00:55:30,862
HE HAD NO REASON
TO GO THERE.

1312
00:55:30,928 --> 00:55:33,632
IN THAT CASE, CAN'T YOU TELL US
WHERE HE IS?

1313
00:55:33,698 --> 00:55:36,267
- PERMIT ME TO CONTINUE.
- HEY, IT'S YOUR MOVIE.

1314
00:55:36,333 --> 00:55:38,135
ALL THESE TRAGIC HAPPENINGS
COULDN'T GO UNATTENDED,

1315
00:55:38,202 --> 00:55:42,140
SO I WENT TO THE POLICE.

1316
00:55:42,207 --> 00:55:43,708
THEN I RETURNED
TO KRUPP'S HIDEOUT,

1317
00:55:43,775 --> 00:55:45,110
ACCOMPANIED BY THE CHIEF
OF POLICE,

1318
00:55:45,177 --> 00:55:46,610
AND A COUPLE OF HIS MEN.

1319
00:55:46,677 --> 00:55:48,513
YOU CAN IMAGINE OUR SURPRISE
WHEN WE DISCOVERED

1320
00:55:48,580 --> 00:55:50,415
THE PLACE WAS COMPLETELY EMPTY.

1321
00:55:50,482 --> 00:55:53,117
EXCEPT FOR ALL
THIS GARBAGE.

1322
00:55:57,522 --> 00:56:00,092
THE LABORATORY HAD BEEN
DISMANTLED,

1323
00:56:00,158 --> 00:56:01,425
AND THE BODIES
OF THE CRIMINALS

1324
00:56:01,492 --> 00:56:03,795
THAT THE MUMMY HAD KILLED
HAD ALSO DISAPPEARED.

1325
00:56:03,862 --> 00:56:08,833
THEY WERE DISMANTLED AS WELL.

1326
00:56:08,900 --> 00:56:11,737
CONTINUING OUR SEARCH,
WE HURRIED TO THE SNAKE PIT.

1327
00:56:11,803 --> 00:56:13,605
I WAS AWESTRUCK
WHEN I REALIZED

1328
00:56:13,672 --> 00:56:16,173
THE THE BODY OF DR. KRUPP
WAS NO LONGER DOWN THERE.

1329
00:56:16,240 --> 00:56:17,975
- AW...
- THEN, TO OUR HORROR,

1330
00:56:18,042 --> 00:56:19,610
WE DISCOVERED THAT THERE WAS
A SMALL DOOR

1331
00:56:19,677 --> 00:56:21,747
IN THE BACK WALL OF THE PIT,
THROUGH WHICH

1332
00:56:21,813 --> 00:56:23,615
THE DOCTOR COULD
HAVE ESCAPED.

1333
00:56:23,682 --> 00:56:25,250
HE WAS SUCH A LARGE MAN,
HOW COULD HE?

1334
00:56:25,283 --> 00:56:27,385
OBVIOUSLY, THE DOCTOR
HAD ESCAPED.

1335
00:56:27,452 --> 00:56:29,387
AND STRANGELY, I DON'T THINK
HE'D BEEN BITTEN.

1336
00:56:29,453 --> 00:56:30,955
THE MAN'S RUNNING LOOSE.

1337
00:56:31,022 --> 00:56:32,923
SO THAT WOULD MEAN THAT
THE DOCTOR KEPT TRYING

1338
00:56:32,990 --> 00:56:34,292
TO COME BY THOSE ARTICLES

1339
00:56:34,358 --> 00:56:36,060
SO THAT HE COULD LOCATE
THE TREASURE.

1340
00:56:36,127 --> 00:56:38,162
YOU'RE RIGHT, MY FRIEND,
HE DID JUST THAT.

1341
00:56:38,228 --> 00:56:40,398
HE BEGAN TO BOTHER US
A COUPLE OF WEEKS LATER.

1342
00:56:40,465 --> 00:56:42,967
IT HAPPENED QUITE SUDDENLY,
YOU SEE.

1343
00:56:43,033 --> 00:56:45,103
ONE DARK NIGHT...

1344
00:56:45,170 --> 00:56:49,607
THIS IS THE HOUSE.

1345
00:56:49,673 --> 00:56:51,375
DO YOU REALLY THINK
THIS PLAN OF YOURS

1346
00:56:51,442 --> 00:56:53,845
IS GONNA WORK, DOC?

1347
00:56:53,912 --> 00:56:56,313
YOU'LL SEE.
NOW I WANT YOU TO BE QUIET.

1348
00:56:56,380 --> 00:56:59,050
KEEP STILL, AND DON'T MAKE
THE SLIGHTEST NOISE.

1349
00:56:59,117 --> 00:57:02,453
PEAS AND CARROTS,
PEAS AND CARROTS...

1350
00:57:02,520 --> 00:57:04,822
I WISH THAT YOU COME
TO MY SIDE.

1351
00:57:04,888 --> 00:57:07,958
♪♪

1352
00:57:08,025 --> 00:57:10,862
FLORA, I COMMAND YOU
TO COME TO ME.

1353
00:57:10,928 --> 00:57:12,497
I THINK HE'S USING
TELEFLORA.

1354
00:57:12,563 --> 00:57:18,703
FLORA, I COMMAND YOU
TO COME TO ME.

1355
00:57:19,503 --> 00:57:21,372
USE THE DOORBELL.

1356
00:57:21,438 --> 00:57:24,108
DOORKNOB.

1357
00:57:24,142 --> 00:57:27,612
FLORA, ARE YOU LISTENING?
COME HERE TO ME.

1358
00:57:27,678 --> 00:57:30,113
IS HE SPEAKING INTO
HIS GLOVE?

1359
00:57:30,182 --> 00:57:32,617
MUST BE A PARTY LINE.

1360
00:57:37,255 --> 00:57:40,558
976-FLORA?

1361
00:57:45,397 --> 00:57:48,198
- STAND UP.
- WEAR SOMETHING SHEER.

1362
00:57:48,265 --> 00:57:49,600
PUT ON A HOUSECOAT.

1363
00:57:49,667 --> 00:57:52,937
FLORA, DO NOT TRY
TO FIGHT IT, COME HERE.

1364
00:57:55,873 --> 00:58:00,077
NOTICE YOU NEVER ACTUALLY
SEE HER GET DRESSED.

1365
00:58:00,143 --> 00:58:04,282
NOW, OPEN THE DOOR THIS TIME.
DON'T WALK THROUGH IT.

1366
00:58:04,348 --> 00:58:06,885
- GOOD GIRL.
- WELL DONE.

1367
00:58:06,952 --> 00:58:09,453
THAT'LL SAVE
SOME REPAIR

1368
00:58:09,520 --> 00:58:12,023
HEY, CLOSE IT ALL THE WAY.
WERE YOU BORN IN A BARN?

1369
00:58:12,090 --> 00:58:14,458
FLORA, DO NOT TRY
TO FIGHT IT, COME HERE!

1370
00:58:18,062 --> 00:58:21,098
STEP, STEP, STEP, KICK.

1371
00:58:21,165 --> 00:58:25,703
STEP, KICK.

1372
00:58:25,770 --> 00:58:30,675
RIGHT, LEFT, RIGHT, LEFT.

1373
00:58:30,742 --> 00:58:34,112
OKAY, IT'S ALL FLAT
FROM HERE, FLORA.

1374
00:58:34,178 --> 00:58:35,713
OH.

1375
00:58:35,780 --> 00:58:39,583
- SHE'S NOT FALLING FOR IT.
- NO.

1376
00:58:39,650 --> 00:58:43,120
SHE'S NO PUSHOVER

1377
00:58:43,187 --> 00:58:48,325
LOUD CLOCK...
AND KETTLE DRUM.

1378
00:58:50,328 --> 00:58:55,165
FLORA, ARE YOU LISTENING?
I COMMAND YOU TO COME TO ME.

1379
00:58:55,233 --> 00:58:58,737
I'M COMING, I'M COMING.

1380
00:59:01,072 --> 00:59:05,277
FLORA, YOU ARE TO DO
AS I COMMAND-- COME HERE.

1381
00:59:05,343 --> 00:59:07,912
DIGGING FOR GOLD,
BRUNO?

1382
00:59:12,950 --> 00:59:15,287
OKAY, BRUNO, WHEN SHE
PASSES IN FRONT OF THE CAR,

1383
00:59:15,353 --> 00:59:21,625
HONK REALLY LOUD.
[IMITATING CAR HORN HONKING]

1384
00:59:21,692 --> 00:59:24,028
LOVE ME AND MY
DEFORMED FRIEND.

1385
00:59:24,095 --> 00:59:25,963
YOU CAN HEAR THE WAVES
THAT ARE BEING SENT OUT

1386
00:59:26,030 --> 00:59:27,098
BY THAT MUMMY, CAN YOU NOT?

1387
00:59:27,165 --> 00:59:28,365
AND THE GUY IN THE CAR.

1388
00:59:28,432 --> 00:59:30,067
I KNOW WELL THAT YOU ARE ABLE
TO LEAD US TO HIM

1389
00:59:30,133 --> 00:59:31,835
YES, I CAN.

1390
00:59:31,902 --> 00:59:33,705
THEN TELL US,
WHERE IS POPOCA?

1391
00:59:33,772 --> 00:59:35,707
THE BEER BARREL POPOCA?

1392
00:59:35,773 --> 00:59:37,608
IN THE ANCIENT CEMETERY.

1393
00:59:37,675 --> 00:59:40,312
COME WITH ME.

1394
00:59:44,315 --> 00:59:47,452
IS THE ANCIENT CEMETERY
DENOMINATIONAL?

1395
00:59:51,288 --> 00:59:53,457
MEANWHILE, IN THE ANCIENT
CEMETERY,

1396
00:59:53,523 --> 00:59:54,825
THEY WERE LOOKING
FOR THE MUMMY.

1397
00:59:54,892 --> 00:59:57,962
BUT FIRST, LET'S KICK OVER
SOME GRAVE STONES, HEE HEE HEE.

1398
00:59:58,028 --> 00:59:59,697
YOU KNOW, THAT WOULD MAKE
ANOTHER EXCELLENT

1399
00:59:59,763 --> 01:00:03,400
MINIATURE GOLF COURSE,
LIKE THE OTHER MOVIE.

1400
01:00:03,467 --> 01:00:06,903
EACH HOLE WOULD BE DEADLY.

1401
01:00:06,972 --> 01:00:09,907
[CHUCKLES]
THAT LAST STEP IS A DOOZY.

1402
01:00:09,973 --> 01:00:11,875
LOW OVERHEAD.

1403
01:00:11,942 --> 01:00:14,812
BUT GRAVE CONSEQUENCES.

1404
01:00:14,878 --> 01:00:16,613
- YIKES.
- SORRY.

1405
01:00:16,680 --> 01:00:19,117
- I'LL SHUT YOU OFF.
- DON'T DO IT.

1406
01:00:19,183 --> 01:00:22,920
- COME ON, BRUNO, KEEP UP.
AND STOP PICKING YOUR NOSE.

1407
01:00:22,987 --> 01:00:24,355
LOOK, PETER GRAVES!

1408
01:00:24,422 --> 01:00:26,890
[LAUGHS]

1409
01:00:26,957 --> 01:00:28,693
WHO'S BURIED
IN PETER'S GRAVE?

1410
01:00:28,760 --> 01:00:31,362
JAMES ARNESS.

1411
01:00:36,233 --> 01:00:38,602
WHAT ARE YOU DOING HERE?
ANSWER ME!

1412
01:00:38,670 --> 01:00:40,338
WHAT ARE YOU DOING HERE?

1413
01:00:40,405 --> 01:00:42,540
WE'RE HITTING PEOPLE.

1414
01:00:42,607 --> 01:00:44,075
COME NOW, FLORA.

1415
01:00:44,142 --> 01:00:46,210
MUST HAVE BEEN
A DISPOSABLE CHARACTER.

1416
01:00:46,277 --> 01:00:48,913
COME ON, WE MUST HURRY.

1417
01:00:52,550 --> 01:00:55,353
SHUFFLE, SHUFFLE.

1418
01:00:55,420 --> 01:00:56,787
STEP, STEP, STEP.

1419
01:00:56,853 --> 01:00:59,557
NO NEED TO HURRY,
THE PLOT WILL SUPPORT

1420
01:00:59,623 --> 01:01:02,127
ALL OF THIS
FRIKKIN' SLOWNESS.

1421
01:01:02,193 --> 01:01:05,630
[ALL)
LIONS AND TIGERS AND BEARS,
OH, MY.

1422
01:01:05,697 --> 01:01:09,167
LIONS AND TIGERS AND BEARS,
OH, MY.

1423
01:01:09,233 --> 01:01:12,070
LIONS AND TIGERS AND BEARS,
OH, MY.

1424
01:01:24,715 --> 01:01:26,350
SEE, THIS'LL BE
OUR NEW HOME.

1425
01:01:26,417 --> 01:01:29,187
YOU SEE, THERE'LL BE YOU
AND ME, AND BRUNO MAKES THREE.

1426
01:01:29,253 --> 01:01:31,922
AND MY LITTLE
DEFORMED FRIEND.

1427
01:01:37,928 --> 01:01:41,265
- IS THIS THE PLACE?
- YES.

1428
01:01:43,835 --> 01:01:46,870
KNOCK TWICE.
TELL 'EM SAM SENT YOU.

1429
01:01:46,937 --> 01:01:48,372
[CHAIN RATTLES]

1430
01:01:48,438 --> 01:01:51,442
SHH!
YOU TRYING TO WAKE THE DEAD?

1431
01:01:54,112 --> 01:02:00,017
IT'S OPEN.

1432
01:02:00,083 --> 01:02:03,087
AT LEAST CARRY HER
ACROSS THE THRESHOLD.

1433
01:02:03,153 --> 01:02:06,357
SURE AM GLAD FLORA WORE
HER PHOSPHORESCENT DRESS.

1434
01:02:06,423 --> 01:02:09,527
DON'T YOU KNOW THAT'S
THE CURSE OF THE MUMMY, CROW?

1435
01:02:09,593 --> 01:02:11,195
- CURSE OF THE MUMMY?
- YEAH.

1436
01:02:11,262 --> 01:02:14,932
IT'S BEING-- NOT BEING ABLE
TO DRESS WHEN YOU ROB A GRAVE.

1437
01:02:14,998 --> 01:02:17,768
I HATE THAT.
I'VE HAD THIS DREAM BEFORE.

1438
01:02:17,835 --> 01:02:20,838
I'M IN MY PAJAMAS,
I'M IN A CRYPT...

1439
01:02:20,905 --> 01:02:24,275
I'M BEING CHASED
BY A BIG BANANA.

1440
01:02:24,342 --> 01:02:27,545
OH, MAN, HIS FACE LOOKS LIKE
COTTAGE CHEESE.

1441
01:02:27,612 --> 01:02:29,880
IT LOOKS LIKE A DIET PLATE.

1442
01:02:29,947 --> 01:02:32,117
YOU DEVIL.

1443
01:02:32,183 --> 01:02:35,052
YOU STINKING DEVIL!

1444
01:02:35,118 --> 01:02:40,958
HOW I'D LIKE TO CHOP
YOUR ROTTEN FLESH TO PIECES!

1445
01:02:41,025 --> 01:02:43,060
BRUNO, STOP LETTING HATE
RUN YOUR LIFE.

1446
01:02:43,127 --> 01:02:44,162
IT WOULD CERTAINLY
BE GREAT TO DO SO...

1447
01:02:44,228 --> 01:02:46,430
WHO'S HE HIDING
HIS FACE FROM?

1448
01:02:46,497 --> 01:02:47,732
HIS AGENT, I THINK.

1449
01:02:47,798 --> 01:02:50,200
HE'S GOING TO MAKE
MY EXPERIMENT,

1450
01:02:50,267 --> 01:02:52,002
SO WE MUST WAIT.

1451
01:02:52,068 --> 01:02:56,107
WAIT?
WHEN I GOT SO MUCH HATE

1452
01:02:56,173 --> 01:02:57,975
EATING DOWN DEEP INSIDE
OF MY GUTS?

1453
01:02:58,042 --> 01:03:00,077
YOU AIN'T GOT NO IDEA
WHAT IT IS TO LIVE LIKE THIS!

1454
01:03:00,143 --> 01:03:03,113
OH, MAN, LOOK, THEY TAPED
PLASTIC GOOP TO HIS FACE.

1455
01:03:03,180 --> 01:03:07,918
JUST BECAUSE
OF THAT STINKING MONSTER.

1456
01:03:07,985 --> 01:03:10,453
YOUR FACE COULD HOLD
A THREE-DAY RAIN, BRUNO.

1457
01:03:10,522 --> 01:03:12,623
I PROMISE YOU THAT
HE'LL BE DESTROYED.

1458
01:03:12,690 --> 01:03:15,392
[BRUNO CRYING]

1459
01:03:15,458 --> 01:03:20,130
BUT GIVE ME TIME.
JUST A LITTLE TIME!

1460
01:03:20,197 --> 01:03:23,767
IT WON'T BE TOO LONG BEFORE
YOU CAN HAVE YOUR REVENGE.

1461
01:03:23,835 --> 01:03:26,970
LET ME GET THE FIRST
PLATE FIRST-- THE BRACELET!

1462
01:03:27,037 --> 01:03:29,407
LOOKS LIKE IT
SCABBED OVER NICELY.

1463
01:03:29,473 --> 01:03:32,643
... AND YET SO FAR,
BECAUSE I CAN'T TOUCH THEM.

1464
01:03:32,710 --> 01:03:36,713
IT IS TOO DANGEROUS
TO DO IT.

1465
01:03:36,780 --> 01:03:41,918
HE'LL WAKE UP IN AN INSTANT
AND DESTROY US.

1466
01:03:41,985 --> 01:03:43,888
SOUNDS OKAY TO ME.

1467
01:03:43,955 --> 01:03:47,958
BUT I'LL GET HIM BACK,
I SWEAR IT,

1468
01:03:48,025 --> 01:03:50,928
NO MATTER HOW LONG
IT TAKES ME.

1469
01:03:50,995 --> 01:03:53,965
YOU DEVILISH MUMMY!

1470
01:03:54,032 --> 01:03:56,800
HE LOOKS LIKE MR. FRENCH.

1471
01:03:56,867 --> 01:04:00,170
LINE.

1472
01:04:00,237 --> 01:04:04,075
COME ON, WE BETTER GO NOW.

1473
01:04:04,142 --> 01:04:06,710
WE'LL BE NEEDING
A LOT OF TIME

1474
01:04:06,777 --> 01:04:10,513
IF THE PLAN I HAVE IS
GOING TO WORK OUT.

1475
01:04:10,582 --> 01:04:12,783
ANYTHING YOU SAY.

1476
01:04:12,850 --> 01:04:15,853
CAN AND WILL BE
USED AGAINST YOU.

1477
01:04:15,920 --> 01:04:19,723
COME, FLORA.

1478
01:04:24,428 --> 01:04:27,598
WOW, A LOT OF GOOD ACTING
IN THAT SCENE.

1479
01:04:27,665 --> 01:04:30,000
JOEL, WHAT WAS THE POINT
OF THIS LITTLE, UH--

1480
01:04:30,067 --> 01:04:31,302
LITTLE SCENE HERE.

1481
01:04:31,368 --> 01:04:32,803
- I DON'T KNOW.

1482
01:04:32,870 --> 01:04:34,705
I THINK THEY WERE JUST
STAKING OUT A LOCATION

1483
01:04:34,772 --> 01:04:36,040
TO COME AND SHOOT HERE LATER

1484
01:04:36,107 --> 01:04:37,842
WHEN THEY HAD SOMETHING
MEANINGFUL TO DO.

1485
01:04:37,908 --> 01:04:39,343
- OH.

1486
01:04:39,410 --> 01:04:41,045
YOU KNOW,
I REALLY DID YOU, HON.

1487
01:04:41,112 --> 01:04:43,680
CAN I CALL YOU AGAIN?

1488
01:04:43,747 --> 01:04:47,083
THINK HE'LL KISS HER NOW OR WAIT
TILL HE GETS TO THE DOOR?

1489
01:04:47,150 --> 01:04:49,387
IT'S ALWAYS A BETTER POLICY
TO KISS ON THE STEPS.

1490
01:04:49,453 --> 01:04:51,822
- AH.
- OR BY THE CAR.

1491
01:04:51,888 --> 01:04:54,358
- OR UNDER THE CAR.
- OR ON THE MOUTH.

1492
01:04:54,425 --> 01:04:57,762
YOU'LL GO UP TO YOUR ROOM,
THEN YOU'LL GO TO SLEEP.

1493
01:04:57,828 --> 01:05:01,498
AND WHEN YOU AWAKEN,
YOU'LL ACT QUITE NORMALLY.

1494
01:05:01,565 --> 01:05:04,102
YOU WILL BE REFRESHED
AND INVIGORATED.

1495
01:05:04,168 --> 01:05:06,203
DO YOU UNDERSTAND?

1496
01:05:06,270 --> 01:05:09,907
YOU WON'T RECALL A THING.

1497
01:05:09,973 --> 01:05:12,042
NOW, WALK.

1498
01:05:12,108 --> 01:05:13,810
- LIKE AN EGYPTIAN.
- GO ON.

1499
01:05:13,877 --> 01:05:15,780
BRUNO, DO THAT THINK
WITH THE CAR HORN AGAIN.

1500
01:05:15,847 --> 01:05:16,780
I LOVE THAT BIT.

1501
01:05:16,847 --> 01:05:19,250
[IMITATING HORN HONKING]

1502
01:05:19,283 --> 01:05:22,287
HEH, SHE FALLS FOR IT
EVERY TIME.

1503
01:05:35,232 --> 01:05:39,870
♪♪

1504
01:05:42,038 --> 01:05:47,110
WE'VE DONE THIS SCENE
BEFORE, ONLY AT NIGHT.

1505
01:05:47,177 --> 01:05:49,813
- ♪ I FEEL PRETTY ♪
- WELL, GOOD MORNING.

1506
01:05:49,880 --> 01:05:51,582
- ♪ OH SO PRETTY ♪
- GOOD MORNING, SWEETHEART.

1507
01:05:51,648 --> 01:05:53,383
YOU MUST HAVE BEEN
VERY TIRED.

1508
01:05:53,450 --> 01:05:55,618
WE WERE WAITING DOWN HERE
TO HAVE BREAKFAST WITH YOU.

1509
01:05:55,687 --> 01:05:56,853
WE COULD BOTH EAT A HORSE.

1510
01:05:56,920 --> 01:05:58,588
BACON AND EGGS,
LIKE ALWAYS?

1511
01:05:58,655 --> 01:06:00,157
NOTHING FOR ME, MARIA.

1512
01:06:00,223 --> 01:06:02,560
I HAVE A TERRIBLE
HEADACHE, DEAR.

1513
01:06:02,627 --> 01:06:05,628
WHAT'S THAT YOU'VE GOT
ON YOUR GOWN?

1514
01:06:05,697 --> 01:06:06,863
IT'S ALL DIRTY.

1515
01:06:06,930 --> 01:06:08,232
LOOKS LIKE DEAD,
DRIED FLESH.

1516
01:06:08,298 --> 01:06:10,735
YOU'VE BEEN DOWN
IN THE CELLAR.

1517
01:06:10,802 --> 01:06:13,503
NO, SWEETHEART.
I DON'T KNOW.

1518
01:06:13,570 --> 01:06:16,007
BUT LOOK AT YOUR SLIPPERS,
THEY'RE ALL MUDDY.

1519
01:06:16,073 --> 01:06:17,342
AND YOU PITTED OUT
YOUR GOWN.

1520
01:06:17,408 --> 01:06:18,475
COME ON, WHAT HAVE YOU
BEEN UP TO?

1521
01:06:18,542 --> 01:06:20,377
JUST CAVORTING WITH MUMMIES
ALL NIGHT.

1522
01:06:20,443 --> 01:06:22,178
IT'S FUNNY, THESE ARE NEW
SLIPPERS, I JUST BOUGHT THEM.

1523
01:06:22,245 --> 01:06:24,015
- AND NOW THEY'RE DIRTY.
- AND SO ARE YOU!

1524
01:06:24,082 --> 01:06:26,183
- I THINK YOU WENT OUT
LAST NIGHT.

1525
01:06:26,250 --> 01:06:28,518
NO.
AFTER I TOOK MY BATH,

1526
01:06:28,585 --> 01:06:30,320
I WENT TO BED
BECAUSE I WAS TIRED.

1527
01:06:30,387 --> 01:06:32,723
YES, BUT YOU GOT UP
LATER ON, DIDN'T YOU?

1528
01:06:32,790 --> 01:06:35,158
- I DID? NO.
- SHH! WHO'S THE KID?

1529
01:06:35,225 --> 01:06:37,995
YES, BECAUSE I WOKE UP
A COUPLE OF TIMES,

1530
01:06:38,062 --> 01:06:39,730
AND YOU WERE NOT
IN BED.

1531
01:06:39,797 --> 01:06:41,965
NO, YOU'RE MISTAKEN, DARLING.

1532
01:06:42,032 --> 01:06:44,135
- I ASSURE YOU...
- GET THAT KID OUT OF THERE.

1533
01:06:44,202 --> 01:06:46,303
YOU WENT OUT LAST NIGHT,
HONEST, MOM.

1534
01:06:46,370 --> 01:06:48,805
COME ON, LET'S FORGET THE WHOLE
THING FOR NOW, ALL RIGHT?

1535
01:06:48,872 --> 01:06:50,273
FLOYD LOOKS CONFUSED.

1536
01:06:50,340 --> 01:06:52,910
REMEMBER, SHE HAS
A GREAT IMAGINATION.

1537
01:06:52,977 --> 01:06:54,778
TELL ME, HAS YOUR
HEADACHE PASSED?

1538
01:06:54,845 --> 01:06:57,682
NO. I'M GOING TO
LIE DOWN FOR A WHILE.

1539
01:06:57,748 --> 01:06:58,982
EXCUSE ME, PLEASE.

1540
01:06:59,083 --> 01:07:01,052
AND I DON'T LIKE THE SMELL
OF THIS CONVERSATION.

1541
01:07:01,118 --> 01:07:02,787
YOU CHILDREN GO ON
AND HAVE YOUR BREAKFAST.

1542
01:07:02,853 --> 01:07:04,020
YES, DADDY.

1543
01:07:04,088 --> 01:07:08,325
COME ON, PINACATE,
I WANT TO TALK TO YOU.

1544
01:07:08,392 --> 01:07:10,762
OH, BOY,
WHAT A LIAR YOU ARE!

1545
01:07:10,828 --> 01:07:13,430
YOU SHUT YOUR BIG MOUTH.
YOU'RE THE LIAR!

1546
01:07:13,497 --> 01:07:15,432
YOU CAN'T EVEN ACT YOURSELF
OUT OF A PAPER BAG.

1547
01:07:15,498 --> 01:07:18,468
YOU'LL NEVER WORK
IN CORAL GABLES AGAIN!

1548
01:07:18,535 --> 01:07:20,470
PINACATE,
I'M VERY WORRIED.

1549
01:07:20,537 --> 01:07:22,573
THIS ATTITUDE THAT
WE'VE OBSERVED IN FLORA

1550
01:07:22,640 --> 01:07:23,873
IS NOT NORMAL.

1551
01:07:23,940 --> 01:07:25,275
WHAT'S MORE, I'M AFRAID
THAT THE BAT

1552
01:07:25,342 --> 01:07:26,843
HAS SOMETHING
TO DO WITH THIS.

1553
01:07:26,910 --> 01:07:28,612
MAYBE SHE SHOULD CHOKE UP
ON IT A LITTLE BIT.

1554
01:07:28,678 --> 01:07:29,647
THEN DO YOU REALLY THINK
THAT CHILD WAS TELLING

1555
01:07:29,713 --> 01:07:30,782
THE TRUTH ABOUT IT,

1556
01:07:30,848 --> 01:07:32,617
AND THAT HER MOTHER GOT UP
AND WENT OUT?

1557
01:07:32,683 --> 01:07:35,252
YES, IT'S QUITE PROBABLE.

1558
01:07:35,318 --> 01:07:38,822
BUT FLORA INSISTED SHE DIDN'T
LEAVE HER BED FOR A SECOND.

1559
01:07:38,888 --> 01:07:41,192
BECAUSE SHE CAN'T
RECALL ANYTHING.

1560
01:07:41,258 --> 01:07:44,828
WHEN SHE GOT UP LAST NIGHT,
SHE WAS SLEEPING.

1561
01:07:44,895 --> 01:07:46,563
I DON'T UNDERSTAND IT.

1562
01:07:46,630 --> 01:07:48,365
IT SEEMS IMPOSSIBLE.

1563
01:07:48,432 --> 01:07:50,400
I'LL TELL YOU WHAT I THINK.

1564
01:07:50,467 --> 01:07:54,105
SHE WAS HYPNOTIZED AND COULD BE
UNDER POSTHYPNOTIC SUGGESTION.

1565
01:07:54,172 --> 01:07:56,173
SO IT SEEMS TO ME
THAT THE BAT CONTROLS HER

1566
01:07:56,240 --> 01:07:57,542
FROM A DISTANCE.

1567
01:07:57,608 --> 01:07:59,310
- WITH SONAR.
- IT'S LOGICAL.

1568
01:07:59,377 --> 01:08:00,643
- WHAT A SLEUTH.

1569
01:08:00,710 --> 01:08:03,880
THIS STRANGE ATTITUDE
IN FLORA INDICATED

1570
01:08:03,947 --> 01:08:06,283
THAT UNSCRUPULOUS VILLAIN KRUPP
MADE HER LEAVE THE HOUSE

1571
01:08:06,350 --> 01:08:07,585
DURING THE NIGHT.

1572
01:08:07,652 --> 01:08:08,952
BUT WHERE DID THEY GO TO?

1573
01:08:09,018 --> 01:08:10,888
CAN'T YOU GUESS
WHAT HE'S TRYING TO DO?

1574
01:08:10,955 --> 01:08:12,188
NO.

1575
01:08:12,255 --> 01:08:14,892
YOU CERTAINLY KNOW WHAT HE'S
AFTER-- THE BREASTPLATE

1576
01:08:14,958 --> 01:08:16,693
AND BESIDES THAT,
THE BRACELET.

1577
01:08:16,760 --> 01:08:18,362
AND HE SNAPPY COCO CHANEL
PANTS SUIT.

1578
01:08:18,428 --> 01:08:19,830
THEN YOU THINK THAT
SHE WAS MADE

1579
01:08:19,897 --> 01:08:21,665
TO GO ALONG WITH KRUPP,
AND HE WANTED HER

1580
01:08:21,732 --> 01:08:23,100
TO GUIDE HIM
TO FIND THE MUMMY.

1581
01:08:23,167 --> 01:08:25,702
EXACTLY, AND YOU AND I
MUST GO THERE.

1582
01:08:25,768 --> 01:08:27,203
I'M GOING TO FIND OUT
IF THAT SCOUNDREL

1583
01:08:27,270 --> 01:08:28,405
STOLE THOSE OBJECTS.

1584
01:08:28,472 --> 01:08:30,273
BUT THAT'LL BE DIFFICULT.

1585
01:08:30,340 --> 01:08:32,342
YOU CAN'T INVESTIGATE
WITHOUT ANY CLUES.

1586
01:08:32,408 --> 01:08:35,078
FLOYD'S A GREAT BARBER, BUT NOT
A VERY GOOD DETECTIVE.

1587
01:08:35,145 --> 01:08:36,213
YES.

1588
01:08:36,280 --> 01:08:37,815
NEITHER OF THEM ARE
VERY GOOD ACTORS.

1589
01:08:37,848 --> 01:08:39,517
WELL, THAT GOES
WITHOUT SAYING.

1590
01:08:39,583 --> 01:08:43,987
HE SMOKES--
HE SMOKES VERY WELL, THOUGH.

1591
01:08:44,053 --> 01:08:46,757
IF LOVING YOU IS WRONG,
I DON'T WANT TO BE RIGHT.

1592
01:08:46,823 --> 01:08:49,025
SUPPOSE WE TOOK HER SLIPPERS
TO THE LABORATORY

1593
01:08:49,092 --> 01:08:50,760
TO HAVE THAT MUD ANALYZED.

1594
01:08:50,828 --> 01:08:53,163
THAT COULD HELP US
DON'T YOU THINK?

1595
01:08:53,230 --> 01:08:54,832
I CAN TELL YOU WHAT KIND
OF SLIPPERS THEY ARE.

1596
01:08:54,898 --> 01:08:57,333
YES, THAT MIGHT JUST BE
THE SOLUTION.

1597
01:08:57,400 --> 01:09:00,303
WE'LL TAKE THEM, BUT I DON'T
THINK SHE SHOULD FIND OUT.

1598
01:09:00,370 --> 01:09:01,872
WE'D BETTER DO IT ALL
IN SECRET.

1599
01:09:01,938 --> 01:09:03,140
- YEAH!
- COME ON.

1600
01:09:03,207 --> 01:09:04,375
SECRET!

1601
01:09:04,442 --> 01:09:07,177
WE'LL GET IN DISGUISE.
WE'LL BE WOMEN.

1602
01:09:07,243 --> 01:09:10,347
YES, NOW, I'M QUITE SURE.
IT'S EMBEDDED IN THE DIRT.

1603
01:09:10,413 --> 01:09:12,082
THEY'RE SLIPPERS.

1604
01:09:12,115 --> 01:09:13,550
OF COURSE, IT'S A SMALL
QUANTITY, DOCTOR,

1605
01:09:13,617 --> 01:09:14,752
BUT YOUR SUSPICIONS
ARE CORRECT--

1606
01:09:14,818 --> 01:09:17,153
THEY'RE PIECES OF MARBLE.

1607
01:09:17,220 --> 01:09:18,488
YOU'RE SURE IT'S MARBLE?

1608
01:09:18,555 --> 01:09:20,490
- MARBLE?
- CAN YOU IDENTIFY ITS SOURCE?

1609
01:09:20,557 --> 01:09:22,593
IS IT A SPECIAL KIND?
- NO, IT ISN'T.

1610
01:09:22,660 --> 01:09:23,927
BUT IT'S A FINE QUALITY.

1611
01:09:23,993 --> 01:09:25,695
- CLASSY.
- IT MIGHT BE A TARARE MARBLE.

1612
01:09:25,762 --> 01:09:27,230
- I CAN SAY THAT.
- MAYBE A...

1613
01:09:27,297 --> 01:09:31,535
IT'S USED IN THE CONSTRUCTION
OF MAUSOLEUMS, AS FAR AS I KNOW.

1614
01:09:31,602 --> 01:09:34,205
- THANK YOU.
- OH...

1615
01:09:34,272 --> 01:09:36,440
SHE WENT OUT LATE AT NIGHT
AND PLAYED MARBLES.

1616
01:09:36,507 --> 01:09:38,842
WHAT COULD IT MEAN?

1617
01:09:43,247 --> 01:09:44,782
MEANWHILE,
BACK AT THE OTHER SET...

1618
01:09:44,882 --> 01:09:49,920
FORTUNATELY,
IT WAS STILL LIT.

1619
01:09:49,987 --> 01:09:52,923
THIS IS THE LAST CEMETERY.
WE'VE SEEN ALL THE OTHERS.

1620
01:09:52,990 --> 01:09:54,458
IF WE DON'T FIND
ANYTHING HERE,

1621
01:09:54,525 --> 01:09:57,527
WE'D BETTER FORGET ABOUT IT.

1622
01:09:57,595 --> 01:09:59,297
- HELLO THERE
- GOOD EVENING

1623
01:09:59,363 --> 01:10:00,330
WELL-ACTED, FLOYD.

1624
01:10:00,397 --> 01:10:01,398
TELL ME, ARE YOU
THE WATCHMAN HERE?

1625
01:10:01,465 --> 01:10:03,400
YES, SIR.
ANYTHING I CAN DO FOR YOU?

1626
01:10:03,467 --> 01:10:05,903
WHY YES, WE'D LIKE TO
ASK YOU A FEW QUESTIONS.

1627
01:10:05,970 --> 01:10:07,972
WE'D LIKE TO KNOW IF YOU'VE
SEEN ANYTHING STRANGE

1628
01:10:08,038 --> 01:10:10,340
THE LAST FEW WEEKS,
OR MORE RECENTLY.

1629
01:10:10,407 --> 01:10:13,343
ANYTHING VERY SUSPICIOUS
IN OR AROUND THE CEMETERY,

1630
01:10:13,410 --> 01:10:14,945
PERTAINING TO ONE
OF THE GRAVES.

1631
01:10:15,012 --> 01:10:16,447
- JUST THE FILM CREW.
- ARE YOU FROM THE POLICE?

1632
01:10:16,513 --> 01:10:18,248
YES, THAT'S RIGHT,
MY FRIEND,

1633
01:10:18,348 --> 01:10:20,985
AND WE'RE AFTER A VERY
DANGEROUS CRIMINAL,

1634
01:10:21,052 --> 01:10:22,820
WHOM WE SUSPECT HAS BEEN
HIDING ONE

1635
01:10:22,887 --> 01:10:24,187
OF THE CEMETERIES
AROUND THE CITY.

1636
01:10:24,255 --> 01:10:26,990
WELL, THE FACT IS, SOMETHING
PRETTY DOGGONE CURIOUS

1637
01:10:27,057 --> 01:10:28,292
DID HAPPEN.

1638
01:10:28,358 --> 01:10:30,127
JUST TWO NIGHTS AGO,
I WAS SURPRISED

1639
01:10:30,193 --> 01:10:33,197
TO RUN INTO A YOUNG WOMAN HERE
WEARING A KIND OF WHITE ROBE.

1640
01:10:33,263 --> 01:10:34,632
SHE SEEMED TO BE ASLEEP,

1641
01:10:34,698 --> 01:10:36,900
AND TWO MEN ENTERED
THE GROUNDS WITH HER.

1642
01:10:36,967 --> 01:10:38,002
HE'S NOT GONNA
FLASH BACK, IS HE?

1643
01:10:38,068 --> 01:10:39,035
WHEN I ASKED THEM
WHO THEY WERE,

1644
01:10:39,102 --> 01:10:40,270
ONE OF THE GUYS SLUGGED ME,

1645
01:10:40,337 --> 01:10:41,538
AND THEY LEFT ME OUT COLD
HERE ON THE GROUND.

1646
01:10:41,605 --> 01:10:45,242
HOW DO YOU THINK I GOT
THIS SWELL HAT?

1647
01:10:45,308 --> 01:10:47,778
THEN WE'LL BE TAKING A LOOK
AROUND THE GROUNDS.

1648
01:10:47,845 --> 01:10:49,045
YOU CAN DO ANYTHING
YOU WANT.

1649
01:10:49,112 --> 01:10:51,215
- ANYTHING YOU WANT.
- YOU'RE THE POLICE.

1650
01:10:51,248 --> 01:10:54,250
DON'T TOUCH HIM, HE'S FILTHY.

1651
01:10:54,318 --> 01:10:55,685
YOU SEE, I WAS RIGHT.

1652
01:10:55,752 --> 01:10:57,353
AT LAST,
WE'RE ON THE TRAIL.

1653
01:10:57,420 --> 01:10:58,722
NOW THE TOUGH PART
HAS YET TO COME.

1654
01:10:58,788 --> 01:10:59,857
NO, YOU'RE ON MY FOOT.

1655
01:10:59,923 --> 01:11:00,857
'CAUSE WE'VE GOT TO
WALK AROUND

1656
01:11:00,923 --> 01:11:02,627
TILL WE FIND THE MUMMY.

1657
01:11:02,693 --> 01:11:04,628
LOOK, WE'D BETTER
SEPARATE NOW.

1658
01:11:04,695 --> 01:11:06,830
GO THAT WAY PINACATE.
I'LL GO OVER THERE.

1659
01:11:06,897 --> 01:11:10,500
- SEPARATE?
- BUT I LOVE YOU.

1660
01:11:10,567 --> 01:11:14,738
[A LA JERRY LEWIS]
OW, DEAN!

1661
01:11:14,805 --> 01:11:17,607
DON'T--
WOW--OW...

1662
01:11:17,675 --> 01:11:23,480
HEY, OH, DAD AND MUMMY
AND BRUNO!

1663
01:11:23,547 --> 01:11:26,583
♪♪

1664
01:11:26,650 --> 01:11:28,618
OH, VERY BAD.
OH!

1665
01:11:28,685 --> 01:11:32,055
OH, DINO?
OH, OH...

1666
01:11:32,122 --> 01:11:34,758
LIONS AND TIGERS AND OW!

1667
01:11:34,825 --> 01:11:38,062
[ALL IMITATING JERRY LEWIS,
OVERLAPPING DIALOGUE]

1668
01:11:41,798 --> 01:11:45,035
DINO?
HEY.

1669
01:11:45,102 --> 01:11:49,072
OH, OH, BEWARE,
ALL WHO ENTER, WHOA!

1670
01:11:49,138 --> 01:11:51,008
"M."
OH...

1671
01:12:04,220 --> 01:12:06,690
WHOA, DEAN?

1672
01:12:06,757 --> 01:12:09,258
DINO?
DINO?

1673
01:12:09,325 --> 01:12:12,328
WHERE ARE YOU?
WOW.

1674
01:12:12,395 --> 01:12:14,263
[A LA BING CROSBY]
JERRY, JERRY, WHERE ARE YA?

1675
01:12:14,330 --> 01:12:15,398
I CAN'T FIND YA.

1676
01:12:15,465 --> 01:12:16,600
COME ON, JERRY,
WHERE ARE YA?

1677
01:12:16,633 --> 01:12:19,370
COME ON, SAY SOMETHING
TO ME, BOY.

1678
01:12:21,405 --> 01:12:24,875
DEAN, OVER HERE!
OH, THERE YOU ARE.

1679
01:12:24,942 --> 01:12:27,010
QUIT HORSING AROUND,
WE GOT A MUMMY TO FIND.

1680
01:12:27,077 --> 01:12:29,380
EDWARD, EDWARD,
COME HERE.

1681
01:12:33,783 --> 01:12:35,652
WHAT HAPPENED?

1682
01:12:35,718 --> 01:12:38,055
- WE'VE GOTTA GET OUT OF HERE.
- I'M GETTING OUT OF HERE.

1683
01:12:38,122 --> 01:12:39,557
WOW...JOL...

1684
01:12:39,623 --> 01:12:41,658
I HOPE THERE'S DOGS
IN HERE.

1685
01:12:46,630 --> 01:12:49,098
COME ON!

1686
01:13:02,012 --> 01:13:04,247
I JUST DON'T SEE IT
AT ALL, GUYS.

1687
01:13:04,313 --> 01:13:05,648
COME ON, CROW,
I THINK IT'LL WORK.

1688
01:13:05,715 --> 01:13:07,852
YOU'RE THE ONLY ONE OF US
WHO EVEN LOOKS A LITTLE BIT

1689
01:13:07,918 --> 01:13:09,018
LIKE ENOCH DID.
[DOGS YAPPING IN BACKGROUND]

1690
01:13:09,085 --> 01:13:11,588
NO, MY BROW'S ALL DIFFERENT.

1691
01:13:11,655 --> 01:13:12,790
I'M-- I'M JUST-- NO.

1692
01:13:12,857 --> 01:13:14,458
OH, IT'S THERE.
I SEE IT.

1693
01:13:14,525 --> 01:13:16,760
JOEL, BE SURE TO
WIPE DOWN HIS NOSE.

1694
01:13:16,827 --> 01:13:19,228
BOY, IF I WERE A DEMON DOG,
I'D JUST BOW DOWN

1695
01:13:19,295 --> 01:13:20,597
AN KNEEL AND BOW TO YOU.

1696
01:13:20,663 --> 01:13:22,465
I'M ALREADY STARTING
TO MISS THAT OLD ENOCH.

1697
01:13:22,532 --> 01:13:24,233
YOU KNOW, I ALMOST CRIED
WHEN HE LEFT.

1698
01:13:24,300 --> 01:13:26,270
JUST LIKE WHEN
OLD YELLER GOT SHOT.

1699
01:13:26,337 --> 01:13:28,072
OH, CROW, COME ON,
IT'LL BE EASY.

1700
01:13:28,138 --> 01:13:30,040
YOU GO OUT THERE,
YOU SAY TO THE DEMON DOGS,

1701
01:13:30,107 --> 01:13:31,375
"COME ONE, EVERYBODY,
LET'S GO.

1702
01:13:31,442 --> 01:13:33,043
I'LL BE RIGHT BEHIND YOU."

1703
01:13:33,110 --> 01:13:34,177
YOU DUCK BACK IN.
IT'S EASY.

1704
01:13:34,243 --> 01:13:36,045
GREAT ADVICE COMING FROM
MR. FIREPLUG.

1705
01:13:36,113 --> 01:13:37,113
- HEY, WATCH IT, PAL.
- HEY...

1706
01:13:37,180 --> 01:13:38,848
HEY, TAKE IT EASY, YOU TWO,
LISTEN,

1707
01:13:38,915 --> 01:13:40,617
IF WORSE COMES TO WORST,
JUST TELL 'EM

1708
01:13:40,683 --> 01:13:43,387
THE SATELLITE OF LOVE IS
A GIANT CHICKEN BONE, OKAY?

1709
01:13:43,453 --> 01:13:45,622
YOU LOOK GREAT, NOW JUST GO
DO THE JOB, AND BE REGAL.

1710
01:13:45,688 --> 01:13:48,658
ALL RIGHT.
I LOOK LIKE CHARLIE MCCARTHY.

1711
01:13:48,725 --> 01:13:50,427
[DOGS YAPPING]
LET'S WATCH IT ON THE MONITOR.

1712
01:13:50,493 --> 01:13:52,762
[CROW]
ALL RIGHT, QUIET DOWN,
QUIET DOWN.

1713
01:13:52,830 --> 01:13:55,165
AHEM,
I AM ENOCH.

1714
01:13:55,232 --> 01:13:57,433
I AM YOUR LORD
AND CHARISMATIC LEADER.

1715
01:13:57,500 --> 01:13:59,703
REMEMBER?

1716
01:13:59,770 --> 01:14:01,037
AND, HEY, WHAT'S
THE LEASH LAW HERE?

1717
01:14:01,103 --> 01:14:02,205
- HEY!
- OH, HE'S GETTING IT.

1718
01:14:02,272 --> 01:14:06,610
HEY, HEY, CURB YOUR BUDDY
OVER THERE-- OH!

1719
01:14:06,677 --> 01:14:10,280
[BOTH GROANING]

1720
01:14:10,347 --> 01:14:11,382
[TOM LAUGHING]

1721
01:14:11,482 --> 01:14:13,183
KIND OF A WARM FEELING,
EH, CROW?

1722
01:14:13,250 --> 01:14:16,052
WELL, I THINK IT WENT
KINDA WELL, YOU KNOW?

1723
01:14:16,118 --> 01:14:18,555
THEY WERE EATING OUT
OF THE PALM OF MY HAND...

1724
01:14:18,622 --> 01:14:20,090
TILL I RAN OUT OF TREATS.

1725
01:14:20,157 --> 01:14:22,325
AND SPEAKING OF TREATS,
WE'LL BE RIGHT BACK.

1726
01:14:22,392 --> 01:14:26,963
♪♪

1727
01:14:29,332 --> 01:14:35,372
♪♪

1728
01:14:35,438 --> 01:14:38,908
THEY'RE IN THE CRYPT.

1729
01:14:38,975 --> 01:14:43,513
DEMON DOGS EVERYWHERE.

1730
01:14:43,580 --> 01:14:45,648
DUDE, IT'S SCARING ME.

1731
01:14:45,682 --> 01:14:47,483
YOU GOT ALL THAT STUFF
OFF YOU, CROW?

1732
01:14:47,550 --> 01:14:50,387
YES, I DID.

1733
01:14:50,453 --> 01:14:52,055
GREAT IDEA.

1734
01:14:52,122 --> 01:14:55,492
LOOK, THE BREASTPLATE
AND THE BRACELET.

1735
01:14:55,558 --> 01:14:57,427
THEY DIDN'T TAKE IT.

1736
01:14:57,493 --> 01:15:01,332
ALL THIS I'VE JUST TOLD YOU
OCCURRED FIVE YEARS AGO.

1737
01:15:01,398 --> 01:15:03,900
WE VISITED THE CRYPT
FROM TIME TO TIME

1738
01:15:03,967 --> 01:15:05,668
TO TAKE A LOOK
AT THE MUMMY,

1739
01:15:05,735 --> 01:15:08,172
WITH ITS BREASTPLATE
AND ITS BRACELET TOO.

1740
01:15:08,238 --> 01:15:09,740
AND THE SNAPPY
COCO CHANEL PANTS SUIT.

1741
01:15:09,807 --> 01:15:11,242
IS HE STILL AROUND?

1742
01:15:11,308 --> 01:15:13,410
YOU KNOW, HE DISAPPEARED
FROM SIGHT.

1743
01:15:13,477 --> 01:15:14,978
THEN, JUST A COUPLE
OF DAYS AGO,

1744
01:15:15,045 --> 01:15:17,080
WE READ AN ARTICLE
THAT IS VERY INTERESTING.

1745
01:15:17,147 --> 01:15:19,148
WE WERE PROFOUNDLY
SURPRISED BY IT.

1746
01:15:19,248 --> 01:15:21,318
ACCORDING THE THE ARTICLE,
A COUPLE OF NIGHTS BEFORE,

1747
01:15:21,385 --> 01:15:23,253
A CADAVER HAD BEEN ROBBED
FROM THE AMPHITHEATER.

1748
01:15:23,320 --> 01:15:24,520
ABRACADAVER?

1749
01:15:24,588 --> 01:15:27,090
AND THE INDIVIDUAL WHO DID IT
WAS THE BAT, OF COURSE.

1750
01:15:27,157 --> 01:15:30,260
YES. IN THE BEGINNING,
WE HAD SOME DOUBTS,

1751
01:15:30,327 --> 01:15:31,628
SINCE THE MAN
WHO HAD BEEN ATTACKED

1752
01:15:31,695 --> 01:15:33,963
COULDN'T OFFER US A DESCRIPTION
OF HIS ASSAILANTS.

1753
01:15:34,030 --> 01:15:37,067
BUT LATER ON,
OUR SUSPICIONS WERE CONFIRMED.

1754
01:15:37,133 --> 01:15:38,502
DON'T PLAY WITH THAT.

1755
01:15:38,568 --> 01:15:41,572
YESTERDAY THERE WAS A BURGLARY
IN THE RADIOLOGY INSTITUTE.

1756
01:15:41,638 --> 01:15:43,807
THE THIEVES TOOK A MACHINE
THAT USES RADIUM.

1757
01:15:43,873 --> 01:15:45,708
THEY ALSO STOLE A BRAIN
OUT OF A LABORATORY.

1758
01:15:45,775 --> 01:15:47,310
- ICK.
- EXCELLENT.

1759
01:15:47,377 --> 01:15:48,612
THIS TIME, THE POLICE
WERE ABLE

1760
01:15:48,678 --> 01:15:50,847
TO IDENTIFY THE CROOKS
AS THE BAT AND ALL HIS BAND.

1761
01:15:50,913 --> 01:15:53,283
WE'RE COVERING A PLOT HOLE
WITH ASPHALT HERE.

1762
01:15:53,350 --> 01:15:55,118
ARE THERE ANY
GOOD CLUES, DOCTOR?

1763
01:15:55,185 --> 01:15:59,455
LEAD IS THE ONLY METAL
CAPABLE OF RESISTING RADIATION.

1764
01:15:59,522 --> 01:16:01,090
LEAD MATERIAL
IN THIS CITY IS HANDLED

1765
01:16:01,157 --> 01:16:02,492
BY MANY WHOLESALERS.

1766
01:16:02,558 --> 01:16:06,397
AFTER VISITING THE FIRST
THREE OR FOUR...

1767
01:16:06,463 --> 01:16:07,730
THEY GOT TO THE RIGHT ONE.

1768
01:16:07,797 --> 01:16:09,365
- GOOD MORNING, SIR.
- GOOD MORNING.

1769
01:16:09,432 --> 01:16:10,467
WHAT CAN I DO
FOR YOU, GENTLEMEN?

1770
01:16:10,533 --> 01:16:11,968
WE'RE SORRY TO BE
A BOTHER TO YOU,

1771
01:16:12,035 --> 01:16:13,703
BUT IS IT JUST POSSIBLE
THAT LATELY

1772
01:16:13,770 --> 01:16:15,672
YOU SENT OUT A LARGE
SHIPMENT OF LEAD?

1773
01:16:15,738 --> 01:16:16,873
COULD YOU GIVE ME
THAT INFORMATION?

1774
01:16:16,940 --> 01:16:18,242
IN THE LAST TWO DAYS?

1775
01:16:18,308 --> 01:16:20,243
OR IT COULD BE A WEEK,
MORE OR LESS.

1776
01:16:20,310 --> 01:16:22,378
- LET ME CHECK.
- FIVE YEARS, MAYBE.

1777
01:16:22,445 --> 01:16:26,115
WE KEEP A RECORD
OF OUR SHIPMENTS IN THIS BOOK.

1778
01:16:26,182 --> 01:16:30,820
WHY, YES, WE SEND A LEAD BALLOON
TO THE WRITERS OF THIS FILM.

1779
01:16:30,887 --> 01:16:33,490
YES, HERE IT IS.
EXACTLY FIVE DAYS AGO

1780
01:16:33,557 --> 01:16:35,625
WE MADE DELIVERY
OF 20 PLATES OF LEAD SHIELDING,

1781
01:16:35,692 --> 01:16:39,428
FOUR INCHES IN WIDTH,
TO NUMBER 22 SHADE STREET.

1782
01:16:39,495 --> 01:16:41,398
TO A MAN CALLED, UH,
"THE BAT."

1783
01:16:41,465 --> 01:16:43,500
- MANY THANKS.
- YOU'RE WELCOME.

1784
01:16:43,567 --> 01:16:45,302
I CAN'T BELIEVE HE TOLD US.

1785
01:16:45,368 --> 01:16:47,637
WE WERE INVESTIGATING
FOR DAYS.

1786
01:16:47,703 --> 01:16:49,105
AT LAST WE GOT
THE ADDRESS.

1787
01:16:49,172 --> 01:16:50,673
I THINK THE BAT HAD MADE
HIS HIDEOUT THERE,

1788
01:16:50,740 --> 01:16:51,708
OR HIS LABORATORY.

1789
01:16:51,775 --> 01:16:53,143
OR HIS NEST.

1790
01:16:53,210 --> 01:16:54,610
WELL, I DON'T SEE WHY
THIS THIEVING DR. KRUPP

1791
01:16:54,678 --> 01:16:56,380
WOULD GO TO THE EFFORT
OF STEALING RADIUM,

1792
01:16:56,447 --> 01:16:59,382
A COMPLETE HUMAN BRAIN,
AN ALSO THE BODY OF SOME MAN.

1793
01:16:59,448 --> 01:17:00,483
HE'S NUTS.

1794
01:17:00,550 --> 01:17:01,918
DO YOU RECALL THAT THE BAT
ONCE TOLD FLORA

1795
01:17:01,985 --> 01:17:03,320
THAT HE WAS WORKING
ON A NEW EXPERIMENT?

1796
01:17:03,387 --> 01:17:04,487
MM-HMM.

1797
01:17:04,553 --> 01:17:06,390
I THINK THAT IS
THE EXPLANATION.

1798
01:17:06,457 --> 01:17:08,158
- OH...
- IT'S POSSIBLE.

1799
01:17:08,225 --> 01:17:10,393
BUT THERE'S NO DOUBT THAT
DR. KRUPP AND HIS CRIMINALS

1800
01:17:10,460 --> 01:17:11,662
ARE PLANNING
TO CAUSE TROUBLE.

1801
01:17:11,728 --> 01:17:14,865
THAT'S WHAT CRIMINALS
DO BEST.

1802
01:17:14,932 --> 01:17:17,133
NOW I'LL TELL YOU WHY I CALLED
YOU HERE TONIGHT, GENTLEMEN--

1803
01:17:17,200 --> 01:17:18,868
BECAUSE YOU BOTH
ARE SCIENTISTS...

1804
01:17:18,935 --> 01:17:21,638
AND WE LIKE BORING STUFF.

1805
01:17:21,705 --> 01:17:24,607
JUST IN CASE WE END UP
BEING MURDERED

1806
01:17:24,675 --> 01:17:26,977
YOU MEAN TO SAY YOU TWO
ARE THINKING OF GOING THERE

1807
01:17:27,043 --> 01:17:29,212
WITHOUT TAKING
THE POLICE ALONG?

1808
01:17:29,278 --> 01:17:31,648
- YES, BECAUSE, YOU SEE,
WE'RE STILL NOT SURE

1809
01:17:31,682 --> 01:17:34,217
THAT THAT'S
THE BAT'S LABORATORY.

1810
01:17:34,283 --> 01:17:36,285
AND THE POLICE STILL DON'T HAVE
MUCH FAITH IN US

1811
01:17:36,353 --> 01:17:38,122
BECAUSE OF WHAT HAPPENED
BEFORE.

1812
01:17:38,188 --> 01:17:40,190
THEY JUST NEED TO CHECK
FOR BAT DROPPINGS.

1813
01:17:40,257 --> 01:17:41,992
- FLORA...
- GUANO?

1814
01:17:42,058 --> 01:17:43,693
IN CASE WE'RE NOT
BACK HERE AT THE HOUSE

1815
01:17:43,760 --> 01:17:45,728
BY 3:00 IN THE MORNING,

1816
01:17:45,795 --> 01:17:48,632
I'M LEAVING IT UP TO YOU
TO CALL THE POLICE.

1817
01:17:48,698 --> 01:17:51,902
- EDWARD!
- SELL EVERYTHING.

1818
01:17:51,968 --> 01:17:54,070
- LET'S KISS.
- HEY, WATCH IT, WATCH IT!

1819
01:17:54,137 --> 01:17:57,273
- LIGHTS.
- LOOKS PAINFUL.

1820
01:17:57,340 --> 01:17:59,242
BETTY CROCKER
TEST KITCHENS.

1821
01:17:59,308 --> 01:18:02,012
LET'S SEE, ONE, TWO THREE.

1822
01:18:02,078 --> 01:18:04,047
OKAY, IT FORMS
THREE CREAMY LAYERS.

1823
01:18:04,113 --> 01:18:05,748
NO, WAIT, THREE LAYERS--

1824
01:18:05,815 --> 01:18:07,550
A CREAMY LAYER,
A GELATINOUS LAYER AND--

1825
01:18:07,617 --> 01:18:10,553
DAMN IT, I MUST FIND
THAT FORMULA!

1826
01:18:10,620 --> 01:18:13,557
♪♪

1827
01:18:13,623 --> 01:18:16,993
[LOW RUMBLING]

1828
01:18:17,060 --> 01:18:20,563
POP ROCKS SEEM TO ME
MOVING ALONG NICELY.

1829
01:18:24,500 --> 01:18:28,172
AND THOSE M&Ms ARE
ALMOST DONE.

1830
01:18:28,238 --> 01:18:32,408
OH, MY GOD, HE'S TORN APART
THE MICHELIN MAN.

1831
01:18:32,475 --> 01:18:36,278
BIF, BUDDY, IT'S US.
PULL YOURSELF TOGETHER.

1832
01:18:36,345 --> 01:18:39,817
OH, HOW HORRIBLE HE EVEN
SLASHED HIS SPARE.

1833
01:18:42,618 --> 01:18:43,987
FREEZE, YOU TWO!

1834
01:18:44,053 --> 01:18:47,490
THIS LOOKS LIKE IT WAS SHOT
WITH A SECURITY CAMERA.

1835
01:18:50,660 --> 01:18:54,630
- OH, IT'S CRATER FACE.
- DR. ALMADA.

1836
01:18:54,697 --> 01:18:58,202
WHAT A PLEASANT SURPRISE.

1837
01:18:58,268 --> 01:19:00,770
- BRUNO?
- NO, KITTY CARLISLE!

1838
01:19:00,837 --> 01:19:02,772
WHO DID YOU THINK IT IS?

1839
01:19:02,838 --> 01:19:06,175
A SOUVENIR OF THE MUMMY.

1840
01:19:06,242 --> 01:19:07,977
THE BOSS IS GONNA BE
VERY HAPPY

1841
01:19:08,043 --> 01:19:09,980
TO SAY HELLO
TO YOU TWO AGAIN.

1842
01:19:10,047 --> 01:19:13,983
COME ALONG.

1843
01:19:14,050 --> 01:19:15,552
THIS IS THE KIND OF FILM
YOU WON'T PUT ON PAUSE

1844
01:19:15,618 --> 01:19:16,620
WHEN YOU LEAVE THE ROOM.

1845
01:19:16,687 --> 01:19:18,988
[THUNDER]

1846
01:19:19,055 --> 01:19:23,393
IT ENCOURAGES YOU TO GO
TO GET A SANDWICH.

1847
01:19:23,460 --> 01:19:27,197
- BOSS.
- KINDA LIKE TV REPELLENT.

1848
01:19:27,263 --> 01:19:30,533
LOOK WHAT I FOUND
OUT IN FRONT.

1849
01:19:30,600 --> 01:19:33,170
DR. ALMADA
AND HIS SHADOW.

1850
01:19:33,237 --> 01:19:35,172
THIS IS A PLEASANT
SURPRISE, GENTLEMEN.

1851
01:19:35,238 --> 01:19:36,907
- AFTER SUCH A LONG TIME...
- I'M NOT HIS SHADOW.

1852
01:19:36,973 --> 01:19:40,377
... I COME FACT TO FACE
WITH SUCH GOOD FRIENDS.

1853
01:19:40,443 --> 01:19:42,145
EXACTLY WHERE DID YOU
FIND THEM?

1854
01:19:42,212 --> 01:19:45,448
OUT IN THE SHOP THERE,
LOOKING AROUND.

1855
01:19:45,482 --> 01:19:47,550
- I OFFER YOU
MY CONGRATULATIONS,

1856
01:19:47,617 --> 01:19:51,453
BECAUSE YOU ARE
MAGNIFICENT DETECTIVES.

1857
01:19:51,522 --> 01:19:53,157
DID ANYONE ELSE
COME WITH THEM?

1858
01:19:53,223 --> 01:19:54,657
NOBODY ELSE.

1859
01:19:54,723 --> 01:19:57,860
I SAW THEM WHEN THEY DREW UP
IN THE AUTOMOBILE, ALONE.

1860
01:19:57,927 --> 01:20:00,397
BRUNO, AREN'T YOU GOING
TO ATTEND OUR GUESTS

1861
01:20:00,463 --> 01:20:02,798
THEY WAY THEY DESERVE?

1862
01:20:02,865 --> 01:20:04,800
GO FETCH CHAIRS
FOR THE GENTLEMEN.

1863
01:20:04,868 --> 01:20:06,368
SURE, RIGHT AWAY.

1864
01:20:06,435 --> 01:20:10,407
ELECTRIC CHAIRS.

1865
01:20:10,473 --> 01:20:14,343
TELL ME, HOW'S YOUR BEAUTIFUL
AND CHARMING WIFE, DR. ALMADA?

1866
01:20:14,410 --> 01:20:15,978
I LEARNED ABOUT
YOUR MARRIAGE,

1867
01:20:16,045 --> 01:20:17,847
AND I ADMIT IT'S
A BIT LATE TO SAY IT,

1868
01:20:17,913 --> 01:20:19,782
BUT RECEIVE
MY CONGRATULATIONS.

1869
01:20:19,850 --> 01:20:22,252
AND TAKE THIS TOASTER
AND FONDU SET AS A GIFT.

1870
01:20:22,318 --> 01:20:23,587
HOW ARE YOU THESE DAYS?

1871
01:20:23,653 --> 01:20:25,988
ARE YOU STILL
THE CHAMPION OF RIGHT?

1872
01:20:26,055 --> 01:20:28,525
THERE'S NO DOUBT ABOUT IT,
AND I'M GLAD.

1873
01:20:28,592 --> 01:20:30,793
NO, I'M JUST A SHADOW,
JERK.

1874
01:20:30,860 --> 01:20:32,528
COME OVER HERE.

1875
01:20:32,595 --> 01:20:36,165
[THUNDER]

1876
01:20:36,232 --> 01:20:37,900
START THE MUSIC.

1877
01:20:37,967 --> 01:20:39,635
THEY'RE PLAYING
MUSICAL CHAIRS.

1878
01:20:39,702 --> 01:20:42,505
HOW HORRIBLE.

1879
01:20:42,572 --> 01:20:44,507
NEXT, THEY'LL BE PINNING
THE TAIL ON SOMEBODY.

1880
01:20:44,573 --> 01:20:45,942
[BOTH]
WHO WOULD HAVE THOUGHT

1881
01:20:46,008 --> 01:20:48,912
THAT YOU'D BE HERE
AT THE MOMENT TO WITNESS THIS?

1882
01:20:48,978 --> 01:20:50,180
BECAUSE YOU'RE ABOUT
TO SEE SOMETHING

1883
01:20:50,247 --> 01:20:52,815
THAT WILL ASTONISH YOU--
TRULY UNBELIEVABLE.

1884
01:20:52,882 --> 01:20:54,817
[LAUGHS]

1885
01:20:54,885 --> 01:20:56,418
WHEN YOU FEAST YOUR EYES
ON THIS,

1886
01:20:56,485 --> 01:20:58,888
I DON'T DOUBT THAT
YOU'LL BE AMAZED, DOCTOR.

1887
01:20:58,955 --> 01:21:01,023
AND YOU'LL BE THE FIRST
TO CONGRATULATE ME!

1888
01:21:01,090 --> 01:21:02,092
BET IT'S A ROBOT.

1889
01:21:02,158 --> 01:21:03,125
FRANKLY, I'M HAPPY
THAT YOU CAME HERE

1890
01:21:03,192 --> 01:21:05,128
TO VISIT US,
DR. ALMADA.

1891
01:21:05,195 --> 01:21:07,663
YOU'RE A MAN WHO IS
BASICALLY AN INTELLECTUAL,

1892
01:21:07,730 --> 01:21:10,033
AND THAT'S WHY YOU'LL
BE ABLE TO UNDERSTAND...

1893
01:21:10,100 --> 01:21:11,033
BUT YOU HURT INSIDE.

1894
01:21:11,100 --> 01:21:12,268
... THE GREATNESS
OF MY INVENTION.

1895
01:21:12,335 --> 01:21:13,837
YOU'RE BASICALLY AN OVEREATER.

1896
01:21:13,903 --> 01:21:15,838
I THINK YOU REMEMBER
THAT TIME WE MET.

1897
01:21:15,905 --> 01:21:17,707
SINCE THEN, I'VE WORKED
DAY AND NIGHT,

1898
01:21:17,773 --> 01:21:20,810
WITHOUT RESTING
FOR A MINUTE.

1899
01:21:20,877 --> 01:21:23,447
AND DURING ALL THAT
HECTIC TIME,

1900
01:21:23,513 --> 01:21:27,283
I EXPLORED POWERS
THAT NO ONE ELSE KNOWS.

1901
01:21:27,350 --> 01:21:30,587
ALL THOSE GREAT MYSTERIES,
THE VERY BASIS OF CREATION.

1902
01:21:30,653 --> 01:21:32,955
THEN THAT MEANS THAT
YOU DEFY ALL THE LIMITS

1903
01:21:33,022 --> 01:21:34,390
THAT WERE PUT DOWN
BY GOD.

1904
01:21:34,457 --> 01:21:35,658
EHH, MAYBE.

1905
01:21:35,725 --> 01:21:37,893
THERE ARE CERTAIN SECRETS
THAT WE COULD EXPLORE

1906
01:21:37,960 --> 01:21:39,628
AND DISCOVER RAPIDLY.

1907
01:21:39,695 --> 01:21:41,030
I'M JUST TOYING
WITH GOD'S LAWS.

1908
01:21:41,097 --> 01:21:42,032
AND THAT'S WHY
IT'S SUCH A SHAME

1909
01:21:42,098 --> 01:21:45,068
THAT FEAR IMPEDES US SO,
DR. ALMADA.

1910
01:21:45,135 --> 01:21:47,670
YOU'RE COMPLETELY MAD,
AND IGNORANT ALSO.

1911
01:21:47,737 --> 01:21:50,807
[ALL]
THANK YOU.

1912
01:21:50,873 --> 01:21:53,277
EVERY MAD SCIENTIST HAS
ONE OF THESE SPEECHES.

1913
01:21:53,343 --> 01:21:54,343
[THUNDER]

1914
01:21:54,410 --> 01:21:56,178
DON'T YOU RESPECT
RESEARCH AT ALL?

1915
01:21:56,245 --> 01:21:58,848
DON'T YOU WANT TO LEAR TO KNOW
WHY A BODY FUNCTIONS?

1916
01:21:58,948 --> 01:22:03,185
I DO, AND AT LAST
I FOUND THE CAUSE.

1917
01:22:03,252 --> 01:22:05,122
TAKE A LOOK AT THIS HEART
THAT'S BEATING.

1918
01:22:05,188 --> 01:22:06,455
IT LIVES!

1919
01:22:06,522 --> 01:22:08,658
IT LIVES AND PULSATES
BECAUSE I GAVE IT LIFE,

1920
01:22:08,725 --> 01:22:09,892
AND IF I CAN GIVE LIFE...

1921
01:22:09,960 --> 01:22:11,628
DOESN'T HAVE VERY GOOD
RHYTHM, THOUGH.

1922
01:22:11,695 --> 01:22:12,928
... WHY CAN'T I GIVE IT
TO THE BODIES

1923
01:22:12,995 --> 01:22:14,730
THAT ARE DAMNED TO DEATH
AND DECAY?

1924
01:22:14,797 --> 01:22:17,600
AND WHY CAN'T YOU GIVE IT
TO THE SCRIPT?

1925
01:22:17,667 --> 01:22:20,670
NO ONE CAN POSSIBLY IMAGINE
HOW I WORKED

1926
01:22:20,737 --> 01:22:22,638
WHEN I DUG IN THE MUD
WITH THESE HANDS

1927
01:22:22,705 --> 01:22:24,073
AND ENTERED TOMBS.

1928
01:22:24,140 --> 01:22:26,977
I TORTURED MANY ANIMALS
WITH PLEASURE

1929
01:22:27,043 --> 01:22:28,778
TO FIND THE ANSWERS...

1930
01:22:28,845 --> 01:22:32,715
REMEMBER THE UNFORTUNATE
PUSH ME/PULL YOU.

1931
01:22:32,815 --> 01:22:34,850
YOU'RE INSANE, DO YOU KNOW?

1932
01:22:34,917 --> 01:22:36,585
[TOM]
YES!

1933
01:22:36,653 --> 01:22:39,188
I DECIDE TO CREATE A MAN.

1934
01:22:39,255 --> 01:22:42,258
A BREATHING BODY--
A REAL MAN!

1935
01:22:42,325 --> 01:22:44,593
AND I HAVE MADE
THAT DREAM COME TRUE.

1936
01:22:44,660 --> 01:22:47,763
THERE YOU HAVE THE GREATEST...
[ALL] YAY!

1937
01:22:47,830 --> 01:22:50,400
- COOL.
- A HUMAN ROBOT, DOCTOR.

1938
01:22:50,467 --> 01:22:55,338
[THUNDER]

1939
01:22:55,405 --> 01:22:57,707
TONIGHT I'M GOING
TO FIND OUT.

1940
01:22:57,773 --> 01:23:00,077
TONIGHT I'M GOING TO PUT IT
TO THE SUPREME TEST.

1941
01:23:00,143 --> 01:23:01,577
THE "COSMO"
SEX QUIZ?

1942
01:23:01,643 --> 01:23:03,347
I'LL ACTIVATE THE CREATURE.

1943
01:23:03,413 --> 01:23:05,015
BUT THIS IS MONSTROUS,
DOCTOR!

1944
01:23:05,115 --> 01:23:09,085
IF IT LIVES, THEN MY TRIUMPH
WILL BE COMPLETE, DR. ALMADA.

1945
01:23:09,152 --> 01:23:12,422
BECAUSE I'LL GET THE TREASURE,
AND I'LL BE RICH!

1946
01:23:12,488 --> 01:23:14,057
[JOEL]
SHUT UP.

1947
01:23:14,123 --> 01:23:17,560
THIS THING I CREATED
HAS ENORMOUS POWER.

1948
01:23:17,627 --> 01:23:19,962
AND YOU'LL WATCH IT!

1949
01:23:20,030 --> 01:23:23,132
NOW, THEN,
LIFE FOR THE ROBOT!

1950
01:23:23,198 --> 01:23:26,468
THE ONLY THIN DIABOLICAL
ABOUT THIS GUY IS HIS ACTING.

1951
01:23:26,535 --> 01:23:28,738
DOCTOR, WATCH THIS!

1952
01:23:31,040 --> 01:23:33,577
[THUNDER]

1953
01:23:37,113 --> 01:23:40,683
THAT WOULD MAKE A REALLY
EXCELLENT MINIATURE GOLF COURSE.

1954
01:23:40,750 --> 01:23:43,118
[TOM]
DO I DETECT A THEME?

1955
01:23:43,185 --> 01:23:44,720
[JOEL]
I JUST-- I DON'T KNOW, I'M...

1956
01:23:44,787 --> 01:23:46,288
[CROW]
ROBOT, YAY!

1957
01:23:46,355 --> 01:23:48,057
I'M JUST SEEING
MINIATURE GOLF COURSES.

1958
01:23:48,123 --> 01:23:50,727
COOL.

1959
01:23:50,793 --> 01:23:53,730
WHO'S GOT THE LINE?
LINE, PLEASE.

1960
01:23:53,797 --> 01:23:55,398
[THUNDER]

1961
01:23:55,465 --> 01:23:56,800
DON'T YOU THINK
IT WOULD BE BETTER--

1962
01:23:56,867 --> 01:24:00,770
ROBOT, SCARFACE, LIGHT BULB,
FLOYD...

1963
01:24:00,837 --> 01:24:04,773
ROBOT, DOCTOR,
GOOD SHOT OF ME.

1964
01:24:04,840 --> 01:24:07,377
DO YOU HAVE ANY JUMPER CABLES
IN YOUR CAR OR SOMETHING?

1965
01:24:07,443 --> 01:24:10,213
IT'S NOT WORKING.

1966
01:24:13,148 --> 01:24:15,985
2:30 ALREADY.

1967
01:24:16,052 --> 01:24:17,420
DON'T YOU THINK
IT WOULD BE BETTER

1968
01:24:17,487 --> 01:24:18,822
TO CALL THE POLICE NOW?

1969
01:24:18,888 --> 01:24:20,090
- I DON'T KNOW WHAT TO DO.
- PICK UP THE PHONE AND DIAL.

1970
01:24:20,157 --> 01:24:22,125
NO, LET'S ALL WAIT
TILL 3:00 A.M.

1971
01:24:22,192 --> 01:24:23,358
AND RESPECT
THE DOCTOR'S WISHES.

1972
01:24:23,427 --> 01:24:24,793
SUPPOSE THEY'RE IN DANGER?

1973
01:24:24,860 --> 01:24:27,130
[MACHINE TRILLING}

1974
01:24:27,197 --> 01:24:30,633
[THUNDER]

1975
01:24:30,700 --> 01:24:32,635
[CROW]
ANOTHER GOOD SHOT OF ME.

1976
01:24:32,702 --> 01:24:33,970
[TOM]
GOOD SHOT OF THE ROBOT.

1977
01:24:34,037 --> 01:24:38,073
NOBODY'S MOVING.

1978
01:24:38,140 --> 01:24:39,942
[THUNDER]

1979
01:24:40,008 --> 01:24:45,482
I... THINK THAT'S
A DIFFERENT EMOTION, THOUGH.

1980
01:24:45,548 --> 01:24:46,615
TABLE'S MOVING.

1981
01:24:46,682 --> 01:24:50,120
THE TABLE'S A BETTER ACTOR
THAN ANYONE.

1982
01:24:50,187 --> 01:24:53,388
THEY'RE ALL MADE OUT
OF THE SAME MATERIAL... WOOD.

1983
01:24:57,593 --> 01:25:00,163
[BEEPING]

1984
01:25:02,265 --> 01:25:04,000
[CROW]
SOMEBODY MOVE.

1985
01:25:06,102 --> 01:25:08,037
LAUGH OR SOMETHING.
SQUEEZE IT OUT.

1986
01:25:08,103 --> 01:25:12,042
COME ON, FLOYD.
BRUNO?

1987
01:25:12,108 --> 01:25:14,677
[TOM AND CROW]
ROBOT?

1988
01:25:17,880 --> 01:25:20,817
♪ CHAIN CHAIN CHAIN ♪

1989
01:25:27,257 --> 01:25:28,925
[JOEL]
HE'S SO POWERFUL.

1990
01:25:28,992 --> 01:25:31,793
[LAUGHING]

1991
01:25:31,862 --> 01:25:32,895
YOU THINK THAT'S FUNNY?

1992
01:25:32,962 --> 01:25:35,030
OH, THIS IS GREAT,
DOCTOR!

1993
01:25:35,097 --> 01:25:36,598
THE GREATEST INVENTION!

1994
01:25:36,665 --> 01:25:38,433
[LAUGHING]

1995
01:25:38,502 --> 01:25:41,905
SINCE THE COFFEE MAKER.

1996
01:25:41,972 --> 01:25:43,238
DO YOU KNOW WHAT
COULD HAVE HAPPENED TO YOU?

1997
01:25:43,305 --> 01:25:46,877
IT'S NOT SO GREAT,
IT DOESN'T HAVE KNEES.

1998
01:25:46,943 --> 01:25:50,078
[TOM]
YOU CAN SEE IT STANDING THERE.
YOU CAN SEE IT STANDING THERE.

1999
01:25:50,145 --> 01:25:52,282
YOU CAN SEE IT
STANDING THERE!

2000
01:25:52,382 --> 01:25:53,683
A MARVELOUS MACHINE.

2001
01:25:53,750 --> 01:25:56,685
A TRIBUTE TO THE GREAT
INTELLIGENCE OF MAN!

2002
01:25:56,752 --> 01:25:58,788
A HUMAN ROBOT.

2003
01:25:58,855 --> 01:26:00,523
WITH THIS SHINY CREATURE,

2004
01:26:00,590 --> 01:26:02,892
NO HUMAN BEING ON THIS EARTH
CAN OPPOSE ME!

2005
01:26:02,958 --> 01:26:05,328
WAIT A "HUMAN ROBOT"?

2006
01:26:05,395 --> 01:26:07,697
THERE'S A FLAW RIGHT THERE.

2007
01:26:07,763 --> 01:26:09,032
DO YOU KNOW WHAT COULD HAVE
HAPPENED TO YOU RIGHT NOW?

2008
01:26:09,098 --> 01:26:10,767
[CROW]
ONLY BITS OF IT ARE HUMAN.

2009
01:26:10,833 --> 01:26:12,868
HAD I NOT DIMINISHED
THE ELECTRIC FORCE,

2010
01:26:12,935 --> 01:26:14,403
THE CURRENT
THAT MAKES HIM MOVE

2011
01:26:14,470 --> 01:26:16,338
AND THAT IS CONTAINED
IN THIS APPARATUS?

2012
01:26:16,405 --> 01:26:18,842
WITH THE SLIGHTEST TWIST
OF THIS DIAL...

2013
01:26:18,908 --> 01:26:19,875
FLOYD IS STUNNED.

2014
01:26:19,942 --> 01:26:20,877
YOU TOO WOULD HAVE BEEN
CONVERTED

2015
01:26:20,943 --> 01:26:23,613
INTO ATOMIC DUST
INSTANTANEOUSLY!

2016
01:26:23,680 --> 01:26:27,717
BECAUSE THE ROBOT
UTILIZES RADIUM,

2017
01:26:27,783 --> 01:26:29,918
AND HAS SUFFICIENT POWER
TO DISINTEGRATE

2018
01:26:29,985 --> 01:26:33,088
ANYTHING IN THE WORLD!

2019
01:26:33,155 --> 01:26:36,792
TONIGHT IT MEETS THE MUMMY.

2020
01:26:36,858 --> 01:26:40,162
BRUNO, PREPARE
THE SPECIAL PLATES.

2021
01:26:40,230 --> 01:26:41,530
THE LEAD WILL SHIELD
MY TRUCK.

2022
01:26:41,597 --> 01:26:42,665
[JOEL]
BRING THE GOOD CHINA.

2023
01:26:42,732 --> 01:26:44,333
HURRY, TIME IS FLYING!

2024
01:26:44,400 --> 01:26:47,137
TONIGHT MY ROBOT HAS
TO MAKE A VISIT, YOU KNOW,

2025
01:26:47,203 --> 01:26:49,172
IN A CERTAIN CEMETERY.

2026
01:26:49,238 --> 01:26:50,740
- RAPID OIL CHANGE.
- WHAT TIME IS IT?

2027
01:26:50,807 --> 01:26:51,908
TEN MINUTES TO 3:00.

2028
01:26:51,975 --> 01:26:53,810
I TOLD YOU, THERE'S NO TIME
TO LOSE, BRUNO!

2029
01:26:53,877 --> 01:26:55,945
WE HAVE A COMMERCIAL.
TOODLES.

2030
01:26:56,012 --> 01:26:57,247
[LAUGHING]

2031
01:26:57,313 --> 01:27:01,985
♪♪

2032
01:27:06,488 --> 01:27:08,157
I WANT THE POLICE.
IT'S URGENT.

2033
01:27:08,223 --> 01:27:10,058
[JOEL DOES SILLY,
INDISTINCT VOICE]

2034
01:27:10,125 --> 01:27:12,262
HEADQUARTERS, I WANT TO TALK
TO THE CHIEF OF POLICE.

2035
01:27:12,328 --> 01:27:13,797
[CLOCK CHIMING]

2036
01:27:13,863 --> 01:27:15,765
3:00, AND ALL'S HELL.

2037
01:27:15,832 --> 01:27:17,967
I WANT YOU TO STOP
AND THINK ABOUT THIS.

2038
01:27:18,033 --> 01:27:21,137
A NEW KIND OF WORLD.
AN ARMY OF ROBOTS OBEYING ME.

2039
01:27:21,203 --> 01:27:22,872
HEY, LOOK, WE GOT
THE POINT, BUT--

2040
01:27:22,938 --> 01:27:25,908
THIS IS GREAT--
WE GOTTA GO, OKAY?

2041
01:27:25,975 --> 01:27:27,943
SHEEP OBEYING MY ORDERS.

2042
01:27:28,010 --> 01:27:29,578
A NEW THEORY THAT MAN
HAS NOT DARED IMAGINE!

2043
01:27:29,645 --> 01:27:31,547
THAT WOULD MAKE YOU
A SHEPHERD.

2044
01:27:31,613 --> 01:27:32,915
I'LL MAKE SOME MORE.

2045
01:27:33,015 --> 01:27:35,318
MAYBE 1,000.

2046
01:27:35,385 --> 01:27:37,820
NOW THAT I KNOW HOW,
THE REST IS EASY.

2047
01:27:37,887 --> 01:27:39,855
OH, YOU'RE TOO LOW.
GO A MILLION.

2048
01:27:39,922 --> 01:27:42,058
THE TREASURE OF THE AZTECS!

2049
01:27:42,125 --> 01:27:44,727
THAT'S WHY TONIGHT, THE MUMMY
WILL GIVE ME WHAT I WANT!

2050
01:27:44,793 --> 01:27:46,228
[JOEL]
CORN?

2051
01:27:46,295 --> 01:27:48,363
- IT'S ALL SET.
- THIS GUY SNAPPED A TWIG.

2052
01:27:48,430 --> 01:27:51,233
- FINE.

2053
01:27:51,300 --> 01:27:52,902
- I THINK THE WHOLE BRANCH
CAME DOWN.

2054
01:27:52,968 --> 01:27:56,072
- ... AND GUARD
OUR DISTINGUISHED FRIENDS.

2055
01:27:56,138 --> 01:27:58,675
THEY, MUSTN'T GET AWAY.

2056
01:27:58,742 --> 01:28:01,743
THEY'RE AN EXTREMELY IMPORTANT
COG IN MY PLAN.

2057
01:28:01,810 --> 01:28:05,982
GREAT, FIRST I'M A SHADOW
NOW I'M A COG.

2058
01:28:06,015 --> 01:28:08,317
BUT YOU'D ONLY
GET UNDERFOOT.

2059
01:28:08,383 --> 01:28:10,853
WRIGHT'S GOTTA TAKE
MEDICINE EVERY TWO HOURS,

2060
01:28:10,920 --> 01:28:12,255
CAN HE GO?

2061
01:28:12,322 --> 01:28:14,323
... I COULD DESTROY
THE MUMMY.

2062
01:28:14,390 --> 01:28:18,193
AND WITH THE GOLD BREASTPLATE
AND BRACELET IN MY HANDS,

2063
01:28:18,260 --> 01:28:20,162
YOU BEGAN ONCE MORE

2064
01:28:20,228 --> 01:28:21,830
TO TRANSLATE THE
HIEROGLYPHICS.

2065
01:28:21,897 --> 01:28:25,368
GEEZ, IS HE LONG-WINDED.

2066
01:28:25,435 --> 01:28:26,802
THIS TIME YOU'RE HELPLESS

2067
01:28:26,868 --> 01:28:28,705
BECAUSE NO ONE KNOWS
YOU'RE HERE.

2068
01:28:28,772 --> 01:28:29,772
SHUT UP!

2069
01:28:29,838 --> 01:28:31,573
DR. ALMADA.

2070
01:28:31,640 --> 01:28:34,043
[LAUGHS]

2071
01:28:34,110 --> 01:28:37,380
TIME FOR BRUNO'S
ELECTROLYSIS.

2072
01:28:37,447 --> 01:28:39,948
[BEEPING COMING FROM
ROBOT]

2073
01:28:43,618 --> 01:28:46,688
WHAT'S HE GOING TO DO?

2074
01:28:46,755 --> 01:28:51,293
- UH, HE'S GOING TO PAT
HIS PART.
- GITCHEE GITCHEE GOO

2075
01:28:51,360 --> 01:28:53,730
DICK YORK AS
THE MUMMY.

2076
01:28:53,797 --> 01:28:56,432
NO, THAT'S THE ROBOT.

2077
01:28:56,498 --> 01:28:57,833
OH, THE ROBOT, SORRY.

2078
01:28:57,900 --> 01:29:01,237
I THINK IT MIGHT BE
DICK SARGENT ANYWAY.

2079
01:29:01,303 --> 01:29:04,907
♪ I'M MILTON YOUR
BRAND NEW SON ♪

2080
01:29:09,445 --> 01:29:11,747
♪ PUT YOUR RIGHT FOOT IN ♪

2081
01:29:11,780 --> 01:29:14,383
♪ YOU PUT YOUR RIGHT
FOOT OUT ♪

2082
01:29:14,450 --> 01:29:16,385
♪ YOU DO THE ROBEY POKEY ♪

2083
01:29:16,452 --> 01:29:18,722
♪ AND YOU TURN
YOURSELF ABOUT ♪

2084
01:29:18,788 --> 01:29:21,357
♪ YOUR HEAD IS FILLED
WITH ELECTRODES ♪

2085
01:29:21,423 --> 01:29:23,425
♪ IT MAKES YOU
WANT TO SHOUT ♪

2086
01:29:23,492 --> 01:29:26,728
♪ AND THAT'S WHAT
IT'S ALL ABOUT ♪

2087
01:29:26,795 --> 01:29:27,997
HEY.

2088
01:29:28,063 --> 01:29:30,065
♪ RIGHT FOOT IN ♪

2089
01:29:30,132 --> 01:29:31,400
- I DON'T HAVE ANY
FEET, JOEL.
- OH.

2090
01:29:31,467 --> 01:29:32,402
THE FUN'S OVER.

2091
01:29:32,468 --> 01:29:37,107
OH, WE'RE TO
THE NEW PLACE.

2092
01:29:37,173 --> 01:29:39,842
LET'S HURRY, I'M
AFRAID FOR THEIR LIVES.

2093
01:29:39,908 --> 01:29:41,377
YOU'RE AFRAID FOR
YOUR LIVES?

2094
01:29:41,443 --> 01:29:43,712
I'M AFRAID FOR
YOUR CAREER.

2095
01:29:43,780 --> 01:29:45,147
YOU CALL THAT A CAREER?

2096
01:29:45,213 --> 01:29:47,517
YOU KNOW I CAN'T HELP
BUT THINK THAT ROBOT

2097
01:29:47,583 --> 01:29:50,118
WOULD BE EXCELLENT
ON A MINIATURE GOLF COURSE.

2098
01:29:50,185 --> 01:29:52,053
STOP IT.

2099
01:29:52,122 --> 01:29:54,357
LOOKS LIKE A COFFEE MAKER.

2100
01:29:54,423 --> 01:29:56,058
KRUPPS COFFEE MAKER

2101
01:29:56,125 --> 01:29:57,527
OH, NO.

2102
01:29:57,593 --> 01:29:59,328
SORRY.

2103
01:29:59,395 --> 01:30:00,663
[GROANING, GUNSHOT]
WAY TO GO.

2104
01:30:00,730 --> 01:30:03,498
OH, UH, OH.

2105
01:30:03,565 --> 01:30:07,403
♪ UH-HUH, THIS IS
FOR ANDY ♪

2106
01:30:07,470 --> 01:30:09,272
CAN YOU DO YOU
FLOYD VOICE?

2107
01:30:09,338 --> 01:30:15,612
HUH, YES. HUH, YES.

2108
01:30:15,678 --> 01:30:17,847
- OH, THE ROBOT'S VERY--
- ALL RIGHT, FLOYD, FLOYD,

2109
01:30:17,913 --> 01:30:19,582
HEY, CUT IT OUT.

2110
01:30:19,682 --> 01:30:20,783
THAT'S FOR AUNT BEA.

2111
01:30:20,850 --> 01:30:21,817
THAT'S FOR OPIE.

2112
01:30:21,883 --> 01:30:24,753
THAT'S FOR GOOBER.

2113
01:30:24,820 --> 01:30:25,788
UH, OW.

2114
01:30:25,855 --> 01:30:26,788
WHERE'RE MY GLASSES?

2115
01:30:26,855 --> 01:30:27,823
WHERE ARE MY GLASSES?

2116
01:30:27,890 --> 01:30:29,392
WHERE ARE MY GLASSES?

2117
01:30:29,458 --> 01:30:30,527
THEY'RE ON YOUR FACE.

2118
01:30:30,593 --> 01:30:31,527
THERE THEY ARE.

2119
01:30:31,593 --> 01:30:35,130
HUH, YES.

2120
01:30:35,197 --> 01:30:37,098
OH, YES.

2121
01:30:37,167 --> 01:30:39,502
GREAT COMIC ACTOR.

2122
01:30:39,568 --> 01:30:41,103
POOR, BIP, THE MISSION MAN.

2123
01:30:41,170 --> 01:30:42,738
WHAT HAPPENED HERE?

2124
01:30:42,805 --> 01:30:43,772
CHIEF YOU CAN ARREST
THOSE TWO MEN THERE

2125
01:30:43,840 --> 01:30:44,807
IN THE OTHER ROOM.

2126
01:30:44,873 --> 01:30:46,042
COME ON.

2127
01:30:46,108 --> 01:30:47,377
DOCTOR, THE BAT HAS
GONE TO THE TOMB

2128
01:30:47,443 --> 01:30:48,410
WHERE THE MUMMY IS.

2129
01:30:48,477 --> 01:30:50,980
LET'S HURRY, THERE'S
NO TIME TO LOSE.

2130
01:30:57,052 --> 01:31:00,923
[ROBOT BEEPING]

2131
01:31:09,098 --> 01:31:12,133
WHAT'S THAT?

2132
01:31:17,640 --> 01:31:20,242
A MAN MADE OUT
OF TIN.

2133
01:31:20,308 --> 01:31:26,382
HUH, YES.

2134
01:31:26,448 --> 01:31:28,550
HEY, GUYS, GUESS WHO'S
HISTORY IN THIS SCENE?

2135
01:31:28,617 --> 01:31:30,653
JUAN VALDEZ.

2136
01:31:30,720 --> 01:31:34,723
BINGO.

2137
01:31:34,790 --> 01:31:37,158
YEAH.

2138
01:31:37,227 --> 01:31:38,227
USE THE ROBOT.

2139
01:31:38,293 --> 01:31:42,232
I'LL MURDERLIZE HIM.

2140
01:31:48,203 --> 01:31:49,272
LET'S SEE, I'LL PUT
THIS ON BROIL.

2141
01:31:49,338 --> 01:31:50,272
IT'S A DECOY.

2142
01:31:50,338 --> 01:31:51,507
[HISSING]
AH!

2143
01:31:51,573 --> 01:31:53,408
- [SCREAMING]
- MUST'VE BEEN A
SMOKING JACKET.

2144
01:31:53,475 --> 01:31:57,580
WELL, EMULATION IS THE
SINCEREST FORM OF FLATTERY.

2145
01:31:57,647 --> 01:31:59,448
I READ THAT IN A BOOK.

2146
01:32:01,350 --> 01:32:03,152
[ROBOT BEEPING]

2147
01:32:05,153 --> 01:32:07,055
♪♪

2148
01:32:08,123 --> 01:32:09,392
HURRY, BRUNO.

2149
01:32:09,458 --> 01:32:12,462
TAKE THE BREASTPLATE
AND BRACELET OFF OF HIM.

2150
01:32:12,528 --> 01:32:15,832
YES.

2151
01:32:15,898 --> 01:32:17,633
WELL, I THINK WE'RE
ABOUT TO SEE

2152
01:32:17,700 --> 01:32:20,035
THE NAMESAKE OF
THIS MOVIE.

2153
01:32:20,102 --> 01:32:25,473
THE ROBOT VS.
THE MUMMY.

2154
01:32:25,540 --> 01:32:29,612
I'M IN FOR TWENTY
ON THE ROBOT.

2155
01:32:29,678 --> 01:32:32,915
I DON'T KNOW, THAT MUMMY'S
GOT REAL NICE SPEED.

2156
01:32:33,015 --> 01:32:36,152
AMAZING SNAKE-LIKE
ACCURACY, TOO.

2157
01:32:36,218 --> 01:32:38,020
HE DOES A HELL
OF A SOFT SHOE, TOO.

2158
01:32:38,087 --> 01:32:42,592
HE'S THE AZTEC OF
A THOUSAND-AND-ONE HOLES.

2159
01:32:42,658 --> 01:32:46,562
THIS SCENE IS CLOSE CAPTIONED
FOR THE SPEED IMPAIRED.

2160
01:32:46,628 --> 01:32:50,298
HE MOVES LIKE GEORGE BURNS.

2161
01:32:50,365 --> 01:32:51,600
HE'LL PUT YOU IN
THE SLEEPER HOLD

2162
01:32:51,667 --> 01:32:53,102
IF HE JUST BREATHES
ON YOU.

2163
01:32:53,168 --> 01:32:58,173
THIS WHOLE MOVIE'S
A SLEEPER HOLD.

2164
01:32:58,240 --> 01:33:00,475
TAKE TWO OF THESE
AND A GLASS OF WATER

2165
01:33:00,542 --> 01:33:03,212
AND YOU'LL SLEEP
LIKE A BABY.

2166
01:33:03,278 --> 01:33:05,715
I COULDN'T TAKE
TWO OF THESE.

2167
01:33:05,782 --> 01:33:06,782
[GROWLING]

2168
01:33:06,848 --> 01:33:09,052
THIS ONE FEELS LIKE
A SUPPOSITORY.

2169
01:33:09,118 --> 01:33:10,552
LET'S KISS.

2170
01:33:10,620 --> 01:33:14,757
IT'S LIKE PROFESSIONAL
WRESTLING IN SLOW MOTION.

2171
01:33:18,127 --> 01:33:21,963
LIKE PROFESSIONAL ACTING
IN SLOW MOTION, TOO.

2172
01:33:22,030 --> 01:33:23,932
YOU KNOW WHAT IF
THE BAT WAS TRYING

2173
01:33:24,000 --> 01:33:26,335
TO FOOL EVERYBODY
AND HE'S JUST GOT A GUY

2174
01:33:26,402 --> 01:33:29,105
IN A SUIT, IT'S NOT REALLY
A ROBOT AT ALL.

2175
01:33:29,172 --> 01:33:32,207
THAT COULDN'T HAPPEN.

2176
01:33:32,273 --> 01:33:34,477
MAKES YOU THINK, THOUGH.

2177
01:33:34,543 --> 01:33:36,478
I DON'T KNOW, ONCE THAT
ROBOT GETS INTO GEAR,

2178
01:33:36,545 --> 01:33:37,713
YOU'RE REALLY GOING
TO SEE HIM KICK

2179
01:33:37,780 --> 01:33:39,882
SOME AZTEC.

2180
01:33:39,948 --> 01:33:41,350
HOO-HOO.

2181
01:33:41,417 --> 01:33:43,552
HUH-HO.

2182
01:33:43,618 --> 01:33:47,623
WELL, THAT'S SOMETHING
YOU HADN'T COUNTED ON.

2183
01:33:47,690 --> 01:33:51,627
ALL MUMMMIES
CARRY PLIERS.

2184
01:33:51,693 --> 01:33:54,597
HE DIDN'T GIVE MUCH
OF A FIGHT AT ALL.

2185
01:33:54,663 --> 01:33:56,498
OH, MUMMY, HOLD ME.

2186
01:33:56,565 --> 01:34:00,335
I THINK IT'S REALLY THE HUMAN
PART OF HIM THAT'S FAILING.

2187
01:34:00,402 --> 01:34:03,105
WELL THE HUMAN SIDE
LIKES THE RICH TASTE,

2188
01:34:03,172 --> 01:34:08,510
BUT THE ROBOT IN HIM LOVES
THE FROSTY GOODNESS.

2189
01:34:08,577 --> 01:34:12,615
OH, THIS ISN'T
A SERIAL, IS IT?

2190
01:34:12,648 --> 01:34:16,352
OH, YEAH, THE OTHER ONE
WAS A SERIAL.

2191
01:34:16,418 --> 01:34:18,853
OH, HOLD ME.

2192
01:34:18,920 --> 01:34:22,223
JOEL, RIGHT IN
THE ADAM'S APPLE.

2193
01:34:22,290 --> 01:34:24,060
[GUN FIRES]

2194
01:34:24,127 --> 01:34:26,095
[MUMMY GROWLS]

2195
01:34:32,368 --> 01:34:34,537
I LOOKED UP ANTI-CLIMAX
IN THE DICTIONARY

2196
01:34:34,603 --> 01:34:39,742
AND IT SAID SEE
"AZTEC MUMMY."

2197
01:34:39,808 --> 01:34:41,710
- THEY CONSTIPATED THE--
- NO THAT LOOKS REAL.

2198
01:34:41,777 --> 01:34:43,945
YEAH, I THINK THAT'S REAL.

2199
01:34:44,012 --> 01:34:45,815
I DIDN'T KNOW BILLY
BARTY WAS IN THIS.

2200
01:34:45,915 --> 01:34:46,915
[SCREAMS]

2201
01:34:46,982 --> 01:34:50,218
HE'S GOT A SMALL PART.

2202
01:34:50,285 --> 01:34:54,157
AHH!

2203
01:34:54,223 --> 01:34:55,992
THOSE TWO HAD TO DIE.

2204
01:34:56,058 --> 01:34:59,928
THANK GOD FLORA'S HERE.

2205
01:34:59,995 --> 01:35:03,832
POPOCA, IN MEMORY OF
THE GREAT LOVE

2206
01:35:03,898 --> 01:35:05,868
THAT ONCE EXISTED
BETWEEN US.

2207
01:35:05,935 --> 01:35:07,537
OH, HONEY.

2208
01:35:07,603 --> 01:35:10,072
BEFORE YOUR SKIN
WENT BAD.

2209
01:35:10,138 --> 01:35:12,642
... YOURS TO GUARD,
AND GO BACK TO THE GRAVE

2210
01:35:12,708 --> 01:35:17,178
OF OUR ANCESTORS WHERE WE
SHOULD NEVER HAVE INTERRUPTED

2211
01:35:17,245 --> 01:35:19,215
- YOUR ETERNAL SLEEP.
- AND NEVER DARKEN THIS
FILM AGAIN.

2212
01:35:19,282 --> 01:35:22,217
JOEL, ISN'T THAT
A DEMON DOG?

2213
01:35:23,352 --> 01:35:24,453
DEMON DOG?

2214
01:35:24,520 --> 01:35:26,922
[BOTH SCREAMING]

2215
01:35:28,090 --> 01:35:30,158
[DOG GROWLS]

2216
01:35:34,430 --> 01:35:37,700
[DOG CONTINUES GROWLING]

2217
01:35:54,317 --> 01:35:55,650
OH, MAN.

2218
01:35:55,717 --> 01:35:56,885
THIS ISN'T WORKING.

2219
01:35:56,952 --> 01:35:59,288
THIS IS GREAT, WHAT DO
WE DO NOW?

2220
01:35:59,355 --> 01:36:02,692
NO, I CAN SEE CLEARLY
THAT WHAT HOW WE'RE DEALING

2221
01:36:02,758 --> 01:36:03,725
WITH THESE THINGS
JUST ISN'T GOING TO WORK.

2222
01:36:03,792 --> 01:36:04,893
NO WAY.

2223
01:36:04,960 --> 01:36:07,463
MAYBE WE SHOULD JUST TRY
TO REVIEW THE MOVIE.

2224
01:36:07,530 --> 01:36:09,732
OUCH, INCOMING.

2225
01:36:09,798 --> 01:36:12,735
WHOA, I THOUGHT THAT A ROBOT
WITH A HUMAN HEAD

2226
01:36:12,802 --> 01:36:14,703
WAS REALLY OFFENSIVE.

2227
01:36:14,770 --> 01:36:16,672
- AH!
- YEAH, MYSTIC MANIA,

2228
01:36:16,738 --> 01:36:18,240
IT'S OBVIOUSLY WHY A LOT
OF THEM ARE FLYING US,

2229
01:36:18,307 --> 01:36:19,642
PROBABLY COMING
A MILE A WAY,

2230
01:36:19,708 --> 01:36:20,943
LET'S CRUSH.

2231
01:36:21,010 --> 01:36:22,745
I CAN SEE NOW THAT
THIS COMPLETELY

2232
01:36:22,812 --> 01:36:24,880
ISN'T WORKING, WE GOT
TO GET RID OF THESE THINGS

2233
01:36:24,947 --> 01:36:26,482
QUICK, CHECK YOUR FILES.

2234
01:36:26,548 --> 01:36:27,850
WE'RE ALMOST OUT OF
GAME BURGERS.

2235
01:36:27,917 --> 01:36:29,518
YEAH, NEWSPAPERS TOO.

2236
01:36:29,585 --> 01:36:31,920
WHICH WHAT GETS A DOG
GOING ON EARTH.

2237
01:36:31,987 --> 01:36:34,390
WELL, UH, CHASING RABBITS,
TICKS, CARS,

2238
01:36:34,457 --> 01:36:37,292
LICKING, SCRATCHING,
UH, TENNIS BALLS, UH...

2239
01:36:37,358 --> 01:36:39,162
- THAT'S IT, TENNIS BALLS.
- TENNIS BALLS?

2240
01:36:39,228 --> 01:36:41,330
LISTEN, GO DOWN TO THE
SERVICE POD,

2241
01:36:41,397 --> 01:36:43,932
FIND THE THRUSTERS
OFF OF 33A,

2242
01:36:43,998 --> 01:36:46,502
ATTACH THEM TO THAT
BIG DISPOSABLE BALL,

2243
01:36:46,568 --> 01:36:47,870
SHAPED LIKE A GIANT BALL.

2244
01:36:47,937 --> 01:36:49,972
WE'LL PUSH IT OUT
THE BAY PORT DOORS.

2245
01:36:50,038 --> 01:36:51,573
GO DOWN THERE,
KEEP YOUR FINGERS CROSSED

2246
01:36:51,640 --> 01:36:54,510
IF YOU GOT THEM.

2247
01:36:54,577 --> 01:36:57,245
OKAY, CAMBOT, PUT ME
ON EXTERIOR.

2248
01:36:57,312 --> 01:37:01,817
PUT IN FETCH MODE
ON MY MARK, NOW.

2249
01:37:01,883 --> 01:37:05,087
[DOGS BARKING]

2250
01:37:08,223 --> 01:37:11,627
[BARKING FADES]

2251
01:37:14,095 --> 01:37:16,798
- ALL RIGHT, THEY'RE GONE.
- [LAUGHS]

2252
01:37:16,865 --> 01:37:19,635
OH, JOEL, I DON'T WANT
TO BE A KILLJOY,

2253
01:37:19,702 --> 01:37:24,740
BUT DOESN'T "FETCH" MEAN
GO GET AND BRING BACK?

2254
01:37:24,807 --> 01:37:28,277
[ALL THREE]
OH!

2255
01:37:28,343 --> 01:37:30,112
THAT'S THE END
OF OUR EXPERIMENT,

2256
01:37:30,178 --> 01:37:31,880
I HOPE YOU'RE HAPPY.

2257
01:37:31,980 --> 01:37:33,815
OH, I'M HAPPY.

2258
01:37:33,882 --> 01:37:35,317
ARE YOU, HAPPY?

2259
